  {t="T", seg=11, q={95795}, names={"Fallen in the Fen"}, text="Fallen in the Fen: Dorin Songblade.", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=25.7, y=46.7, dg=5},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={180}, names={"Wanted: Lieutenant Fangore"}, text="The wanted poster in Lakeshire (21.7,46.4)", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=21.7, y=46.4},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={126}, names={"Howling in the Hills"}, text="Go north out of Lakeshire into the canyons. Yowler (25) stands in the gnoll camp at 22.6,21.4. Everything here is grey or green to you", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=22.6, y=21.4},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={128}, names={"Blackrock Bounty"}, text="Further north, the Blackrock camp (21-31,6-17): kill 15 Blackrock Champions (24-25)", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=24.5, y=12.0, path={{24.9,19.3}}},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={219}, names={"Missing In Action"}, text="Corporal Keeshan, held in the same camp (23.3,12.6). Clear the orcs around him first, then accept: it is an escort", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=23.3, y=12.6},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={219}, names={"Missing In Action"}, text="Walk with Keeshan back to Lakeshire. He fights everything on the way: let the Voidwalker hold what attacks him and DoT every orc (you cannot heal him), and do not run ahead", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=26.0, y=30.0, path={{24.9,13.0},{25.2,19.6},{28.2,24.1},{28.2,27.4}}},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={219}, names={"Missing In Action"}, text="Marshal Marris, Lakeshire", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=28.4, y=49.0},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={126}, names={"Howling in the Hills"}, text="Verner Osgood", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=25.9, y=47.3},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={128}, names={"Blackrock Bounty"}, text="Guard Howe, at the bridge", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=26.4, y=57.9},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={180}, names={"Wanted: Lieutenant Fangore"}, text="Lieutenant Fangore (26) is far east in Galardell Valley, in the Shadowhide camp at 75.1,37.1. Take the road east past Stonewatch, a long walk. Gnolls stand with him: kill the outer ones first with the Voidwalker, then send it at him; Fear a gnoll that comes along", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=75.1, y=37.1},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={180}, names={"Wanted: Lieutenant Fangore"}, text="Magistrate Solomon, Lakeshire (24.9,44.5)", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=24.9, y=44.5},
  {t="FLY", seg=11, arg="Darkshire", text="Ariena Stormfeather, Lakeshire", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=25.5, y=59.4},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={78}, names={"The Legend of Stalvan"}, text="Tavernkeep Smitts", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=73.8, y=44.5},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={79}, names={"The Legend of Stalvan"}, text="Tavernkeep Smitts", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=73.8, y=44.5},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={79}, names={"The Legend of Stalvan"}, text="Commander Althea Ebonlocke", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=73.5, y=46.8},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={80}, names={"The Legend of Stalvan"}, text="Commander Althea Ebonlocke", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=73.5, y=46.8},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={80}, names={"The Legend of Stalvan"}, text="Clerk Daltry", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=72.5, y=46.9},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={97}, names={"The Legend of Stalvan"}, text="Clerk Daltry", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=72.5, y=46.9},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={97}, names={"The Legend of Stalvan"}, text="Commander Althea Ebonlocke", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=73.5, y=46.8},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={98}, names={"The Legend of Stalvan"}, text="Commander Althea Ebonlocke. Stalvan is level 32: he is the very last fight of this segment", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=73.5, y=46.8},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={222}, names={"Worgen in the Woods"}, text="South of Darkshire (61-74,67-84): 8 Nightbane Vile Fangs (29-30) and 8 Nightbane Tainted Ones (30-31). Work in from the north edge, one at a time, Voidwalker first, all three DoTs, then Drain Life. If a second one comes, back off toward the road and Fear it there, away from the other packs. Rest to full between pulls and keep a Healthstone in your bags", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=69.0, y=76.0},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={181}, names={"Look To The Stars"}, text="South road west to the Vul'Gol Ogre Mound. Zzarc'Vul (33) is at the south end of the mound (36-38,80-84) with Splinter Fist Enslavers (30-31). Clear the way in one ogre at a time, wait until he stands apart from the others, then put a Soulstone on yourself, make a Healthstone and fight him at full health and mana: Voidwalker first, give it a few seconds, then Curse of Agony, Corruption, Immolate and Drain Life; Health Funnel keeps the Voidwalker alive, its Sacrifice shield and a potion are for the moment he turns on you. Fear an Enslaver that joins in. He is 3 levels above you, so some spells will be resisted. Loot the Ogre's Monocle. If he kills you twice, drop the quest. Finish Merrick's Bow here if it is still open", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=37.0, y=81.5},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={98447}, names={"The Valor Family"}, text="Only if Sirra gave you the second Valor Family quest. Go to Raven Hill village (17.4,54.0, near Jitters) with the dagger and the bow in your bags until \"Raven Hill investigated\" ticks. What appears there is not in the data: be ready for a fight (Voidwalker out, full health and mana, a Healthstone in your bags)", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=17.4, y=54.0},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={58}, names={"The Night Watch"}, text="North into the cemetery: 20 Plague Spreaders (27-28) around the eastern mausoleum and the graves below Abercrombie's hill (16-26,28-37). They give you a disease and a warlock cannot cure it: keep them on the Voidwalker, and bandage, Drain Life and eat", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=22.8, y=33.2},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={134}, names={"Ogre Thieves"}, text="Abercrombie", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=28.1, y=31.5},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={160}, names={"Note to the Mayor"}, text="Abercrombie", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=28.1, y=31.5},
  {t="H", seg=11, arg="Darkshire", text="Hearthstone to Darkshire"},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={160}, names={"Note to the Mayor"}, text="Lord Ello Ebonlocke, the mayor, in the town hall", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=71.9, y=46.4},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={251}, names={"Translate Abercrombie's Note"}, text="Lord Ello Ebonlocke", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=71.9, y=46.4},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={251}, names={"Translate Abercrombie's Note"}, text="Sirra Von'Indi", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=72.6, y=47.6},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={401}, names={"Wait for Sirra to Finish"}, text="Sirra Von'Indi. Wait a few seconds beside her", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=72.6, y=47.6},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={401}, names={"Wait for Sirra to Finish"}, text="Sirra Von'Indi", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=72.6, y=47.6},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={252}, names={"Translation to Ello"}, text="Sirra Von'Indi", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=72.6, y=47.6},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={252}, names={"Translation to Ello"}, text="Lord Ello Ebonlocke. Do not take Bride of the Embalmer (253): elite", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=71.9, y=46.4},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={98447}, names={"The Valor Family"}, text="Sirra Von'Indi (if you did it). Hand in any weapon quest that is still open as well", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=72.6, y=47.5},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={58}, names={"The Night Watch"}, text="Commander Althea Ebonlocke", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=73.5, y=46.8},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={222}, names={"Worgen in the Woods"}, text="Calor", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=75.8, y=47.6},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={223}, names={"Worgen in the Woods"}, text="Calor", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=75.8, y=47.6},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={223}, names={"Worgen in the Woods"}, text="Jonathan Carevin, close to Calor (75.3,49.0)", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=75.3, y=49.0},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={181}, names={"Look To The Stars"}, text="Viktori Prism'Antras, east of town (79.8,48.0)", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=79.8, y=48.0},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={98}, names={"The Legend of Stalvan"}, text="Stalvan Mistmantle (32) is in the cottage north of Darkshire at 77.3,36.2. Fetid Corpses (29-30) stand around it: kill the ones near the door first. Then rest to full, put a Soulstone on yourself, and send the Voidwalker in so that he comes out to the cleared ground in front of the door. He casts and you have no interrupt: keep Curse of Tongues on him (it slows his spells), add Corruption and Immolate, Drain Life, Health Funnel for the Voidwalker, and use the Healthstone and a potion when you need them. He drops the Mistmantle Family Ring. Too strong? Abandon the quest and move on", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=77.3, y=36.2, path={{80.3,40.3},{78.3,36.1}}},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={98}, names={"The Legend of Stalvan"}, text="Madame Eva, in her house (75.8,45.3)", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=75.8, y=45.3},
  {t="FLY", seg=11, arg="Stormwind", text="Felicia Maline, Darkshire", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=77.5, y=44.3},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={690}, names={"Malin's Request"}, text="Archmage Malin, in front of the mage tower in the Mage Quarter (50.5,87.5). Needs level 30: you should be 30 now. It sends you to Refuge Pointe in Arathi (segment 12). The Slaughtered Lamb is a few steps west of him (39.2,85.0, trainers in the cellar): at 30 you may learn your level 30 spells there right now instead of in Ironforge at the start of segment 12", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=50.5, y=87.5},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={92489}, names={"Power Overwhelming"}, text="High Sorcerer Andromath. Kill the Arcanic Enigma inside.", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=37.6, y=81.6, dg=6},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={92456}, names={"A Green Sample"}, text="Shylamiir. A Fel Infused Blossom from inside.", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=31.5, y=63.0, dg=6},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={2928}, names={"Gyrodrillmatic Excavationators"}, text="Shoni the Shilent. 24 Robo-mechanical Guts from the robots inside.", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=55.5, y=12.5, dg=7},
  {t="N", seg=11, arg="Take the Deeprun Tram from the Dwarven District to Ironforge"},
  {t="N", seg=11, arg="Segment done. In the log: 270, 1248 and 98223 (Menethil), 472 (Dun Modr), 690 (Refuge Pointe), 98219 (Southshore), 1026 (Ashenvale)", text="Your hearthstone stays in Darkshire until Southshore"},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=12, text="Briarthorn, the warlock trainer in the Forlorn Cavern in the north of the city: learn your level 30 spells (everything he offers), unless you already trained at the Slaughtered Lamb at the end of segment 11. The demon trainer beside him sells the Voidwalker's spell books. Leave with 3-5 Soul Shards", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=50.4, y=5.7},
  {t="N", seg=12, arg="Optional, not routed: the level 30 Felhunter chain", text="1798 Seeking Strahad is given by Gakin the Darkbinder in the cellar of the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind (not by Briarthorn) and sends you to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet, then Tome of the Cabal, with errands in Ratchet and Ironforge and beyond: two continents, so this guide leaves it out and keeps the Voidwalker as your pet. Also optional and not routed: Menara Voidrender's quests in Ratchet, the robe at level 31 and the orb at level 35. Take them if you want them and fit them in where they suit you; the logger records what you take"},
  {t="N", seg=12, arg="Auction House: buy 1 Hillman's Cloak and 1 Bolt of Woolen Cloth for Bartolo's Yeti Fur Cloak (565)", text="The cloak is made by leatherworkers and not sold by vendors. None for sale at a fair price? Then do not take 565 in Southshore and skip its steps"},
  {t="FLY", seg=12, arg="Thelsamar", text="Gryth Thurden", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=55.5, y=47.7},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={472}, names={"Fall of Dun Modr"}, text="From Thelsamar take the road north and west through Dun Algaz into the Wetlands, then follow the road north all the way to Dun Modr (a long walk). Longbraid the Grim and his dwarves stand outside the town on the west side (49.8,18.3). Dark Iron dwarves hold the town itself: stay out. Do not take his follow-ups (elite)", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=49.8, y=18.3},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={378}, names={"The Fury Runs Deep"}, zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=49.7, y=18.2, dg=3},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={161}, names={"A Dark Threat Looms"}, text="Ashlan Stonesmirk, the explosives expert among the dwarves at Dun Modr: the powder from the Stonewrought Dam. Do not take his follow-ups: they lead to an elite fight on the Thandol Span", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=50.0, y=18.2},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={637}, names={"Sully Balloo's Letter"}, text="Before you climb the Thandol Span: go down to the water under the broken western span and swim to the dwarf corpse on the bottom (Arathi map 44.3,92.9); cast Unending Breath first. Loot the Waterlogged Envelope and right-click it to start the quest. Then swim back to the Wetlands shore and walk up to the bridge", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=44.3, y=92.9},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={647}, names={"MacKreel's Moonshine"}, text="Foggy MacKreel sits on the stub of the broken western span, at the south (Wetlands) end of the Thandol Span (Arathi map 43.2,92.6). Needs level 28. His moonshine goes to Southshore", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=43.2, y=92.6},
  {t="N", seg=12, arg="Cross the Thandol Span north into the Arathi Highlands", text="Dark Iron dwarves (28-30) stand on the bridge: send the Voidwalker at one at a time and DoT it; do not Fear on the bridge (a feared dwarf fetches the rest) and do not try to run through the whole group"},
  {t="F", seg=12, arg="Refuge Pointe", text="Follow the road north, then east, to Refuge Pointe in the middle of the zone. Cedrik Prose is the gryphon master", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=45.7, y=46.1, path={{43.0,88.2},{47.2,81.9},{47.2,78.3},{48.2,76.8},{48.2,68.1},{41.0,57.0},{41.0,53.1},{42.4,51.0},{42.6,45.1},{45.4,42.7}}},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={690}, names={"Malin's Request"}, text="Skuerto, Refuge Pointe", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=46.6, y=47.0},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={681}, names={"Northfold Manor"}, text="Captain Nials, Refuge Pointe. Needs level 30", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=45.8, y=47.6},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={681}, names={"Northfold Manor"}, text="North-west across the hills to Northfold Manor (29-35,24-33): 10 Syndicate Highwaymen (30-31, stealthed around the fields) and 6 Syndicate Mercenaries (31-32, at the buildings). All melee. Send the Voidwalker at one at a time from the edge of the farm, then Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate and the wand. They run at low health: your DoTs usually finish them as they run; a Shadow Bolt helps. Do not Fear inside the farm, they bring friends. A Highwayman that opens on you from stealth: Drain Life it until the Voidwalker has it", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=32.3, y=28.7},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={681}, names={"Northfold Manor"}, text="Back to Captain Nials at Refuge Pointe. Leave the other Refuge Pointe quests: you come back to Arathi in segment 16", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=45.8, y=47.6},
  {t="N", seg=12, arg="Follow the road west through Thoradin's Wall into the Hillsbrad Foothills and on to Southshore", text="A long walk, close to 10 minutes. Stay on the road past Durnholde Keep; Tarren Mill, north of the road, is a Horde town"},
  {t="F", seg=12, arg="Southshore", text="Darla Harris, the gryphon master north of the town", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=49.3, y=52.3},
  {t="S", seg=12, arg="Southshore", text="Innkeeper Anderson", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=51.2, y=58.9},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={98463}, names={"Talk of the Town"}, text="Barkeep Kelly, in the same inn (needs level 28): Talk of the Town. Only a message for the barkeep in Booty Bay; you carry it until the route gets there", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=51.6, y=58.6},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={647}, names={"MacKreel's Moonshine"}, text="Brewmeister Bilger, in the inn", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=52.1, y=58.7},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={98071}, names={"Brewer's Trade"}, text="Brewmeister Bilger (new in Forever)", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=52.1, y=58.7},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={98219}, names={"The Shamed Lieutenant"}, text="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle, in the inn", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=51.5, y=58.4},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={536}, names={"Down the Coast"}, text="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=51.5, y=58.4},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={555}, names={"Soothing Turtle Bisque"}, text="Chef Jessen, in the inn", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=51.9, y=58.7},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={564}, names={"Costly Menace"}, text="Darren Malvew (52.4,56.0). Needs level 30", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=52.4, y=56.0},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={565}, names={"Bartolo's Yeti Fur Cloak"}, text="Bartolo Ginsetti (49.4,55.5). Only if you have the Hillman's Cloak and the Bolt of Woolen Cloth", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=49.4, y=55.5},
  {t="N", seg=12, arg="Buy Soothing Spices (555) and Fine Thread (565) from Micha Yance, the trade goods vendor (48.9, 55.0)"},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={505}, names={"Syndicate Assassins"}, text="Magistrate Henry Maleb, in the town hall (48.1,59.1)", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=48.1, y=59.1},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={98059}, names={"Hillsbrad's Hoard"}, text="Captain McManus (new in Forever), north-west of town (46.5,50.1)", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=46.5, y=50.1},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={536}, names={"Down the Coast"}, text="The coast south-west of Southshore (36-49,63-73): 10 Torn Fin Tidehunters (31-32) and 10 Torn Fin Oracles (30-31). Oracles heal and cast: you have no interrupt, so put Curse of Tongues on them and kill them first. Murlocs run at low health and bring friends: keep Corruption and Curse of Agony on each so it dies while it runs, and never Fear on this beach. Send the Voidwalker in from the land side and never fight in the water", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=42.3, y=68.4, path={{44.2,52.5},{44.0,58.5},{40.8,63.3}}},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={536}, names={"Down the Coast"}, text="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=51.5, y=58.4},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={559}, names={"Farren's Proof"}, text="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=51.5, y=58.4},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={559}, names={"Farren's Proof"}, text="Back to the Western Strand. Every Torn Fin murloc drops Murloc Heads (10 needed); the Muckdwellers and Coastrunners further west (20-35,64-76) are only 28-30", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=30.0, y=70.0},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={98059}, names={"Hillsbrad's Hoard"}, text="North to Hillsbrad Fields. The town hall is the big building where the Hillsbrad Councilmen and Magistrate Burnside stand (about 29.7,41.6). Put the Sealed Company Request on the bookkeeping table inside. In Classic these farmers are friendly to the Alliance; if Forever made them hostile, go in and out fast. Horde players quest here", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=29.7, y=41.6},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={565}, names={"Bartolo's Yeti Fur Cloak"}, text="Only if you took 565. The yeti cave in the hills north-east of Hillsbrad Fields (42-47,25-34): Cave Yetis (30-31) and Ferocious Yetis (31-32) drop Yeti Fur, about one in three. 10 needed. Send the Voidwalker at singles at the cave mouth; if a second one comes, back out of the cave, Fear it outside and finish the first. Health Funnel the Voidwalker between your DoTs", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=44.5, y=30.0, path={{35.0,34.9},{38.6,34.9},{42.0,30.1},{46.3,31.6}}, cave=true},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={559}, names={"Farren's Proof"}, text="Back to Southshore. Lieutenant Farren Orinelle", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=51.5, y=58.4},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={560}, names={"Farren's Proof"}, text="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=51.5, y=58.4},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={560}, names={"Farren's Proof"}, text="Marshal Redpath (49.5,58.7)", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=49.5, y=58.7},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={561}, names={"Farren's Proof"}, text="Marshal Redpath", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=49.5, y=58.7},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={561}, names={"Farren's Proof"}, text="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=51.5, y=58.4},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={562}, names={"Stormwind Ho!"}, text="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=51.5, y=58.4},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={98059}, names={"Hillsbrad's Hoard"}, text="Captain McManus", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=46.5, y=50.1},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={565}, names={"Bartolo's Yeti Fur Cloak"}, text="Bartolo Ginsetti (with the cloak, the wool bolt, Fine Thread and 10 Yeti Fur)", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=49.4, y=55.5},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={562}, names={"Stormwind Ho!"}, text="The coast south-east of Southshore (52-62,61-82): 10 Daggerspine Shorehunters (30-31) and 10 Daggerspine Sirens (31-32). Sirens cast: kill them first with Curse of Tongues on them (you have no interrupt). Shorehunters throw nets: a net only holds your feet, so keep casting and let the Voidwalker hold the naga; fight them on land", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=56.9, y=69.2},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={98071}, names={"Brewer's Trade"}, text="Further south-east along the coast to Dun Garok, the dwarven fort (about 71,79). The dwarves are Alliance. Leave the Fallrook Varietal at the fireplace at the bottom of the fort and take a Sack of Homebrew Hops. The exact spot is not in the data", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=71.3, y=78.5},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={562}, names={"Stormwind Ho!"}, text="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle, Southshore", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=51.5, y=58.4, path={{65.2,77.1},{64.0,75.3},{63.6,70.5},{62.0,68.1},{62.0,65.1},{59.8,61.5},{56.4,59.1}}},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={563}, names={"Reassignment"}, text="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle. The report goes to Stormwind Keep: you carry it until segment 15", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=51.5, y=58.4},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={98071}, names={"Brewer's Trade"}, text="Brewmeister Bilger", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=52.0, y=58.6},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={555}, names={"Soothing Turtle Bisque"}, text="Snapjaws (turtles, 30-31) swim in the river north-east of Southshore (56-69,14-57); start where the river meets the road east of town and work upstream until you have 10 Turtle Meat", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=63.5, y=40.0, path={{59.8,59.4},{60.8,57.9},{60.8,53.4},{64.8,48.1}}},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={505,564}, names={"Syndicate Assassins","Costly Menace"}, text="Cross west into the hills north of Southshore, which are the south edge of the Alterac Mountains. Sofera's Naze (the Syndicate camp at 58,68) and Corrahn's Dagger (48,82) hold the Syndicate Footpads (32-33) and Thieves (33-34): 12 and 8. Thieves are stealthed and stun you: keep the Voidwalker out and close so it takes the Thief off you, go in at full health with a Healthstone in your bags, and never start a fight while hurt. Fear a second Syndicate only at the edge of a camp, never in the middle. Mountain Lions (32-33) and Hulking Mountain Lions (33-34) roam the slopes around and between both camps: 8 and 10. Voidwalker first on the lions, all three DoTs, then Drain Life. Rest to full after each pull; they are 2-3 levels above you", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=55.0, y=72.0},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={510}, names={"Foreboding Plans"}, text="Syndicate Documents on the table in the camp: Sofera's Naze (Alterac 58.3,67.9) or Corrahn's Dagger (Alterac 47.9,82.2). Both camps have a copy", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=58.3, y=67.9},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={511}, names={"Encrypted Letter"}, text="The same documents. Needs level 30", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=58.3, y=67.9},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={510}, names={"Foreboding Plans"}, text="Back to Southshore: walk down, or use the Hearthstone (it is bound here and has not been used in this segment). Magistrate Henry Maleb. Leave his next quest: Alterac comes back in segment 16", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=48.1, y=59.1},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={505}, names={"Syndicate Assassins"}, text="Magistrate Henry Maleb", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=48.1, y=59.1},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={511}, names={"Encrypted Letter"}, text="Loremaster Dibbs (50.6,57.1)", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=50.6, y=57.1},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={514}, names={"Letter to Stormpike"}, text="Loremaster Dibbs. For Ironforge", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=50.6, y=57.1},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={555}, names={"Soothing Turtle Bisque"}, text="Chef Jessen", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=51.9, y=58.7},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={564}, names={"Costly Menace"}, text="Darren Malvew", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=52.4, y=56.0},
  {t="FLY", seg=12, arg="Ironforge", text="Darla Harris", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=49.3, y=52.3},
  {t="N", seg=12, arg="Optional dungeon: City of Dalaran, levels 28-33", text="To get in you first need the Dalaran Sewer Key: Emissary Jacques in Southshore gives An Alarming Request, which sends you to the Image of Archmage Modera by Lordamere Lake (Silverpine Forest 68.4, 45.2). She gives Heart of Disruption and Starving Arcane, and with them the key. The way in is through the sewers on the north side of the city, then a portal at the end of a long pipe. One player with the key lets the whole group in. Many enemies here are immune to Arcane damage. Quests you picked up for it: Power Overwhelming, A Green Sample.", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=8.5, y=59.2, dg=6, run=true},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={514}, names={"Letter to Stormpike"}, text="Prospector Stormpike, Hall of Explorers", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=74.6, y=11.7},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={525}, names={"Further Mysteries"}, text="Prospector Stormpike. It goes back to Southshore: keep it until segment 16", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=74.6, y=11.7},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1453}, names={"Reclaimers' Business in Desolace"}, text="Roetten Stonehammer, Reclaimers Inc., in the Hall of Explorers. For Desolace (segment 13)", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=70.0, y=21.3},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={637}, names={"Sully Balloo's Letter"}, text="Sara Balloo (Questie: 63.5,67.3; the ForeverChanges pins for old Ironforge quests use another map scale and are not used here)", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=63.5, y=67.3},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={683}, names={"Sara Balloo's Plea"}, text="Sara Balloo", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=63.5, y=67.3},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={683}, names={"Sara Balloo's Plea"}, text="King Magni Bronzebeard, in the High Seat", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=39.1, y=56.2},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={686}, names={"A King's Tribute"}, text="King Magni Bronzebeard", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=39.1, y=56.2},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={686}, names={"A King's Tribute"}, text="Grand Mason Marblesten (39.0,88.0). Do not take the next step: it needs Alterac Granite", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=39.0, y=88.0},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1179}, names={"The Brassbolts Brothers"}, text="Pilot Longbeard (Questie puts him at 72.7,94.0; the ForeverChanges page says the Hall of Arms). The crate goes to the Shimmering Flats in segment 14", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=72.7, y=94.0},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=12, text="Briarthorn, the warlock trainer in the Forlorn Cavern: learn your level 32 spells if you are 32 (everything he offers). This is your last trainer stop until 36: the next two segments are in Kalimdor", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=50.4, y=5.7},
  {t="N", seg=12, arg="Before you leave: repair, buy food and water, bank what you do not need", text="Keep 3-5 Soul Shards in your bags. You need not save for a mount: a warlock's Felsteed at 40 is a free quest"},
  {t="FLY", seg=12, arg="Menethil Harbor", text="Gryth Thurden", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=55.5, y=47.7},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={2924}, names={"Essential Artificials"}, text="Klockmort Spannerspan in Tinker Town. 12 Essential Artificials from the Artificial Extrapolators inside.", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=67.9, y=46.1, dg=7},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={2930}, names={"Data Rescue"}, text="Master Mechanic Castpipe in Tinker Town. A Prismatic Punch Card: it takes a chain of punch-card machines through the dungeon. Needs level 25.", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=69.8, y=48.1, dg=7},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={2929}, names={"The Grand Betrayal"}, text="High Tinker Mekkatorque in Tinker Town. Kill Mekgineer Thermaplugg, the last boss. Needs level 25.", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=68.8, y=49.0, dg=7},
  {t="N", seg=12, arg="Optional dungeon: Gnomeregan, levels 29-38", text="The entrance is in the west of Dun Morogh, past Brewnall Village: take the lift down and go through the workshop tunnels to the portal. More quests need a small lead-in first: Tinkmaster Overspark in Tinker Town (Save Techbot's Brain!, after a pointer from Brother Sarno in Stormwind) and Ozzie Togglevolt in Kharanos (Gnogaine, after a pointer from Gnoarn in Tinker Town). Inside: Kernobee gives an escort quest that ends with Scooty in Booty Bay. Quests you picked up for it: Gyrodrillmatic Excavationators, Essential Artificials, Data Rescue, The Grand Betrayal.", zone="Dun Morogh", map=1426, x=24.3, y=39.8, dg=7, run=true},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={2924}, names={"Essential Artificials"}, zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=67.9, y=46.1, dg=7},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={2930}, names={"Data Rescue"}, zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=69.8, y=48.1, dg=7},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={2929}, names={"The Grand Betrayal"}, zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=68.8, y=49.0, dg=7},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={98223}, names={"Old Habits"}, text="Captain Stoutfist, Menethil Keep", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=9.9, y=57.4},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1302}, names={"James Hyal"}, text="Vincent Hyal, in the Deepwater Tavern (needs level 30): James Hyal. A message for the clerk in Theramore; you carry it until the route gets there", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.8, y=60.4},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={270}, names={"The Doomed Fleet"}, text="Glorin Steelbrow, in the Deepwater Tavern", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.6, y=60.6},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={321}, names={"Lightforge Iron"}, text="Glorin Steelbrow", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.6, y=60.6},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={321}, names={"Lightforge Iron"}, text="The Waterlogged Chest in the wreck of the Flying Osprey, south of the docks (12.1,64.2)", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=12.1, y=64.2},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={324}, names={"The Lost Ingots"}, text="The same chest", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=12.1, y=64.2},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={324}, names={"The Lost Ingots"}, text="Bluegill Raiders (28-29) around the wreck and on the shore south of it drop the 5 Lightforge Ingots. They are green to you now", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=13.0, y=65.5},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={324}, names={"The Lost Ingots"}, text="Glorin Steelbrow. Do not take Blessed Arm (322)", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.6, y=60.6},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1248}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Mikhail, at the bar in the Deepwater Tavern", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.6, y=60.8},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1249}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Mikhail. Read the next step before you accept", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.6, y=60.8},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={1249}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Tapoke \"Slim\" Jahn (34) sits near Mikhail (10.5,60.3). When you accept he tries to leave and fights. He is 2-4 levels above you: be at full health and mana with the Voidwalker out, stand between him and the door before you accept, send the Voidwalker at him at once, put Curse of Agony, Corruption and Immolate on him and Drain Life until he gives up. Do not Fear him: he must not get out of the door. If he gets away, abandon and take the quest again", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.5, y=60.3},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1249}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Mikhail", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.6, y=60.8},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1250}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Tapoke \"Slim\" Jahn, once he has given up", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.5, y=60.3},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1250}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Mikhail", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.6, y=60.8},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1264}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Mikhail. For Commander Samaul in Theramore (segment 14)", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.6, y=60.8},
  {t="N", seg=12, arg="Take the boat from Menethil Harbor to Auberdine", text="Segment done. In the log: 525, 563, 1026, 1179, 1264, 1453. Your hearthstone stays in Southshore until Astranaar"},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={98209}, names={"Bloom of the Heavens"}, text="Thundris Windweaver, the elder in the building at the north end of Auberdine: hand him Nord'el", zone="Darkshore", map=1439, x=37.4, y=40.1},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1275}, names={"Researching the Corruption"}, zone="Darkshore", map=1439, x=38.3, y=43.0, dg=4},
  {t="FLY", seg=13, arg="Astranaar", text="Caylais Moonfeather, on the Auberdine dock where the boat lands", zone="Darkshore", map=1439, x=36.3, y=45.6},
  {t="S", seg=13, arg="Astranaar", text="Innkeeper Kimlya. You hearth back here twice in this segment", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=37.0, y=49.2},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1035}, names={"Fallen Sky Lake"}, text="Pelturas Whitemoon, Astranaar (37.4,51.8)", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=37.4, y=51.8},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={4581}, names={"Kayneth Stillwind"}, text="Shindrell Swiftfire, Astranaar (34.7,48.8)", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=34.7, y=48.8},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1022}, names={"The Howling Vale"}, text="Take the road west to the Shrine of Aessina (22,53). Sentinel Melyria Frostshadow. The quest text says Forest Song, but Questie and ForeverChanges both place her here", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=22.2, y=53.0},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1021}, names={"Vile Satyr! Dryads in Danger!"}, text="Illiyana, the dryad next to her", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=21.7, y=53.3},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={86757}, names={"Slowing the Orc Advance"}, text="Back east through Astranaar, then south-east to Silverwind Refuge on Mystral Lake. Shandrina (new in Forever). The orcs for it are in the far south-east: you kill them on the loop below", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=49.4, y=67.0},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1022}, names={"The Howling Vale"}, text="Go north across the road into the Howling Vale. The Tome of Mel'Thandris stands in the ruined shrine at 50.5,39.1; the way in is through the short cave at 53.0,37.6. Worgen (27-30) stand close together: send the Voidwalker at singles and do not Fear in the vale (a feared worgen brings the others); leave the rare if one is up. Click the tome", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=50.5, y=39.1, path={{51.7,38.3}}, cave=true},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1026}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="East of the vale, along the road to Felwood: Withered Ancients (26-27, at 54-59,33-42) and Crazed Ancients (27-28, at 57-62,31-45) drop the Wooden Key. They are elementals: if two come, Banish one and kill the other. Then open the Worn Chest in the small glade west of the road at 54.4,35.4 for the Iron Shaft", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=56.5, y=36.5},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1026}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="Shael'dryn, the dryad at the moonwell beside the main road (53.5,46.2)", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=53.5, y=46.2},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1027}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="Shael'dryn. The last rod piece is at Dor'danil in the south-east: you pick it up later on this loop", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=53.5, y=46.2},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1021}, names={"Vile Satyr! Dryads in Danger!"}, text="Follow the main road east. Anilia lies at the edge of the Xavian satyr camp, north of the road (78.3,44.8). Kill the one or two satyrs next to her (satyrs are demons: Banish the second one while the Voidwalker holds the first); the rest of the camp comes later", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=78.3, y=44.8},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1031}, names={"The Branch of Cenarius"}, text="Anilia", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=78.3, y=44.8},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={4581}, names={"Kayneth Stillwind"}, text="Kayneth Stillwind at Forest Song, at the east end of the road (85.2,44.7)", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=85.2, y=44.7, path={{82.3,46.3},{84.7,46.3}}},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1011}, names={"Forsaken Diseases"}, text="Kayneth Stillwind", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=85.2, y=44.7},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={98417}, names={"Vengeful Trail"}, text="Maseara Autumnmoon, Forest Song (new in Forever)", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=86.2, y=45.8},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={98417}, names={"Vengeful Trail"}, text="Satyrnaar, the satyr camp south-west of Forest Song (about 80-82,48-52). Find the Vine-Wrapped Scroll: the data does not say whether it drops from the satyrs (28-30) or lies in the camp, so kill and look around. Hellcallers cast and you have no interrupt: put Curse of Tongues on them and kill them first. Satyrs are demons: Banish a second one instead of using Fear inside the camp", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=81.0, y=50.0},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={98417}, names={"Vengeful Trail"}, text="Maseara Autumnmoon", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=86.3, y=45.8},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={98418}, names={"Shared Fury"}, text="Maseara Autumnmoon", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=86.3, y=45.8},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={98418,1031}, names={"Shared Fury","The Branch of Cenarius"}, text="Xavian (77-80,42-48): 5 Xavian Rogues, 5 Felsworn, 5 Betrayers and 5 Hellcallers (28-30). There are only 2 Betrayer spawns: wait for them to come back. Geltharis (32) stands at the north end at 78.0,42.4: clear around him, rest to full, then fight him alone: Voidwalker first, Curse of Tongues on him to slow his casts, Corruption, Immolate, Drain Life. Banish a satyr that joins in. He drops the Branch of Cenarius", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=78.4, y=45.4},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={98418}, names={"Shared Fury"}, text="Maseara Autumnmoon at Forest Song. The ForeverChanges page also shows a hand-in at Satyrnaar (81.0,50.2): if she is not at Forest Song, look there", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=86.3, y=45.8},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1011}, names={"Forsaken Diseases"}, text="South from Forest Song, past the Warsong lumber camp (stay west of it). The Forsaken camp is outside the Dor'danil Barrow Den; the Bottles of Disease stand on the ground at 75.3,72.0. Forsaken here are 28-30 and stealthed in part: walk in at full health with the Voidwalker beside you, and Fear a second one away from the camp", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=75.3, y=72.0, path={{78.9,46.3},{76.3,52.8},{71.4,58.8},{71.6,69.0}}},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1027}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="The Rusty Chest with the Iron Pommel is at Dor'danil too. Its spot is not in the data: check in front of and just inside the barrow den entrance and along the hill behind the Forsaken camp", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=76.0, y=73.5},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={86757}, names={"Slowing the Orc Advance"}, text="Warsong orcs (scouts and grunts, about 28-30) drop Jagged Orcish Swords (6) and Curved Orcish Daggers (4). ForeverChanges saw the drops south-west of Dor'danil toward Fallen Sky Lake (65-75,75-85) and around the lumber camp south of Forest Song (85-90,50-65). Camps are Horde-flagged: send the Voidwalker at stragglers at the edges, and do not Fear toward a camp", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=70.0, y=79.0},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1035}, names={"Fallen Sky Lake"}, text="Fallen Sky Lake: the Shadethicket Oracle (30) stands on the island in the middle (66.7,82.2). Bark Rippers and Stone Movers around it are 25-27. He drops the Fallen Moonstone", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=66.7, y=82.2},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1011}, names={"Forsaken Diseases"}, text="Back north to Kayneth Stillwind at Forest Song (finish the orc weapons at the lumber camp on the way if you are short)", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=85.2, y=44.7, path={{68.8,82.2},{71.8,75.6},{71.4,58.8},{76.3,52.8},{76.5,50.4},{78.9,46.3},{84.7,46.3}}},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1012}, names={"Insane Druids"}, text="Kayneth Stillwind", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=85.2, y=44.7},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1012}, names={"Insane Druids"}, text="Back to the Dor'danil Barrow Den, this time inside: Taneel Darkwood (77.2,74.0), Uthil Mooncall (78.0,72.7) and Mavoris Cloudsbreak (75.1,74.2), all level 32, with Severed druids (28-30) between them. Clear each room first. They cast heals and roots and you have no interrupt: keep Curse of Tongues on the druid to slow the heals, all DoTs up, and the Voidwalker on him. Roots only hold your feet: keep casting. Do not Fear inside the den", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=76.8, y=73.6, path={{84.7,46.3},{78.9,46.3},{76.3,52.8},{71.2,59.4},{71.6,69.0}}},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1012}, names={"Insane Druids"}, text="Kayneth Stillwind", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=85.2, y=44.7, path={{71.6,69.0},{71.2,59.4},{76.3,52.8},{76.5,50.4},{78.9,46.3},{84.7,46.3}}},
  {t="F", seg=13, arg="Talrendis Point", text="Follow the road east from Forest Song over the bridge into Azshara. Talrendis Point is right behind the border; Jarrodenus is the hippogryph master", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=11.9, y=77.6},
  {t="FLY", seg=13, arg="Astranaar", text="Jarrodenus"},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1035}, names={"Fallen Sky Lake"}, text="Pelturas Whitemoon", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=37.4, y=51.8},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1027}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="Run east along the road to Shael'dryn at the moonwell (53.5,46.2)", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=53.5, y=46.2},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1028}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="Shael'dryn", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=53.5, y=46.2},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1028}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="The Hidden Shrine, in the woods just south-east of the moonwell (56.4,49.2)", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=56.4, y=49.2},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1055}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="The Hidden Shrine", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=56.4, y=49.2},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1055}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="Shael'dryn", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=53.5, y=46.2},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1029}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="Shael'dryn", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=53.5, y=46.2},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1029}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="Walk back west along the main road to Astranaar (about 5 minutes; keep the Hearthstone for the end of the furbolg run). Raene Wolfrunner (36.6,49.6)", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=36.6, y=49.6, path={{52.6,50.7},{49.8,51.6},{48.2,54.0},{44.8,54.0},{43.2,48.4},{36.8,48.1}}},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1030}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="Raene Wolfrunner. You now carry Dartol's Rod of Transformation", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=36.6, y=49.6},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1022}, names={"The Howling Vale"}, text="West to the Shrine of Aessina. Sentinel Melyria Frostshadow. Do not take Velinde Starsong: it sends you to Darnassus", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=22.2, y=53.0},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1031}, names={"The Branch of Cenarius"}, text="Illiyana. Do not take Satyr Slaying!: you are done with the satyrs", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=21.7, y=53.3},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={86757}, names={"Slowing the Orc Advance"}, text="Back east and south to Silverwind Refuge. Shandrina", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=49.4, y=67.0},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1030}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="Krolg, the friendly furbolg on the south shore of Mystral Lake (50.8,75.1). Use Dartol's Rod of Transformation before you talk to him: he only speaks to furbolgs", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=50.8, y=75.1},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1045}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="Krolg (still transformed)", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=50.8, y=75.1},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1045}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="The Bloodtooth camp just south-east of Krolg (54-56,75-80): 4 Bloodtooth Guards (27-28) and Ran Bloodtooth (30, at the back, 54.8,79.6). Easy at your level with the Voidwalker in front; taking damage ends the furbolg form", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=54.8, y=78.1},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1045}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="Krolg (use the rod again)", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=50.8, y=75.1},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1046}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="Krolg", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=50.8, y=75.1},
  {t="H", seg=13, arg="Astranaar", text="Hearthstone to Astranaar"},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1046}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="Raene Wolfrunner", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=36.6, y=49.6},
  {t="N", seg=13, arg="Repair, buy food and water. Then go to Desolace on foot", text="South out of Astranaar to the Talondeep Path (the tunnel at Ashenvale 42.3,71.0). It comes out in Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. Follow the road west and then south-west past Sun Rock Retreat (Horde: stay on the far side of the lake) into the Charred Vale, and leave it by the pass at its south end into Desolace. A long walk, 15 minutes or more. Charred Vale mobs are 26-30"},
  {t="F", seg=13, arg="Nijel's Point", text="Nijel's Point is in the hills in the north-east of Desolace; the path up starts from the road east of the Thunder Axe Fortress. Baritanas Skyriver is the hippogryph master", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=64.7, y=10.5},
  {t="S", seg=13, arg="Nijel's Point", text="Innkeeper Lyshaerya", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.3, y=6.5},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1453}, names={"Reclaimers' Business in Desolace"}, text="Kreldig Ungor", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.2, y=9.6},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1458,1454}, names={"Reagents for Reclaimers Inc.","The Karnitol Shipwreck"}, text="Kreldig Ungor", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.2, y=9.6},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1387}, names={"Centaur Bounty"}, text="Corporal Melkins", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.7, y=10.9},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1382}, names={"Strange Alliance"}, text="Captain Pentigast", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.7, y=10.9},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={93224}, names={"Carved Centaur Totems"}, text="Captain Pentigast (new in Forever): 5 Carved Centaur Totems from centaurs of any clan", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.6, y=11.0},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1437}, names={"Vahlarriel's Search"}, text="Vahlarriel Demonslayer", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.4, y=11.8},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1437}, names={"Vahlarriel's Search"}, text="The Malem Chest in the wrecked wagon west of Nijel's Point, by the road (56.5,17.8)", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=56.5, y=17.8},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1465}, names={"Vahlarriel's Search"}, text="The same chest", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=56.5, y=17.8},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1465}, names={"Vahlarriel's Search"}, text="Back up to Vahlarriel Demonslayer", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.4, y=11.8},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1438}, names={"Vahlarriel's Search"}, text="Vahlarriel Demonslayer", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.4, y=11.8},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={97284}, names={"Vahlarriel's Vengeance"}, text="Vahlarriel Demonslayer (new in Forever). The data has no giver for it; its text fits this moment. If she does not offer it yet, take it after the escort and skip its steps until then", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.4, y=11.8},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1458}, names={"Reagents for Reclaimers Inc."}, text="Sargeron, the satyr ruins east of Nijel's Point (71-81,9-30). Any Hatefury satyr (31-33) drops claws and horns: 10 each. Rogues and Shadowstalkers are stealthed, Hellcallers and Felsworn cast: kill the casters first with Curse of Tongues on them (you have no interrupt). Keep the Voidwalker close so it takes a stealthed satyr off you. Work along the outer edge of the ruins so only one comes at a time; satyrs are demons, so Banish a second one and finish the first in peace. Kill the Scorpashi Snappers you pass from now on and keep their venom", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=75.5, y=19.5},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1458}, names={"Reagents for Reclaimers Inc."}, text="Kreldig Ungor", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.2, y=9.6},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1459}, names={"Reagents for Reclaimers Inc."}, text="Kreldig Ungor: 7 Scorpashi Venom and 3 Aged Kodo Hides", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.2, y=9.6},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1459}, names={"Reagents for Reclaimers Inc."}, text="On the way west: Scorpashi Snappers (30-31) are all over the north of the zone; Aged Kodos (34-35) walk along the main road south of Thunder Axe (45-59,19-83). A kodo is a long fight at 33: start at full health and mana, with nothing else close by, let the Voidwalker hold it, keep all three DoTs up, Health Funnel the Voidwalker and Drain Life when the kodo turns on you; rest after each one. Drain Soul the last hit when you are short of Soul Shards. Hides do not always drop", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=56.0, y=22.0},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={5741}, names={"Sceptre of Light"}, text="Azore Aldamort, in the tower at Ethel Rethor on the west coast (38.9,27.2)", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=38.9, y=27.2},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={6161}, names={"Claim Rackmore's Treasure!"}, text="Rackmore's Log, on the beach at the shipwreck just south-west of the tower (36.1,30.4)", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=36.1, y=30.4},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1454}, names={"The Karnitol Shipwreck"}, text="Karnitol's Chest, in the same wreck (36.1,30.5)", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=36.1, y=30.5},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1455}, names={"The Karnitol Shipwreck"}, text="Karnitol's Chest", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=36.1, y=30.5},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={6161}, obj={1}, names={"Claim Rackmore's Treasure!"}, text="Rackmore's Silver Key: Drysnap Crawlers and Pincers (33-35), the makrura on the beach and in the shallows south of the wreck (18-35,28-84)", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=30.0, y=33.0},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={6161}, obj={2}, names={"Claim Rackmore's Treasure!"}, text="Rackmore's Golden Key: any Slitherblade naga. The Nagas and Sorceresses at the ruins just north of the tower (33-42,19-28) are 32-33. Sorceresses cast: Curse of Tongues on them and kill them first; Fear a second naga along the beach, away from the ruins", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=37.0, y=23.0},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={97284,5741}, names={"Vahlarriel's Vengeance","Sceptre of Light"}, text="East to Thunder Axe Fortress (52-58,21-33). Kill 4 each of Burning Blade Augurs, Reavers, Adepts and Felsworn (30-32). The Sceptre of Light is carried by the Burning Blade Seer on top of one of the watchtowers: fight your way up the ramp. Casters everywhere and you have no interrupt: Curse of Tongues on each, and step back behind a wall or the doorway so they have to walk to you and the Voidwalker. Never Fear inside the fortress and never fight three", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=55.0, y=27.0},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1438}, names={"Vahlarriel's Search"}, text="Dalinda Malem, held inside the fortress (54.9,26.1)", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=54.9, y=26.1},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1439}, names={"Search for Tyranis"}, text="Dalinda Malem", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=54.9, y=26.1},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1439}, names={"Search for Tyranis"}, text="Tyranis Malem (36) is at 53.0,29.1, in the south-west part of the fortress. He is 2-3 levels above you and casts: clear the room, rest to full, put a Soulstone on yourself and make a Healthstone. Then Voidwalker first, Curse of Tongues on him (you have no interrupt), Corruption, Immolate and Drain Life; Health Funnel the Voidwalker, and use its Sacrifice shield, the Healthstone and a potion when he turns on you. He drops Tyranis' Pendant. If he is too strong, come back after the coast loop", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=53.0, y=29.1},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1439}, names={"Search for Tyranis"}, text="Dalinda Malem", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=54.9, y=26.1},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1440}, names={"Return to Vahlarriel"}, text="Dalinda Malem. Clear the way to the gate first: it is an escort", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=54.9, y=26.1},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1440}, names={"Return to Vahlarriel"}, text="Walk Dalinda out of the fortress. Stay in front of her, let the Voidwalker hold the attackers and DoT each one (you cannot heal her); it ends at the gate", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=56.5, y=28.5},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1440}, names={"Return to Vahlarriel"}, text="Back up to Nijel's Point. Vahlarriel Demonslayer", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.4, y=11.8},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={97284}, names={"Vahlarriel's Vengeance"}, text="Vahlarriel Demonslayer", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.4, y=11.8},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1455}, names={"The Karnitol Shipwreck"}, text="Kreldig Ungor", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.2, y=9.6},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1456}, names={"The Karnitol Shipwreck"}, text="Kreldig Ungor", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.2, y=9.6},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1459}, names={"Reagents for Reclaimers Inc."}, text="Kreldig Ungor (if the venom and hides are done; otherwise on your next visit)", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.2, y=9.6},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1466}, names={"Reagents for Reclaimers Inc."}, text="Kreldig Ungor. Mannoroc Coven demons are 37-40: this is the last thing you do in Desolace", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.2, y=9.6},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={5741}, names={"Sceptre of Light"}, text="Back west to Azore Aldamort at Ethel Rethor", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=38.9, y=27.2, path={{66.2,14.5},{64.6,16.6},{65.6,19.0},{65.6,28.0},{63.8,34.9},{47.6,34.3},{45.8,31.6},{41.0,31.0}}},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={6027}, names={"Book of the Ancients"}, text="Azore Aldamort. He gives you the Gem of the Serpent", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=38.9, y=27.2},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1456}, names={"The Karnitol Shipwreck"}, text="Swim north-west to Ranazjar Isle (28-35,6-17); Unending Breath if you dive. Karnitol's Satchel drops from Slitherblade Tidehunters (36-37) and Sea Witches (35-36), about one in five. They are 2-4 levels above you: one at a time, on land, at full health, Voidwalker first; Curse of Tongues on the witches to slow their casts, Fear a second naga along the shore, and expect some resists. Get the Golden Key here if you still need it", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=30.5, y=11.0},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={6027}, names={"Book of the Ancients"}, text="Put the Gem of the Serpent in the hand of the Serpent Statue on the isle (its exact spot is not in the data; it is the large naga statue). Lord Kragaru (38) appears: he is 4-5 levels above you. Clear the area first, rest to full, put a Soulstone on yourself and make a Healthstone. Send the Voidwalker first and give it a few seconds, then Curse of Agony, Corruption, Immolate and Drain Life; Health Funnel the Voidwalker, and keep its Sacrifice shield, the Healthstone and a potion for when he turns on you. Many spells will be resisted at this level gap. He drops the Book of the Ancients. Too strong? Abandon 6027", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=28.5, y=7.0},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={6161}, names={"Claim Rackmore's Treasure!"}, text="Rackmore's Chest on the isle (30.0,8.7): it needs both keys", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=30.0, y=8.7},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={6027}, names={"Book of the Ancients"}, text="Azore Aldamort", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=38.9, y=27.2},
  {t="H", seg=13, arg="Nijel's Point", text="Hearthstone (last used in Ashenvale, so it is ready). Not ready? Walk the road east past Thunder Axe and up the path"},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1456}, names={"The Karnitol Shipwreck"}, text="Kreldig Ungor", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.2, y=9.6},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1457}, names={"The Karnitol Shipwreck"}, text="Kreldig Ungor. The satchel goes to Roetten Stonehammer in Ironforge: you keep it until segment 15", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.2, y=9.6},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={261}, names={"Down the Scarlet Path"}, text="Brother Anton (66.5,7.9). Needs level 34: if you are not 34 yet, take it on your next visit here, before the last loop", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.5, y=7.9},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={5501}, names={"Bone Collector"}, text="Follow the road south to Kormek's Hut (62.3,39.0). Bibbly F'utzbuckle. Needs level 33", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=62.3, y=39.0},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={5821}, names={"Bodyguard for Hire"}, text="Cork Gizelton, with the kodo caravan (60.4,38.1). Only when the caravan is standing at Kormek's Hut; otherwise skip the three 5821 steps", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=60.4, y=38.1},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={5821}, names={"Bodyguard for Hire"}, text="Walk with the caravan past the Kolkar village and kill the centaurs that attack it: the Voidwalker holds one, you DoT them all, Fear a third. It ends south of the village", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.0, y=45.0, path={{63.2,37.6},{65.4,40.9},{65.2,43.9}}},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1387,93224}, names={"Centaur Bounty","Carved Centaur Totems"}, text="Kolkar Village, east of Kormek's Hut (68-75,39-52): Kolkar are 30-33: Voidwalker first, DoTs, and Fear a second one away from the tents. Every centaur drops Centaur Ears (15 needed); the Carved Centaur Totems (5) come from centaurs of any clan too. You get more of both from the Magram later", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=71.5, y=45.5},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={5561}, names={"Kodo Roundup"}, text="Road south to Scrabblescrew's Camp (60.9,61.9). Smeed Scrabblescrew", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=60.9, y=61.9},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={5821}, names={"Bodyguard for Hire"}, text="Smeed Scrabblescrew (only if you escorted the caravan)", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=60.9, y=61.9},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={5943}, names={"Gizelton Caravan"}, text="Rigger Gizelton, with the caravan, when it stands at Scrabblescrew's Camp. Demons of 37-39 attack it at Mannoroc Coven: take it only if the caravan is here and you are at least 35; otherwise skip the three 5943 steps", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=60.3, y=38.2},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={5943}, names={"Gizelton Caravan"}, text="Walk with the caravan past Mannoroc Coven and kill what attacks it. The attackers are demons: the Voidwalker holds one, Banish a second, DoT the rest", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=56.0, y=72.0},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={5943}, names={"Gizelton Caravan"}, text="Smeed Scrabblescrew", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=60.9, y=61.9},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={5561,5501}, names={"Kodo Roundup","Bone Collector"}, text="The Kodo Graveyard, west of the camp (46-54,57-64). Pick up 10 Kodo Bones from the bone piles. Use the Kodo Kombobulator on an Aged, Dying or Ancient Kodo (34-37) to tame it, walk it back to Smeed and talk to it there; five times, one kodo at a time", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=51.5, y=60.0},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={5561}, names={"Kodo Roundup"}, text="Smeed Scrabblescrew", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=60.9, y=61.9},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1382}, names={"Strange Alliance"}, text="Magram Village in the south-east (65-76,66-83). Kill Magram centaurs (32-36) until you are Friendly with the Gelkis Clan; each kill shows the gain in the chat log. How many it takes is not in the data: plan for a long grind. Scouts, Wranglers and Windchasers at the north edge are 32-34; Windchasers and Stormers cast, so put Curse of Tongues on them and kill them first. Send the Voidwalker at each centaur, DoT it and wand; Fear a second one only toward the open ground outside the village. Life Tap and Drain Life keep the grind going without much drinking. Stay away from Khan Jehn (37) in the middle. Finish your ears and totems here", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=69.5, y=74.5},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1382}, names={"Strange Alliance"}, text="West along the south road to Gelkis Village. Uthek the Wise stands at the north edge (36.2,79.2). The Gelkis no longer attack you", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=36.2, y=79.2, path={{66.6,70.5},{63.8,70.8},{62.4,73.8},{59.0,73.5},{57.2,70.8},{57.2,68.1},{53.2,61.5},{44.2,61.5},{42.0,65.1},{42.0,70.8},{38.2,76.2},{38.2,79.5}}},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1384}, names={"Raid on the Kolkar"}, text="Uthek the Wise: 10 Crude Charms from the Kolkar", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=36.2, y=79.2},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={6132}, names={"Get Me Out of Here!"}, text="North up the coast to the Valley of Spears. Melizza Brimbuzzle is held in the Maraudine camp (33.9,53.5). Needs level 34. Maraudine centaurs are 35-39: clear a path to her and out again before you accept", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=33.9, y=53.5},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={6132}, names={"Get Me Out of Here!"}, text="Escort Melizza east out of the valley. Stay beside her and let the Voidwalker hold the attackers while you DoT them; you cannot heal her", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=40.0, y=57.0},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={6132}, names={"Get Me Out of Here!"}, text="Hornizz Brimbuzzle, at the camp on the west side of the Kodo Graveyard (47.8,61.8)", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=47.8, y=61.8},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={6134}, names={"Ghost-o-plasm Round Up"}, text="Hornizz Brimbuzzle. For the last loop", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=47.8, y=61.8},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={5501}, names={"Bone Collector"}, text="Back north along the road to Kormek's Hut. Bibbly F'utzbuckle", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=62.3, y=39.0, path={{56.6,62.4},{57.8,60.6},{59.8,56.4},{58.2,52.5},{58.0,40.3},{61.6,37.6}}},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1384}, names={"Raid on the Kolkar"}, text="Kolkar Village again: Crude Charms drop from every Kolkar, best from Windchasers and Scouts", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=71.5, y=45.5, path={{62.6,37.6},{65.6,37.9},{68.0,35.8},{69.6,38.2},{69.8,42.7}}},
  {t="H", seg=13, arg="Nijel's Point", text="Hearthstone. This loop takes well over an hour, so it is ready; if not, walk the road north from Kormek's Hut"},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1387}, names={"Centaur Bounty"}, text="Corporal Melkins. Take Down the Scarlet Path (261) from Brother Anton now if you could not before", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.7, y=10.9},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={93224}, names={"Carved Centaur Totems"}, text="Captain Pentigast. His hand-in text hints at a follow-up delivery to a clan (not in the data): if he offers one for the Gelkis, take it along to Uthek on the next loop", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.6, y=11.0},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1384}, names={"Raid on the Kolkar"}, text="The long run south-west to Uthek the Wise at Gelkis Village (36.2,79.2): road south past Kormek's Hut and the Kodo Graveyard, then south-west. Check that you are still Friendly", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=36.2, y=79.2, path={{66.6,13.9},{64.6,16.6},{65.6,19.0},{65.6,28.0},{63.8,34.9},{49.6,34.3},{47.2,36.1},{46.6,45.4},{42.6,54.6},{42.0,70.8},{38.2,76.2},{38.0,79.8}}},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1370}, names={"Stealing Supplies"}, text="Uthek the Wise", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=36.2, y=79.2},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1370}, names={"Stealing Supplies"}, text="East to Magram Village: 6 bags of Crudely Dried Meat from the Sacks of Meat beside the tents (65.8,80.5 / 69.2,77.3 / 70.9,75.4 / 73.5,73.8 and more)", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=70.5, y=76.5, path={{38.2,79.5},{38.2,76.2},{42.0,70.8},{42.0,65.4},{43.2,63.6},{49.6,67.8},{56.2,66.9},{57.2,70.8},{59.6,73.8},{62.4,73.8},{63.8,70.8},{66.6,70.5}}},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={261,6134}, names={"Down the Scarlet Path","Ghost-o-plasm Round Up"}, text="The Valley of Bones, south of Magram Village (58-65,82-92). Undead Ravagers are 37-38 and you need 30: one at a time, at full health, Voidwalker first, all three DoTs, then Drain Life; Fear a second one (the valley is open, but watch where it runs), and eat, drink or bandage after every fight. If they are still orange and each fight nearly kills you, abandon 261. For Hornizz: place a Ghost Magnet between the two giant skeletons (63.5,91.6), step back and kill the Magrami Spectres (38-39) that walk to it one by one; 8 Ghost-o-plasms", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=63.0, y=89.0},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1466}, names={"Reagents for Reclaimers Inc."}, text="Mannoroc Coven, west of the valley (51-58,69-85): 10 Felhound Brains from Mage Hunters (38-39, at 53-58,73-79), 10 Nether Wings from Nether Sorceresses (39-40) and 10 Doomwarder Blood from Doomwarder Captains (38), both at the south end around 51.7,83.4. Felhounds drain mana: kill them fast and get mana back with Life Tap. Everything here is a demon: Banish the second one of every pull, never Fear between the packs, and put Curse of Tongues on the Sorceresses. Soulstone on yourself, a Healthstone in your bags, Voidwalker always first. This is the hardest step of the segment: if you cannot kill a Sorceress at 35, abandon 1466; segment 15 then has only the satchel (1457) for Ironforge", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=53.0, y=78.0},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1370}, names={"Stealing Supplies"}, text="Uthek the Wise, Gelkis Village. Do not take Ongeku (1373): the Draenethyst Shard is in the Swamp of Sorrows on the other continent, and the route does not come back here afterwards", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=36.2, y=79.2},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={6134}, names={"Ghost-o-plasm Round Up"}, text="Hornizz Brimbuzzle, Kodo Graveyard", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=47.8, y=61.8},
  {t="H", seg=13, arg="Nijel's Point", text="Hearthstone. If it is still on cooldown, walk the road north past Kormek's Hut (about 8 minutes)"},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={261}, names={"Down the Scarlet Path"}, text="Brother Anton. Do not take his next quest: it sends you to the Scarlet Monastery line", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.5, y=7.9},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1466}, names={"Reagents for Reclaimers Inc."}, text="Kreldig Ungor", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.2, y=9.6},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1467}, names={"Reagents for Reclaimers Inc."}, text="Kreldig Ungor. Leftwitch's Package goes to Roetten Stonehammer in Ironforge (segment 15)", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=66.2, y=9.6},
  {t="N", seg=13, arg="Segment done. In the log: 525, 563, 1179, 1264, 1457, 1467", text="Next: fly from Nijel's Point to Astranaar. Your hearthstone stays at Nijel's Point"},
  {t="N", seg=14, arg="Have 3 Soothing Spices in your bags", text="You bought them in Southshore earlier. None left? No problem: Helenia Olden sells them in Theramore (66.4, 51.5), you then do Jarl's two quests on the loop out of Theramore later in this segment."},
  {t="FLY", seg=14, arg="Astranaar", text="Baritanas Skyriver, the hippogryph master at Nijel's Point", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=64.7, y=10.5},
  {t="N", seg=14, arg="Walk from Astranaar to Ratchet", text="A long walk. Take the road east from Astranaar, then the road south into the Barrens. The border gate (Mor'shan Rampart) is a Horde guard post: do not stop, run straight through or around the side. In the Barrens stay on the road south, leave it before the Crossroads (a Horde town, pass it well to the east) and follow the road east to Ratchet on the coast. Ratchet is neutral. This is Classic geography, not re-checked.", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=63.1, y=37.2},
  {t="F", seg=14, arg="Ratchet", text="Bragok, the flight master near the dock", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=63.1, y=37.2},
  {t="N", seg=14, arg="Walk south to the Great Lift and on to the Mirage Raceway", text="From Ratchet go back west to the main road and follow it south through the whole Barrens (pass Camp Taurajo, a Horde camp, at a distance) to the Great Lift at the south end. Ride the lift down into Thousand Needles and follow the canyon road east, past Freewind Post (Horde, up on a mesa: just keep walking), until the canyon opens into the white salt flats. The Mirage Raceway is in the middle of the flats.", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.0, y=77.0},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1179}, names={"The Brassbolts Brothers"}, text="Wizzle Brassbolts, on the gnome side of the raceway", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.1, y=77.1},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1105}, names={"Hardened Shells"}, text="Wizzle Brassbolts", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.1, y=77.1},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1104}, names={"Salt Flat Venom"}, text="Fizzle Brassbolts, next to him", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.1, y=77.1},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1106}, names={"Martek the Exiled"}, text="Fizzle Brassbolts. A letter for Martek in the Badlands: keep it, a later segment hands it in.", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.1, y=77.1},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1110}, names={"Rocket Car Parts"}, text="Kravel Koalbeard, a few steps away", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=77.8, y=77.3},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={5762}, names={"Hemet Nesingwary"}, text="Kravel Koalbeard. A crate for Hemet Nesingwary in Stranglethorn: keep it for the next segment.", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=77.8, y=77.3},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1111}, names={"Wharfmaster Dizzywig"}, text="Kravel Koalbeard. An order for Wharfmaster Dizzywig in Ratchet: keep it for the next Kalimdor trip.", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=77.8, y=77.3},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1176}, names={"Load Lightening"}, text="Pozzik, on the goblin side of the track", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=80.2, y=75.9},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1175}, names={"A Bump in the Road"}, text="Trackmaster Zherin, at the east end of the goblin side", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=81.6, y=78.0},
  {t="C", seg=14, q={1105,1104,1175}, obj={0,0,1}, names={"Hardened Shells","Salt Flat Venom","A Bump in the Road"}, text="North half of the flats. Sparkleshell Tortoises (30-31) and Snappers (34-35) drop the shells, Scorpid Reavers (31-32) the venom, and the Saltstone Basilisks (30-31) only live up here: kill 10. Salt Flats Scavengers (the vultures here) drop Hollow Vulture Bones, Saltstone Crystalhides count for Zherin, and every Rocket Car Rubble pile on the ground holds car parts: pick up all you pass. Everything here is below your level: send the Voidwalker, put Corruption and Curse of Agony on the target and wand it down; Drain Soul the last hit of a few kills until you carry 3-5 Soul Shards. Just do not pull a whole pack at once.", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=76.0, y=60.0},
  {t="C", seg=14, q={1175,1176,1110}, names={"A Bump in the Road","Load Lightening","Rocket Car Parts"}, text="South half, below the raceway. Saltstone Gazers (34-35) are only down here: kill 6. Finish the 10 Crystalhides, get the rest of the 10 vulture bones from the Salt Flats Vultures and keep picking up rubble until you have 30 Rocket Car Parts. Scorpid Terrors and Sparkleshell Borers here also drop venom and shells if you are short.", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.0, y=85.0},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1105}, names={"Hardened Shells"}, text="Wizzle Brassbolts", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.1, y=77.1},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1104}, names={"Salt Flat Venom"}, text="Fizzle Brassbolts", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.1, y=77.1},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1110}, names={"Rocket Car Parts"}, text="Kravel Koalbeard", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=77.8, y=77.3},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1176}, names={"Load Lightening"}, text="Pozzik", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=80.2, y=75.9},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1178}, names={"Goblin Sponsorship"}, text="Pozzik. A message for Gazlowe in Ratchet: keep it for the next Kalimdor trip.", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=80.2, y=75.9},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1175}, names={"A Bump in the Road"}, text="Trackmaster Zherin", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=81.6, y=78.0},
  {t="N", seg=14, arg="Walk south into Tanaris to Gadgetzan", text="Leave the flats by the pass in the south wall and follow the road south to the goblin town. The desert animals near the road are level 40 and up: stay on the road and keep moving.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.0, y=29.3},
  {t="F", seg=14, arg="Gadgetzan", text="Bera Stonehammer, the Alliance gryphon master on the north side of town. Nothing else to do here yet.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.0, y=29.3},
  {t="N", seg=14, arg="Walk back north to the Dustwallow road", text="Back through the flats and the canyon, up the Great Lift and north on the Barrens road. A side road branches off east into Dustwallow Marsh a little north of the lift. The first thing on it is the burnt-out Shady Rest Inn. The marsh animals are 35-38: pull one at a time, Voidwalker first, then Corruption, Curse of Agony and Immolate. The spiders poison and a warlock cannot cure it: Drain Life during the fight, bandage and eat after it.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=29.7, y=47.6},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1284}, names={"Suspicious Hoofprints"}, text="The Suspicious Hoofprint, a mark on the ground in front of the inn ruins", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=29.7, y=47.6},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1253}, names={"The Black Shield"}, text="The Black Shield, hanging over the fireplace of the ruins", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=29.6, y=48.6},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1252}, names={"Lieutenant Paval Reethe"}, text="The Theramore Guard Badge, lying on the floor boards of the ruins", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=29.8, y=48.2},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1177}, names={"Hungry!"}, text="Mudcrush Durtfeet, an ogre standing by the road north-east of the inn, just south of Brackenwall Village. Brackenwall is a Horde ogre town: do not go further north than him. If he is hostile to you or you cannot reach him, skip his quest (this step, the murloc step and the hand-in).", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=35.1, y=38.3},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1218}, names={"Soothing Spices"}, text="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl at the Swamplight Manor, the lonely house in the north of the marsh. Follow the road east and turn north.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=55.4, y=26.3},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1218}, names={"Soothing Spices"}, text="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl. Hand him the 3 Soothing Spices. (No spices: skip this and the next step and come back on the loop out of Theramore.)", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=55.4, y=26.3},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1206}, names={"Jarl Needs Eyes"}, text="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=55.4, y=26.3},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1219}, names={"The Orc Report"}, text="The Loose Dirt mound behind Jarl's house. It gives you the Spy's Report.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=55.4, y=25.9},
  {t="C", seg=14, q={1177}, names={"Hungry!"}, text="Mirefin murlocs (35-38) on the north coast, straight north of Jarl's house, and on the small islands further north-east. About one in three drops a head; you need 8. They come in twos and threes and run when low: pull from the edge of a group with the Voidwalker on the first murloc and your DoTs on it, and Fear the second one only where no other group stands behind it. A runner brings friends: keep Corruption and Curse of Agony on every murloc so it dies on the run, and finish it with Shadow Bolt. Back off along the beach if a third joins (Sacrifice gives you the time).", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=56.8, y=15.6},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1222}, names={"Stinky's Escape"}, text="\"Stinky\" Ignatz, standing in the swamp west of the murloc beach", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=46.9, y=17.5},
  {t="C", seg=14, q={1222}, names={"Stinky's Escape"}, text="Escort: walk beside Stinky while he looks for his bogbean plant and kill whatever attacks him (swamp animals, 35-38). Stay close and send the Voidwalker at everything that attacks him (it holds the attackers; you cannot heal Stinky), then DoT it and Drain Life. Do not Fear here: a feared animal comes back with company. When he thanks you the quest is complete; the hand-in is in Theramore. If he dies, abandon the quest and take it again from him.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=46.9, y=17.5},
  {t="C", seg=14, q={1206}, names={"Jarl Needs Eyes"}, text="Darkmist Cavern, in the north-west corner of the marsh. Darkmist Spiders (35-36), Recluses (36-37) and Silkspinners (38-39) all drop the eyes; you need 20. Work inwards from the entrance, one spider at a time: Voidwalker first, DoTs, wand, and no Fear inside the cave (a feared spider brings the next ones). Their poison stacks and a warlock cannot cure it: Drain Life in the fight, bandage and eat between pulls, Health Funnel the Voidwalker when it gets low, and keep a Healthstone ready. Leave the rare Darkmist Widow (40) alone.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=32.8, y=22.2},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1177}, names={"Hungry!"}, text="Mudcrush Durtfeet, south of the cavern", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=35.1, y=38.3},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1206}, names={"Jarl Needs Eyes"}, text="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl. Do not take Jarl Needs a Blade: it wants a crafted sword.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=55.4, y=26.3},
  {t="F", seg=14, arg="Theramore", text="Follow the road south-east and across the long bridge to Theramore Isle. Baldruc, the gryphon master, is in the south-east of town.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=67.5, y=51.3},
  {t="S", seg=14, arg="Theramore", text="Innkeeper Janene, in the inn at the north end of town", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=66.6, y=45.2},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1222}, names={"Stinky's Escape"}, text="Morgan Stern, in the same inn", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=66.3, y=45.5},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1204}, names={"Mudrock Soup and Bugs"}, text="Morgan Stern: Mudrock Soup and Bugs (needs level 33). The turtles are on the coast north of Theramore: you pass it on the loop below", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=66.3, y=45.5},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1219}, names={"The Orc Report"}, text="A Theramore Lieutenant: the officers standing at the town gates", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=65.1, y=47.2},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1220}, names={"Captain Vimes"}, text="The same Theramore Lieutenant", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=65.1, y=47.2},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1220}, names={"Captain Vimes"}, text="Captain Garran Vimes, top floor of Foothold Citadel, the big barracks in the east of town", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=68.2, y=48.6},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1253}, names={"The Black Shield"}, text="Captain Garran Vimes", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=68.2, y=48.6},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1319}, names={"The Black Shield"}, text="Captain Garran Vimes", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=68.2, y=48.6},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1284}, names={"Suspicious Hoofprints"}, text="Captain Garran Vimes", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=68.2, y=48.6},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1302}, names={"James Hyal"}, text="Clerk Lendry, on the same floor of Foothold Citadel: James Hyal", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=67.9, y=48.2},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1252}, names={"Lieutenant Paval Reethe"}, text="Captain Garran Vimes", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=68.2, y=48.6},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1259}, names={"Lieutenant Paval Reethe"}, text="Captain Garran Vimes", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=68.2, y=48.6},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1259}, names={"Lieutenant Paval Reethe"}, text="Adjutant Tesoran, in the same room", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=68.0, y=48.1},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1285}, names={"Daelin's Men"}, text="Adjutant Tesoran", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=68.0, y=48.1},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1285}, names={"Daelin's Men"}, text="Captain Garran Vimes", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=68.2, y=48.6},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1286}, names={"The Deserters"}, text="Captain Garran Vimes", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=68.2, y=48.6},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1264}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Commander Samaul, in the same room", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=68.0, y=48.7},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1265}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Commander Samaul", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=68.0, y=48.7},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1319}, names={"The Black Shield"}, text="Caz Twosprocket, the gnome at the smithy in the west of town", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=64.8, y=50.4},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1320}, names={"The Black Shield"}, text="Caz Twosprocket", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=64.8, y=50.4},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1320}, names={"The Black Shield"}, text="Captain Garran Vimes, back up in the citadel", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=68.2, y=48.6},
  {t="C", seg=14, q={1265}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Sentry Point, the first guard tower on the road outside Theramore, just past the bridge. Walk up to it until the quest says it is explored.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=59.9, y=40.9},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1265}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Archmage Tervosh, in Lady Jaina Proudmoore's tower in the middle of Theramore", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=66.4, y=49.3},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1266}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Archmage Tervosh", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=66.4, y=49.3},
  {t="C", seg=14, q={1204}, names={"Mudrock Soup and Bugs"}, text="8 Forked Mudrock Tongues. On the way north leave the road to the east: Mudrock Spikeshells and Tortoises (36-38) walk the beach and the shallows of the north-east coast. Only about one in four has a forked tongue, so this is 30 or more kills: it is the grind of this segment, with a quest reward on top. They hit slowly and hard: let the Voidwalker take the hits (Health Funnel when it gets low), Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate and the wand, one turtle at a time; Life Tap and Drain Life keep the breaks short. Drain Soul a kill now and then to keep 3-5 Soul Shards. Had enough? Press Skip here and on the hand-in", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=61.1, y=18.4},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1266}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Private Hendel, at the tents beside the road in the north of the marsh, west of Jarl's house. (Still owe Jarl his spices and eyes? Do his two quests now, the cavern is west of here.)", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=45.2, y=24.7},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1324}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Private Hendel", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=45.2, y=24.7},
  {t="C", seg=14, q={1324}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Hendel (35) and the two guards beside him turn hostile. Start at full health and mana with a Healthstone in your bags, send the Voidwalker at Hendel and fight Hendel himself, not the guards: Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate, then Drain Life. Fear one guard if they hurt too much, and use Sacrifice when it goes wrong. He gives up when he is nearly dead. If Archmage Tervosh appears next to him afterwards, hand the quest in to him right there.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=45.2, y=24.7},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1286}, names={"The Deserters"}, text="Balos Jacken at the Lost Point tower, south-east of the Shady Rest Inn. Take the road back west and turn south. Attack him (38): the deserters around him join in, so keep hitting Jacken only: Voidwalker on him, Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate, then Drain Life; Fear a deserter that is on you. He surrenders when he is nearly dead and then talks to you. Be at full health and mana before you start, with a Healthstone in your bags and your Soulstone on yourself.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=36.1, y=54.3},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1287}, names={"The Deserters"}, text="Balos Jacken", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=36.1, y=54.3},
  {t="H", seg=14, arg="Theramore", text="Hearthstone"},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1287}, names={"The Deserters"}, text="Captain Garran Vimes. If he offers Vimes's Report (a short new quest to Lady Jaina, 290 XP), take it and hand it in at the tower in a moment.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=68.2, y=48.6},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1204}, names={"Mudrock Soup and Bugs"}, text="Morgan Stern, in the inn. Do not take the spider follow-up: it is not on this route", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=66.3, y=45.5},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1324}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Archmage Tervosh in Jaina's tower (unless you already handed it in at the tents)", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=66.4, y=49.3},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1267}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Archmage Tervosh", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=66.4, y=49.3},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1267}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Lady Jaina Proudmoore, standing beside him", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=66.3, y=49.0},
  {t="N", seg=14, arg="Take the boat from Theramore to Menethil Harbor", text="The dock is at the south-east edge of town. You keep for later: 1106 (Martek, Badlands), 5762 (Hemet Nesingwary, Stranglethorn), 1111 and 1178 (Ratchet), 525 (Southshore), 563 (Stormwind), 1457 and 1467 (Ironforge). Your hearthstone stays in Theramore."},
  {t="FLY", seg=15, arg="Ironforge", text="You arrive on the Menethil Harbor dock. Shellei Brondir, the gryphon master, is just inside the town.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=9.5, y=59.7},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={1467}, names={"Reagents for Reclaimers Inc."}, text="Roetten Stonehammer, at Reclaimers Inc. in the Hall of Explorers", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=70.0, y=21.3},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={1457}, names={"The Karnitol Shipwreck"}, text="Roetten Stonehammer", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=70.0, y=21.3},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={707}, names={"Ironband Wants You!"}, text="Prospector Stormpike, in the library at the back of the Hall of Explorers. Keep it: Prospector Ironband in Loch Modan is the first stop of the next segment.", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=74.6, y=11.7},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=15, text="Briarthorn, the warlock trainer in the Forlorn Cavern in the north of the city: learn everything he offers at level 36. The demon trainer beside him sells the Voidwalker's new spell books. Make a fresh Healthstone and stock up on Soul Shards on the first kills of the swamp.", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=50.4, y=5.7},
  {t="N", seg=15, arg="Optional, not routed: the level 35 warlock quest", text="From level 35 Menara Voidrender in Ratchet (The Barrens) offers a warlock orb quest (the robe quest came at 31). It needs trips on two continents, so this guide does not route it: take it on your own when you are in Ratchet if you want the reward; the logger records what you take."},
  {t="N", seg=15, arg="Take the Deeprun Tram from Tinker Town to Stormwind", text="The tram station is at the back of Tinker Town. You come out in Stormwind's Dwarven District."},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={563}, names={"Reassignment"}, text="Major Samuelson, in Stormwind Keep", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=75.8, y=36.7},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={2928}, names={"Gyrodrillmatic Excavationators"}, zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=55.5, y=12.5, dg=7},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={212}, names={"A Meal Served Cold"}, text="Angus Stern, the cook in the Blue Recluse tavern in the Mage Quarter. The haunch comes from a Cold Eye Basilisk in Stranglethorn, later in this segment; the hand-in waits for a later Stormwind visit.", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=51.8, y=93.6},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={92489}, names={"Power Overwhelming"}, zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=48.8, y=88.1, dg=6},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={92456}, names={"A Green Sample"}, zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=31.5, y=63.0, dg=6},
  {t="FLY", seg=15, arg="Darkshire", text="Dungar Longdrink, the gryphon master in the Trade District", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=71.0, y=72.5},
  {t="N", seg=15, arg="Walk east through Deadwind Pass into the Swamp of Sorrows", text="Leave Darkshire on the road east. It winds through Deadwind Pass (stay on the road, the mobs beside it are far above you) and comes out in the swamp. Watcher Biggs camps just south of the road, right after the zone border. Stonard, further east, is a Horde town: stay away from it.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=26.7, y=59.8},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={1396}, names={"Encroaching Wildlife"}, text="Watcher Biggs", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=26.7, y=59.8},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={93176}, names={"My Little Friends"}, text="Amaryllis Webb, a short way north-west of Biggs. New Forever quest: she gives you an Entomology Starter Kit. Read the notes in the kit, they say how to catch the three bugs (Arbor Tarantula, Hay Weevil, Flesh Picker). Where the bugs are is not in my data.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=25.0, y=54.2},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={93585}, names={"This Light of Mine"}, text="Father Tuttle, at the bridge on the road west of Biggs. New Forever escort quest.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=22.0, y=50.6},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={93585}, names={"This Light of Mine"}, text="Escort Father Tuttle north to the Harborage, the draenei village on the island in the north-west of the swamp. Lost Ones (34-37) attack on the way: stay beside him and send the Voidwalker at whatever attacks him (it holds the attackers; you cannot heal him). A warlock has no interrupt: kill the casters first with Corruption, Curse of Agony and Immolate, or put Curse of Tongues on one and Fear a second. If he dies, abandon the quest and take it again at the bridge.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=26.0, y=31.4},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={93585}, names={"This Light of Mine"}, text="At the Harborage. The data does not say who takes the hand-in: it may complete by itself on arrival, otherwise look for the NPC with the yellow question mark (most likely Magtoor or Father Tuttle himself).", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=26.0, y=31.4},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={1389}, names={"Draenethyst Crystals"}, text="Magtoor, the draenei leader at the Harborage", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=26.0, y=31.4},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={1396}, names={"Encroaching Wildlife"}, text="The animals between the Harborage and Biggs' camp: 8 Young Sawtooth Crocolisks (35-36, in and beside the water), 10 Sorrow Spinners (spiders, 36-37) and 10 Swamp Jaguars (36-37). Use the kit from Amaryllis on any quest bug you see on the way. Voidwalker first, then Corruption, Curse of Agony and the wand; Drain Soul a kill now and then to keep 3-5 Soul Shards. The spiders poison and a warlock cannot cure it: Drain Life, bandage and eat.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=32.0, y=44.0},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={1396}, names={"Encroaching Wildlife"}, text="Watcher Biggs", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=26.7, y=59.8},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={1421}, names={"The Lost Caravan"}, text="Watcher Biggs", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=26.7, y=59.8},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={1392}, names={"Noboru the Cudgel"}, text="Noboru the Cudgel (39), a Lost One who walks the swamp north of the road, about half way to the east end, with two followers. Start at full health and mana with a Healthstone in your bags and your Soulstone on yourself: Voidwalker on one follower, Fear the other, kill the followers first, then him with Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate and Drain Life (Sacrifice and walk away early if it goes badly), and right-click the Noboru's Cudgel he drops to start the quest. Not there? Do the Fallow Sanctuary first and look again on the way back.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=55.7, y=34.4},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={1389,1421}, names={"Draenethyst Crystals","The Lost Caravan"}, text="The Fallow Sanctuary, the Lost One village in the north-east. The Draenethyst Crystals are blue crystals standing among the huts and campfires: collect 6. The Caravan Chest with the Wizards' Reagents is at the back of the village (64.5, 18.3). Lost Ones here are 36-38 and stand close together: pull from range with the Voidwalker, one at a time, and do not Fear inside the village (a feared Lost One runs into the next hut and brings it back). Curse of Tongues on the casters. Avoid the Lost One Chieftain (39, rare).", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=62.0, y=22.0},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={1393}, names={"Galen's Escape"}, text="Galen Goodward, in the cage right beside the Caravan Chest. Clear the Lost Ones around the cage before you talk to him.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=65.5, y=18.2},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={1393}, names={"Galen's Escape"}, text="Escort Galen out of the village. Walk ahead of him with the Voidwalker and let it take what he meets; DoT each attacker and Drain Life. When he says goodbye the escort part is done.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=65.5, y=18.2},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={1393}, names={"Galen's Escape"}, text="Galen's Strongbox, in his little camp in the middle of the swamp north of Stonard (stay north of the Horde town)", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=47.8, y=39.8},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={1389}, names={"Draenethyst Crystals"}, text="Magtoor at the Harborage", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=26.0, y=31.4},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={1392}, names={"Noboru the Cudgel"}, text="Magtoor (only if Noboru dropped the cudgel)", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=26.0, y=31.4},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={1421}, names={"The Lost Caravan"}, text="Watcher Biggs. Do not take the follow-up, Driftwood: the route does it on a later visit.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=26.7, y=59.8},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={93176}, names={"My Little Friends"}, text="Amaryllis Webb, if you caught all three bugs. If the kit's notes send you to places outside the swamp, press Skip here and abandon the quest when you leave.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=25.0, y=54.2},
  {t="N", seg=15, arg="Walk back to Duskwood and south into Stranglethorn Vale", text="Back west through Deadwind Pass to Darkshire, then the road south-west out of Duskwood into the jungle. The Rebel Camp is on the left of the road right after the border.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=38.0, y=3.3},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={203}, names={"The Second Rebellion"}, text="Sergeant Yohwa at the Rebel Camp", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=38.0, y=3.3},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={204}, names={"Bad Medicine"}, text="Sergeant Yohwa", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=38.0, y=3.3},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={210}, names={"Krazek's Cookery"}, text="Corporal Kaleb. A broken pot for Krazek in Booty Bay.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=37.7, y=3.3},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={215}, names={"Jungle Secrets"}, text="Private Thorsen. He walks out of the camp on a patrol and gets ambushed by two Kurzen soldiers on the path: follow him, kill the two attackers, then he offers the quest. If he is not in camp, wait a few minutes for him to come back.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=38.0, y=3.4},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={215}, names={"Jungle Secrets"}, text="Lieutenant Doren at the Rebel Camp", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=38.0, y=3.0},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={200}, names={"Bookie Herod"}, text="Lieutenant Doren", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=38.0, y=3.0},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={5762}, names={"Hemet Nesingwary"}, text="Hemet Nesingwary at Nesingwary's Expedition, the hunters' camp a short walk south-west of the Rebel Camp", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.7, y=10.8},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={583}, names={"Welcome to the Jungle"}, text="Barnil Stonepot, at the same camp", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.7, y=10.5},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={583}, names={"Welcome to the Jungle"}, text="Hemet Nesingwary", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.7, y=10.8},
