  {t="A", seg=15, q={196}, names={"Raptor Mastery"}, text="Hemet Nesingwary. Jungle Stalkers are level 40-41: they come on the last loop.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.7, y=10.8},
  {t="N", seg=15, arg="Walk the road south to Booty Bay", text="A long walk: stay on the road all the way to the south tip and through the shark-jaw tunnel. Grom'gol, on the west coast half way down, is a Horde base: do not leave the road there.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.5, y=77.8},
  {t="F", seg=15, arg="Booty Bay", text="Gyll, the gryphon master on the upper level at the east end of town", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.5, y=77.8},
  {t="S", seg=15, arg="Booty Bay", text="Innkeeper Skindle, in the Salty Sailor Tavern", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.0, y=77.3},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={98463}, names={"Talk of the Town"}, text="Nixxrax Fillamug, the barkeep in the same tavern: Talk of the Town", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.0, y=77.2},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={95789}, names={"Shady Saltseers"}, text="Krazek in Booty Bay. 10 Voodoo-Infused Artifacts from the Saltseer pirates inside. He should also have The Saltseer Captain.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.0, y=77.2, dg=14},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={210}, names={"Krazek's Cookery"}, text="Krazek, upstairs in the building next to the inn. Do NOT take Favor for Krazek: its Lesser Bloodstone Ore only comes from Drywhisker Gorge in the Arathi Highlands.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.9, y=77.2},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={201}, names={"Investigate the Camp"}, text="Krazek", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.9, y=77.2},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={616}, names={"The Haunted Isle"}, text="Krazek", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.9, y=77.2},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={616}, names={"The Haunted Isle"}, text="Baron Revilgaz, on the top balcony of the same building", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.2, y=76.9},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={578}, names={"The Stone of the Tides"}, text="Baron Revilgaz", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.2, y=76.9},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={189}, names={"Bloodscalp Ears"}, text="Kebok, next to the Baron", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.0, y=77.1},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={213}, names={"Hostile Takeover"}, text="Kebok", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.0, y=77.1},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={605}, names={"Singing Blue Shards"}, text="Crank Fizzlebub, in the tavern", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.1, y=77.2},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={606}, names={"Scaring Shaky"}, text="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley, in a house on the middle level", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.8, y=77.1},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={575}, names={"Supply and Demand"}, text="Drizzlik, in the leather shop at the east end", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.3, y=77.6},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={595}, names={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers"}, text="First Mate Crazz, on the dock by the tailor's", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.1, y=76.2},
  {t="N", seg=15, arg="Optional dungeon: The Drowned City, levels 35-40", text="New Forever dungeon, not checked in game yet. It is on Gillijim's Isle, in the sea south-west of Stranglethorn Vale; the portal is in a cave called Sunken Hollow, and no boat or flight path was known to go there. Archmage Timear in Dalaran (Alterac Mountains 15.4, 74.0) gives Ancient Gurubashi Secrets. Take whatever else is offered for it: the addon logs it so these steps can be filled in. Quests you picked up for it: Shady Saltseers.", dg=14, run=true},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={595}, names={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers"}, text="The Bloodsail Correspondence: a scroll on a barrel in the small pirate camp on the beach north of Booty Bay. Go back out through the tunnel and down to the shore on the west side. The Bloodsail Raiders and Mages there are 39-41: pull the ones at the camp singly with the Voidwalker, kill the Mages first (Curse of Tongues on them, or Fear a Mage while you kill a Raider), and leave along the beach if more come than you can take (Sacrifice gives you the time).", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.3, y=69.5},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={597}, names={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers"}, text="The Bloodsail Correspondence", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.3, y=69.5},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={597}, names={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers"}, text="First Mate Crazz", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.1, y=76.2},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={599}, names={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers"}, text="First Mate Crazz", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.1, y=76.2},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={599}, names={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers"}, text="Fleet Master Seahorn, on the balcony beside the Baron. Do not take the next part (604) yet.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.2, y=77.0},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={212}, names={"A Meal Served Cold"}, text="Walk the road north. Cold Eye Basilisks (39-40) live on the west side of the road, on the shore south of Grom'gol. Kill them until a Chilled Basilisk Haunch drops; they also drop Singing Crystal Shards for Crank. They are 2-3 levels above you, so some spells are resisted: one at a time, at full health and mana before each pull, Voidwalker first and give it a few seconds, then Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate and Drain Life; Health Funnel the Voidwalker when it gets low. Keep the haunch (Stormwind, a later segment).", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.6, y=40.5},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={578}, names={"The Stone of the Tides"}, text="The haunted island lies off the WEST coast, north-west of Grom'gol (keep well away from the base). Swim out to it and walk onto the island until the quest completes. The Lesser Water Elementals here matter later, not now.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=20.8, y=23.2},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={207}, obj={2}, names={"Kurzen's Mystery"}, text="Second tablet (Gri'lek the Wanderer): under water in the Vile Reef, between the island and the shore. The Saltscale murlocs around it are elite-flagged (35-37): cast Unending Breath, dive straight down to the tablet, click it and swim off.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=24.8, y=23.0},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={189}, names={"Bloodscalp Ears"}, text="Ruins of Zul'Kunda, north along the coast: every Bloodscalp troll (34-37) can drop an ear, you need 15. Pull from the outer edge; kill the Mystics and Witch Doctors first (they heal and a warlock has no interrupt: Curse of Tongues on them, or Fear the healer while you kill the other troll, but only at the outer edge, never towards the ruins). Runners bring friends: keep Corruption and Curse of Agony on every troll so it dies on the run, and finish it with Shadow Bolt.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=24.0, y=11.0},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={207,207}, obj={3,4}, names={"Kurzen's Mystery","Kurzen's Mystery"}, text="Third and fourth tablet, both in Zul'Kunda: Fall of Gurubashi (22.9, 12.0) and The Emperor's Tomb (24.7, 8.9), stone tablets standing among the ruins", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=23.0, y=12.0},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={207}, obj={1}, names={"Kurzen's Mystery"}, text="First tablet (Moon Over the Vale): in the Bal'lal Ruins on the coast south-east of Zul'Kunda", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=29.5, y=19.1},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={605}, names={"Singing Blue Shards"}, text="Still short of 10 Singing Crystal Shards? Crystal Spine Basilisks (34-35) between the Tkashi Ruins and Nesingwary's camp drop them too. The Bloodscalp trolls at the Tkashi Ruins (32, 17) fill up the ears.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.0, y=13.4, path={{33.4,12.1}}},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={201}, names={"Investigate the Camp"}, text="Walk into Nesingwary's Expedition: that is the hunters' camp Krazek wants found", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.7, y=11.0},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={575}, names={"Supply and Demand"}, text="2 Large River Crocolisk Skins: River Crocolisks (30-31) in the river just east of the camp", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=37.3, y=10.9},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={207}, names={"Kurzen's Mystery"}, text="Brother Nimetz at the Rebel Camp", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=37.8, y=3.6},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={205}, names={"Troll Witchery"}, text="Brother Nimetz. Skullsplitter trolls are 39-42: the fetishes come on the last loop, and only if it goes well.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=37.8, y=3.6},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={213}, names={"Hostile Takeover"}, text="8 Tumbled Crystals from Venture Co. Geologists (34-36) at the Venture Co. camp on the east shore of Lake Nazferiti, south of Kurzen's Compound", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=42.9, y=19.1},
  {t="H", seg=15, arg="Booty Bay", text="Hearthstone"},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={201}, names={"Investigate the Camp"}, text="Krazek", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.9, y=77.2},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={578}, names={"The Stone of the Tides"}, text="Baron Revilgaz", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.2, y=76.9},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={601}, names={"Water Elementals"}, text="Baron Revilgaz", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.2, y=76.9},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={189}, names={"Bloodscalp Ears"}, text="Kebok", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.0, y=77.1},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={209}, names={"Skullsplitter Tusks"}, text="Kebok. Skullsplitter Tusks: keep it, it is done on a later Stranglethorn trip.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.0, y=77.1},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={213}, names={"Hostile Takeover"}, text="Kebok", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.0, y=77.1},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={605}, names={"Singing Blue Shards"}, text="Crank Fizzlebub", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.1, y=77.2},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={600}, names={"Venture Company Mining"}, text="Crank Fizzlebub", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.1, y=77.2},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={575}, names={"Supply and Demand"}, text="Drizzlik", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.3, y=77.6},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={577}, names={"Some Assembly Required"}, text="Drizzlik", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.3, y=77.6},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={606}, names={"Scaring Shaky"}, text="5 Mistvale Giblets from Elder Mistvale Gorillas (40-41) in Mistvale Valley, east of the road a short way north of Booty Bay. They are above you and hit hard: one at a time, at full health and mana, Voidwalker first with Health Funnel on it when it gets low, then Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate and Drain Life. Keep a Healthstone ready, and use Sacrifice and walk away when a fight goes badly. If they are too much, abandon Scaring Shaky and skip the next three steps.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.9, y=64.6},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={606}, names={"Scaring Shaky"}, text="\"Shaky\" Phillipe, on the dock at the north end of Booty Bay", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.9, y=73.6},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={607}, names={"Return to MacKinley"}, text="\"Shaky\" Phillipe", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.9, y=73.6},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={607}, names={"Return to MacKinley"}, text="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.8, y=77.1},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={600}, names={"Venture Company Mining"}, text="Walk north again. The Crystalvein Mine is east of the road, about level with Grom'gol. Venture Co. Strip Miners and Tinkerers (40-41) drop the Singing Blue Crystals; you need 10. Stay near the mine entrance and pull singly with the Voidwalker; Fear a second miner away from the mine, not into it. The Foreman and Surveyors inside are 42. Too hard at your level? Abandon the quest and skip its hand-in.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=41.6, y=43.6},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={196}, names={"Raptor Mastery"}, text="10 Jungle Stalkers (40-41): the raptors west of the road, around the Gurubashi Arena. Same rule: one at a time, Voidwalker first, DoTs and Drain Life, and drop the quest rather than die for it.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.9, y=44.9, path={{37.4,38.5},{32.8,39.7}}},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={205}, names={"Troll Witchery"}, text="4 Skullsplitter Fetishes from Skullsplitter Mystics (39-40) in the troll ruins east of the road (Ruins of Zul'Mamwe and around). The ruins are crowded: pick Mystics that stand at the edge, put Curse of Tongues on them (a warlock has no interrupt) and do not Fear here: a feared troll brings the ruins back with it. No luck after a fair try? Abandon Troll Witchery and skip its hand-in.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=45.6, y=36.6, path={{32.8,39.7},{35.6,39.1},{37.2,35.2},{39.6,33.4},{44.0,33.1}}},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={192}, names={"Panther Mastery"}, text="10 Shadowmaw Panthers (37-38): they prowl in stealth all over the jungle east of the road, from here north", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=42.5, y=32.4},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={577}, names={"Some Assembly Required"}, text="5 Snapjaw Crocolisk Skins: Snapjaw Crocolisks (35-36) in the river that runs south from Lake Nazferiti", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=40.3, y=23.5},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={601}, names={"Water Elementals"}, text="6 Water Elemental Bracers from the Lesser Water Elementals (36-37) on the haunted island off the west coast. Your shadow and fire spells all work on them. If two come at once, Banish one (an elemental) and kill the other, with the Voidwalker on it.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=20.9, y=23.3},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={192}, names={"Panther Mastery"}, text="Sir S. J. Erlgadin at Nesingwary's Expedition. Stop here: the next step is elite.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.5, y=10.6},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={196}, names={"Raptor Mastery"}, text="Hemet Nesingwary. Stop here too (Tethis is elite).", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.7, y=10.8},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={205}, names={"Troll Witchery"}, text="Brother Nimetz at the Rebel Camp", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=37.8, y=3.6},
  {t="H", seg=15, arg="Booty Bay", text="Hearthstone: you last used it at the end of loop 1, so it is ready. If it is not, walk the road south to Booty Bay again"},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={601}, names={"Water Elementals"}, text="Baron Revilgaz. Do not take the follow-up: it goes to Dalaran.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.2, y=76.9},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={577}, names={"Some Assembly Required"}, text="Drizzlik. Do not take the next one (elite).", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.3, y=77.6},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={600}, names={"Venture Company Mining"}, text="Crank Fizzlebub", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.1, y=77.2},
  {t="FLY", seg=15, arg="Ironforge", text="Gyll, the Booty Bay gryphon master. You keep 209 (Kebok), 212 (the haunch for Angus Stern), 707 (Prospector Ironband), 525 (Southshore), 1106 (Martek), 1111 and 1178 (Ratchet). Your hearthstone stays in Booty Bay until Southshore.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.5, y=77.8},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=16, text="Briarthorn, the warlock trainer in the Forlorn Cavern in the north of the city: learn everything he offers at level 38. The demon trainer beside him sells the Voidwalker's new spell books. Make a fresh Healthstone before you leave.", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=50.4, y=5.7},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={1050}, names={"Mythology of the Titans"}, text="Librarian Mae Paledust in the Hall of Explorers. Mythology of the Titans is in the Library wing.", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=75.0, y=12.5, dg=8},
  {t="FLY", seg=16, arg="Thelsamar", text="Gryth Thurden, the Ironforge gryphon master", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=55.5, y=47.7},
  {t="N", seg=16, arg="Optional dungeon: Scarlet Monastery, levels 30-46", text="The monastery is in the north-east corner of Tirisfal Glades, deep in Horde land: from Southshore ride north through Alterac and the Western Plaguelands, or west along the north shore of Lordamere Lake. Four wings, each its own run: Graveyard (30-38), Library (33-41), Armory (36-44) and Cathedral (38-46). Raleigh the Devout in Southshore gives In the Name of the Light (the four wing bosses), but only after a letter from Brother Anton at Nijel's Point in Desolace. Magus Olvek (Alterac Mountains 9.8, 63.0, by Dalaran) gives Past Due, a book from the monastery. Quests you picked up for it: Mythology of the Titans.", zone="Tirisfal Glades", map=1420, x=82.6, y=33.8, dg=8, run=true},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1050}, names={"Mythology of the Titans"}, zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=75.0, y=12.5, dg=8},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={2500}, names={"Badlands Reagent Run"}, text="Ghak Healtouch, the alchemist in Thelsamar", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=37.1, y=49.4},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={707}, names={"Ironband Wants You!"}, text="Prospector Ironband, at Ironband's Excavation Site in the south-east of Loch Modan", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=65.9, y=65.6},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={738}, names={"Find Agmond"}, text="Prospector Ironband", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=65.9, y=65.6},
  {t="N", seg=16, arg="Walk south into the Badlands", text="The pass leaves Loch Modan at its south end (Classic geography, not re-checked) and comes out in the north of the Badlands. Head south to the two dwarves camped in the open south of Hammertoe's Dig Site. On the way, start on Ghak's list: Crag Coyotes (35-36) for fangs and Starving Buzzards (35-37) for gizzards.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=53.8, y=43.3},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={718}, names={"Mirages"}, text="Sigrun Ironhew", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=53.8, y=43.3},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={719}, names={"A Dwarf and His Tools"}, text="Prospector Ryedol, next to him", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=53.4, y=43.4},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={719}, names={"A Dwarf and His Tools"}, text="Ryedol's Lucky Pick drops from the Shadowforge dwarves (Tunnelers and Darkweavers, 35-37) at Hammertoe's Dig Site, a short way north. Voidwalker first on every pull. The Darkweavers are casters and a warlock has no interrupt: kill them first with Curse of Tongues on them, or Fear the Darkweaver while you kill the Tunneler beside it.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=53.4, y=32.5},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={718}, names={"Mirages"}, text="The Supply Crate stands in Camp Kosh, the ogre camp in the north-east. The Dustbelcher Warriors and Mystics there are 36-37: clear your way to the crate with the Voidwalker in front (Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate, wand; Fear a second ogre away from the camp, not into it) and loot it.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=66.9, y=23.5, path={{55.2,28.9},{60.0,29.2},{62.2,31.9},{64.0,31.9},{64.4,27.4}}},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={718}, names={"Mirages"}, text="Sigrun Ironhew", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=53.8, y=43.3, path={{64.4,27.4},{64.2,37.9},{59.0,44.2}}},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={733}, names={"Scrounging"}, text="Sigrun Ironhew. Scrap Metal drops from every Dustbelcher ogre: you meet them in the south and south-west on the round below.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=53.8, y=43.3},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={719}, names={"A Dwarf and His Tools"}, text="Prospector Ryedol", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=53.4, y=43.4},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1106}, names={"Martek the Exiled"}, text="Martek the Exiled, at the small racing camp in the Valley of Fangs, south-west of the dwarves", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=42.2, y=52.7},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={1108}, names={"Indurium"}, text="Martek the Exiled", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=42.2, y=52.7},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={703}, names={"Barbecued Buzzard Wings"}, text="Rigglefuzz, the goblin next to Martek", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=42.4, y=52.9},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={710}, names={"Study of the Elements: Rock"}, text="Lotwil Veriatus, at his camp in the west of the Badlands. Kargath, further west, is a Horde outpost: stay clear of it.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=25.9, y=44.9},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={710}, names={"Study of the Elements: Rock"}, text="10 Small Stone Shards from the Lesser Rock Elementals (37-39) on the slopes west of Lotwil's camp. Rock Elemental Shards for Ghak drop from the same elementals. Elementals can be Banished: if two come at once, Banish one and kill the other. Drain Soul a kill now and then to keep 3-5 Soul Shards.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=18.8, y=43.0},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={710}, names={"Study of the Elements: Rock"}, text="Lotwil Veriatus", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=25.9, y=44.9},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={711}, names={"Study of the Elements: Rock"}, text="Lotwil Veriatus", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=25.9, y=44.9},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={711}, names={"Study of the Elements: Rock"}, text="3 Large Stone Slabs from Rock Elementals (39-40), which roam the plain south and south-east of Lotwil. Giant Buzzards (39-41) and Elder Crag Coyotes (38-40) share the area: wings, gizzards and fangs.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=30.0, y=62.0},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={711}, names={"Study of the Elements: Rock"}, text="Lotwil Veriatus", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=25.9, y=44.9},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={712}, names={"Study of the Elements: Rock"}, text="Lotwil Veriatus", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=25.9, y=44.9},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={712}, names={"Study of the Elements: Rock"}, text="5 Bracers of Rock Binding from Greater Rock Elementals (42-44) in the far south-west corner. They are 3-4 levels above you, so spells are often resisted and they hit hard: one at a time, full health and mana before each pull, a Healthstone in your bags and your Soulstone on yourself. Send the Voidwalker and give it a few seconds, then Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate and Drain Life; Health Funnel the Voidwalker when it gets low. Banish a second elemental that joins, and use Sacrifice and walk away early when a fight goes badly. The Dustbelcher ogres camped just north of them (40-43) drop Scrap Metal. If the elementals are too much, abandon this part and skip its hand-in.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=8.3, y=82.8},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={712}, names={"Study of the Elements: Rock"}, text="Lotwil Veriatus", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=25.9, y=44.9},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={738}, names={"Find Agmond"}, text="The Battered Dwarven Skeleton at Agmond's End, in the south of the Badlands. Walk east along the south side; Dustbelcher Ogres and Brutes (38-40) on the way drop Scrap Metal.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=50.9, y=62.4},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={739}, names={"Murdaloc"}, text="The Battered Dwarven Skeleton", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=50.9, y=62.4},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={739,1108}, names={"Murdaloc","Indurium"}, text="The trogg camp right behind the skeleton: kill 12 Stonevault Bonesnappers (39-40) and Murdaloc (42), who walks among them. Bonesnappers and Stonevault Shamans drop the 10 Indurium Flakes. Clear the troggs near Murdaloc first, then fight him alone at full health and mana: Voidwalker on him, Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate, Drain Life, and Health Funnel when the Voidwalker gets low. The Stonevault spellcasters among them heal and a warlock has no interrupt: kill them first with Curse of Tongues on them, or Fear the healer while you kill the trogg beside it.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=50.4, y=68.3},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={709}, names={"Solution to Doom"}, text="Theldurin the Lost. The Tablet of Ryun'eh is in the tunnels before the dungeon portal.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=51.4, y=76.9, dg=9},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={703,2500}, names={"Barbecued Buzzard Wings","Badlands Reagent Run"}, text="Finish the animal parts around Agmond's End: 4 Buzzard Wings and 5 Buzzard Gizzards (Buzzards, 37-39), 10 Crag Coyote Fangs (Feral Crag Coyotes, 37-38) and 5 Rock Elemental Shards (any rock elemental).", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=54.5, y=62.9},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1108}, names={"Indurium"}, text="Martek the Exiled", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=42.2, y=52.7},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={1137}, names={"News for Fizzle"}, text="Martek the Exiled. News for Fizzle at the Mirage Raceway: keep it for the next segment.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=42.2, y=52.7},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={703}, names={"Barbecued Buzzard Wings"}, text="Rigglefuzz", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=42.4, y=52.9},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={2418}, names={"Power Stones"}, text="Rigglefuzz. Power Stones drop from the Shadowforge dwarves in and around Uldaman.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=42.4, y=52.9, dg=9},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={733}, names={"Scrounging"}, text="Still short of 7 Scrap Metal? The Dustbelcher Warriors and Mystics at Camp Kosh in the north-east are the easy source. Otherwise go straight to Sigrun.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=66.2, y=23.3},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={733}, names={"Scrounging"}, text="Sigrun Ironhew", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=53.8, y=43.3, path={{66.4,24.7},{64.4,27.4},{64.2,37.9},{59.0,44.2}}},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={739}, names={"Murdaloc"}, text="Prospector Ironband: back north over the pass into Loch Modan. Do not take the follow-up (Uldaman).", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=65.9, y=65.6},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={2500}, names={"Badlands Reagent Run"}, text="Ghak Healtouch in Thelsamar", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=37.1, y=49.4},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={17}, names={"Uldaman Reagent Run"}, text="Ghak Healtouch in Thelsamar, after his Badlands Reagent Run. 12 Magenta Fungus Caps from inside.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=37.1, y=49.4, dg=9},
  {t="FLY", seg=16, arg="Ironforge", text="Thorgrum Borrelson in Thelsamar. In Ironforge fly straight on to Southshore.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=33.9, y=51.0},
  {t="FLY", seg=16, arg="Southshore", text="Gryth Thurden", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=55.5, y=47.7},
  {t="S", seg=16, arg="Southshore", text="Innkeeper Anderson", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=51.2, y=58.9},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={525}, names={"Further Mysteries"}, text="Magistrate Henry Maleb, in the town hall", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=48.1, y=59.1},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={537}, names={"Dark Council"}, text="Magistrate Henry Maleb", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=48.1, y=59.1},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={512}, names={"Noble Deaths"}, text="Magistrate Henry Maleb", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=48.1, y=59.1},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={500}, names={"Crushridge Bounty"}, text="Marshal Redpath, outside by the barracks", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=49.5, y=58.7},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={659}, names={"Hints of a New Plague?"}, text="Phin Odelic, in the inn building", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=50.3, y=59.0},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={512}, names={"Noble Deaths"}, text="Walk north into the Alterac Mountains. Syndicate Spies and Wizards (34-36) at Sofera's Naze and Corrahn's Dagger, the two camps in the south-east, drop Alterac Signet Rings; you need 7. Voidwalker first. Kill the Wizards first, with Curse of Tongues on them (a warlock has no interrupt), or Fear the Wizard while you kill the Spy; never Fear towards the tents.", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=60.9, y=44.1},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={537}, obj={1}, names={"Dark Council"}, text="4 Argus Shadow Mages (35-36): around Strahnbrad, the ruined town north of the camps. The Syndicate Sentries and Saboteurs there drop rings too.", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=57.9, y=35.1},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={537}, names={"Dark Council"}, text="Nagaz (40) is in the house at Dandred's Fold, in the north-west of the zone. Follow the road west and north around the ruined city. Syndicate Assassins and Enforcers (38-40) guard the farm: pull them away from the house one at a time with the Voidwalker, then fight Nagaz alone at full health and mana; he casts shadow spells and a warlock has no interrupt: put Curse of Tongues on him to slow them, let the Voidwalker hold him, and Drain Life to stay up. Take his head.", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=39.2, y=14.3, path={{58.8,32.5},{57.8,31.0},{55.6,31.0},{47.2,19.6},{42.8,17.8}}},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={500}, names={"Crushridge Bounty"}, text="9 Dirty Knucklebones from Crushridge Ogres and Brutes (34-36) in the outer parts of the Ruins of Alterac, on the way back south. Stay out of the city centre and the western slope: those ogres are elite.", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=50.0, y=45.0},
  {t="H", seg=16, arg="Southshore", text="Hearthstone"},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={500}, names={"Crushridge Bounty"}, text="Marshal Redpath. Do not take Crushridge Warmongers (elite).", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=49.5, y=58.7},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={512}, names={"Noble Deaths"}, text="Magistrate Henry Maleb", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=48.1, y=59.1},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={537}, names={"Dark Council"}, text="Magistrate Henry Maleb", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=48.1, y=59.1},
  {t="N", seg=16, arg="Walk east into the Arathi Highlands", text="Take the road east out of Hillsbrad, through the gap in Thoradin's Wall, and on to Refuge Pointe in the middle of Arathi.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=46.2, y=47.8},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={691}, names={"Worth Its Weight in Gold"}, text="Apprentice Kryten at Refuge Pointe", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=46.2, y=47.8},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={659}, names={"Hints of a New Plague?"}, text="Quae, on the hill above the Go'Shek Farm, east of Refuge Pointe. She and Kinelory stand there in stealth-coloured gear, easy to miss.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=60.2, y=53.9},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={658}, names={"Hints of a New Plague?"}, text="Quae", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=60.2, y=53.9},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={658}, names={"Hints of a New Plague?"}, text="The Forsaken Courier walks the road between Go'Shek Farm and the south-west with four bodyguards (all about 35). They are well below you, but five at once still hurts: start at full health and mana with a Healthstone in your bags, send the Voidwalker at the courier, put Corruption and Curse of Agony on her and then on each bodyguard, Fear the one that hits you and Drain Life; use Sacrifice when it goes wrong. Kill the courier first and loot her Sealed Folder. You can walk away as soon as you have it.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=52.5, y=61.5},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={658}, names={"Hints of a New Plague?"}, text="Quae", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=60.2, y=53.9},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={657}, names={"Hints of a New Plague?"}, text="Quae", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=60.2, y=53.8},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={657}, names={"Hints of a New Plague?"}, text="Kinelory, beside her", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=60.2, y=53.9},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={660}, names={"Hints of a New Plague?"}, text="Kinelory", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=60.2, y=53.9},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={660}, names={"Hints of a New Plague?"}, text="Escort Kinelory down into the Go'Shek Farm and back. She fights well; send the Voidwalker at what attacks her (Forsaken, about 33-36), DoT it, and stay with her until she is back with Quae.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=60.2, y=53.9},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={660}, names={"Hints of a New Plague?"}, text="Quae", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=60.2, y=53.8},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={661}, names={"Hints of a New Plague?"}, text="Quae. Goes to Phin Odelic in Southshore at the end of the Arathi round.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=60.2, y=53.8},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={642}, names={"The Princess Trapped"}, text="The Shards of Myzrael, a crystal on the hillside north of the farm", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=62.5, y=33.7},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={642}, names={"The Princess Trapped"}, text="12 Motes of Myzrael from the Drywhisker kobolds (35-38) in Drywhisker Gorge, in the north-east corner", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=80.0, y=36.0, path={{61.4,34.0},{61.8,35.8},{68.4,35.5},{71.6,30.7},{73.8,30.7},{76.3,32.2},{78.7,36.1}}},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={642}, names={"The Princess Trapped"}, text="The Iridescent Shards, the big crystal at the back of the Drywhisker cave", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=84.3, y=31.0},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={651}, names={"Stones of Binding"}, text="The Iridescent Shards", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=84.3, y=31.0},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={651}, obj={2}, names={"Stones of Binding"}, text="Cresting Key: click the Stone of East Binding, the standing stone in the middle of the Circle of East Binding, and loot the key. Cresting Exiles (water elementals, 38-39) guard the circle: clear the ones near the stone, Voidwalker first; your shadow and fire spells work on them, and you can Banish a second one that joins.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=66.7, y=29.7},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={691}, names={"Worth Its Weight in Gold"}, text="Witherbark Village, in the south-east. 10 Witherbark Tusks from any troll, 4 Medicine Pouches from the Witch Doctors, and the Shadow Hunter Knife from a Witherbark Shadow Hunter (35-36) in the cave at the south end (68, 80). All of it is below your level.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=66.6, y=70.0},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={651}, obj={3}, names={"Stones of Binding"}, text="Thundering Key: loot it from the Stone of Outer Binding in the Circle of Outer Binding, just east of Refuge Pointe. Thundering Exiles (air elementals, 38-39) guard it; your shadow and fire spells work on them. Banish a second one that joins.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=52.0, y=50.7, path={{66.2,72.3},{60.0,70.2},{52.4,57.6},{50.0,57.3},{49.2,52.2},{50.2,50.7}}},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={691}, names={"Worth Its Weight in Gold"}, text="Apprentice Kryten at Refuge Pointe", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=46.2, y=47.8},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={693}, names={"Wand over Fist"}, text="Skuerto, a few steps from Kryten", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=46.6, y=47.0},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={693}, names={"Wand over Fist"}, text="Kor'gresh Coldrage (39) is in the cave at the back of Boulderfist Hall, the ogre mound in the south. The Boulderfist Brutes and Magi on the way are 35-37. Kor'gresh throws frost and can root you, and a warlock has no interrupt: put Curse of Tongues on him, let the Voidwalker hold him, and when you are rooted just keep casting (Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate, Drain Life). Fear a Brute that comes with him. Loot Trelane's Wand of Invocation.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=54.8, y=81.9, path={{53.9,76.8}}, cave=true},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={693}, names={"Wand over Fist"}, text="Skuerto at Refuge Pointe. Stop here: the next part is elite.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=46.6, y=47.0},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={651}, obj={1}, names={"Stones of Binding"}, text="Burning Key: loot it from the Stone of West Binding in the Circle of West Binding, in the north-west. Burning Exiles (fire elementals, 38-39) guard it: fire does nothing to them, so leave Immolate out and use Corruption, Curse of Agony, Shadow Bolt and Drain Life. Banish a second one that joins.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=25.5, y=30.1},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={651}, names={"Stones of Binding"}, text="The Stone of Inner Binding, in the small circle south of the road and east of Stromgarde. Stop here: the next part (Breaking the Keystone) is elite.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=36.2, y=57.4},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={663}, names={"Land Ho!"}, text="Lolo the Lookout. Faldir's Cove is on the south coast: the path down starts south of the Inner Binding circle, west of the Thandol Span, and winds down the cliff to the beach.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=31.8, y=82.7},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={663}, names={"Land Ho!"}, text="Shakes O'Breen, the captain on the beach", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=32.3, y=81.4},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={662}, names={"Deep Sea Salvage"}, text="First Mate Nilzlix", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=32.8, y=81.5},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={664}, names={"Drowned Sorrows"}, text="Captain Steelgut", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=34.0, y=80.8},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={665}, names={"Sunken Treasure"}, text="Professor Phizzlethorpe", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=33.9, y=80.5},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={665}, names={"Sunken Treasure"}, text="Escort the professor up to the cave above the cove and back. Daggerspine naga ambush him at the cave: send the Voidwalker at them (it holds the attackers; you cannot heal him), Fear one if there are more than it can hold, and kill them one by one. Stay close to him the whole way.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=33.9, y=80.5},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={665}, names={"Sunken Treasure"}, text="Doctor Draxlegauge, beside the professor", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=33.9, y=80.4},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={666}, names={"Sunken Treasure"}, text="Doctor Draxlegauge. He gives you the Goggles of Gem Hunting.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=33.9, y=80.5},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={664,662,666}, names={"Drowned Sorrows","Deep Sea Salvage","Sunken Treasure"}, text="Swim west along the coast to the two shipwrecks. Put on the goggles: they show the Calcified Elven Gems on the sea bed around the wrecks, collect 10. The Maiden's Folly (23.1, 84.8) and the Spirit of Silverpine (20.5, 85.4) each hold one chart and one log. Kill 10 Daggerspine Raiders (38-39) and 3 Sorceresses (39-40) between the wrecks: kill the Sorceresses first (Curse of Tongues on them, or Fear one while the Voidwalker holds a Raider). Cast Unending Breath before you dive and renew it when it runs out. Put your own helm back on afterwards.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=22.0, y=87.0},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={662}, names={"Deep Sea Salvage"}, text="First Mate Nilzlix", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=32.8, y=81.5},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={664}, names={"Drowned Sorrows"}, text="Captain Steelgut", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=34.0, y=80.8},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={666}, names={"Sunken Treasure"}, text="Doctor Draxlegauge", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=33.9, y=80.5},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={668}, names={"Sunken Treasure"}, text="Doctor Draxlegauge", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=33.9, y=80.4},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={668}, names={"Sunken Treasure"}, text="Shakes O'Breen", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=32.3, y=81.4},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={669}, names={"Sunken Treasure"}, text="Shakes O'Breen. A sample gem for Fleet Master Seahorn in Booty Bay: keep it for a later Stranglethorn trip.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=32.3, y=81.4},
  {t="L", seg=16, lvl=40, text="Not 40 yet? Stay with the Daggerspine naga at the wrecks until you are: Briarthorn gives the warlock's mount quest, Summon Felsteed, only at level 40, and Ironforge is not on the route again for a long time.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=22.0, y=87.0},
  {t="H", seg=16, arg="Southshore", text="Hearthstone: you last used it after the Alterac round, so it is ready. If it is not, walk up to Refuge Pointe and fly to Southshore"},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={661}, names={"Hints of a New Plague?"}, text="Phin Odelic, in the Southshore inn building", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=50.4, y=59.0},
  {t="FLY", seg=16, arg="Ironforge", text="Darla Harris, the Southshore gryphon master", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=49.3, y=52.3},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=16, text="Briarthorn, the warlock trainer in the Forlorn Cavern in the north of the city: learn everything he offers at level 40, with Howl of Terror, your new escape: it sends every enemy around you running for a few seconds (never use it near other packs). The demon trainer beside him sells the Voidwalker's new spell books.", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=50.4, y=5.7},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={4487}, names={"Summon Felsteed"}, text="Briarthorn: Summon Felsteed, the warlock's mount quest (needs level 40). It sends you to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet, where the next segment starts: he teaches you the Felsteed for free, so you need no riding trainer and no gold for a mount. Keep the quest; you walk until Ratchet.", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=50.4, y=5.7},
  {t="FLY", seg=16, arg="Menethil Harbor", text="Gryth Thurden, the Ironforge gryphon master", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=55.5, y=47.7},
  {t="N", seg=16, arg="Optional dungeon: Krol'dok Stronghold, levels 40-45", text="New Forever dungeon, not checked in game yet. It is in the Riverglades, the new zone east of the Badlands: a fortress on a hill at about 48.6, 26.3 on the Riverglades map. Alliance players fly to Farholde Keep. Quest givers listed for it: Sergeant Riftan (Riverglades 30.6, 49.1: Lingering Essence, Twilight Mementos), and Ashe Amberhall and Commander Demar Brant in Farholde Keep (Riverglades 66.7, 81.0: Curios of Curiosity, Tome of Twilight, Eye of Mugg). Take what they offer: the addon logs it so these steps can be filled in.", dg=15, run=true},
  {t="N", seg=16, arg="Take the boat from Menethil Harbor to Theramore", text="You keep 4487 (Summon Felsteed: Strahad Farsan, Ratchet), 1137 (Fizzle, Mirage Raceway), 1111 and 1178 (Ratchet), 669 and 209 (Booty Bay), 212 (Stormwind). Your hearthstone stays in Southshore until Gadgetzan."},
  {t="FLY", seg=17, arg="Ratchet", text="You arrive on the Theramore dock. Baldruc, the gryphon master, is in the south-east of town: walk there, you have no mount until Ratchet.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=67.5, y=51.3},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={7070}, names={"Shadowshard Fragments"}, text="Archmage Tervosh in Theramore. Shadowshard Fragments drop from the rumblers on the purple side, before the dungeon portal.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=66.4, y=49.3, dg=11},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={1111}, names={"Wharfmaster Dizzywig"}, text="Wharfmaster Dizzywig, on the Ratchet dock", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=63.4, y=38.5},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={1112}, names={"Parts for Kravel"}, text="Wharfmaster Dizzywig", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=63.4, y=38.5},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={1178}, names={"Goblin Sponsorship"}, text="Gazlowe, upstairs in the big building in the middle of Ratchet. Do not take his follow-up: it sends you to Booty Bay.", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=62.7, y=36.2},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={4487}, names={"Summon Felsteed"}, text="Strahad Farsan, the warlock on the hill / tower at the edge of Ratchet (follow the arrow). This is your last walk on foot.", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=62.6, y=35.5},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={4490}, names={"Summon Felsteed"}, text="Strahad Farsan", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=62.6, y=35.5},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={4490}, names={"Summon Felsteed"}, text="Strahad Farsan: he teaches Summon Felsteed. Put it on your bars: from here on the route says \"ride\"", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=62.6, y=35.5},
  {t="N", seg=17, arg="Optional warlock quests at Strahad's tower: not routed", text="Menara Voidrender beside him gives the optional level 31 / 35 warlock quests (robe and orb), and Strahad the level 30 Felhunter chain. None of them is in this route: take them only if you want the detours."},
  {t="FLY", seg=17, arg="Gadgetzan", text="Bragok, the Ratchet flight master", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=63.1, y=37.2},
  {t="S", seg=17, arg="Gadgetzan", text="Innkeeper Fizzgrimble at the inn", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=27.9},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2781}, names={"WANTED: Caliph Scorpidsting"}, text="The Wanted Poster in Gadgetzan, a few steps west of the inn", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.8, y=27.0},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2875}, names={"WANTED: Andre Firebeard"}, text="The same Wanted Poster", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.8, y=27.0},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={1690}, names={"Wastewander Justice"}, text="Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle, in the middle of town", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.5},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={1707}, names={"Water Pouch Bounty"}, text="Spigot Operator Luglunket, next to him", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.4},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={992}, names={"Gadgetzan Water Survey"}, text="Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser, in the west of town", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.2, y=27.5},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={992}, names={"Gadgetzan Water Survey"}, text="Ride west to Sandsorrow Watch and use the Untapped Dowsing Widget at the small pool beside the troll huts. The Sandfury trolls around it are elite (42-44): come in from the south-west, use the widget at the near edge of the pool and ride off at once. A bug may jump you when you tap the water: just ride away from it.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=39.0, y=29.3},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={992}, names={"Gadgetzan Water Survey"}, text="Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser in Gadgetzan", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.2, y=27.5},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={82}, names={"Noxious Lair Investigation"}, text="Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser. Keep it: the Noxious Lair bugs are 47-50 and belong to the next segment.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.2, y=27.5},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={1690,1707}, names={"Wastewander Justice","Water Pouch Bounty"}, text="The Wastewander camps east of Gadgetzan: kill 10 Bandits (41-42) and 10 Thieves (40-41). Every Wastewander can drop a Water Pouch; you need 5. Send the Voidwalker in first, then Corruption, Curse of Agony and Immolate. If a second one comes, Fear it, but only at the outer edge of a camp: a feared mob brings friends. Fight at full health and mana (Life Tap, then Drain Life). They run at low health: your DoTs usually finish a runner, otherwise Shadow Bolt it. Drain Soul some last hits and keep 3-5 Soul Shards.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=62.7, y=29.3},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={1690}, names={"Wastewander Justice"}, text="Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.5},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={1691}, names={"More Wastewander Justice"}, text="Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.5},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={1707}, names={"Water Pouch Bounty"}, text="Spigot Operator Luglunket", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.4},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={1691}, names={"More Wastewander Justice"}, text="The southern Wastewander camps, south of the first ones: 10 Shadow Mages (41-43), 8 Rogues (43-44) and 6 Assassins (44-45). They are above you: pull from the edge, one at a time, and kill the Shadow Mages first: a warlock has no interrupt, so put Curse of Tongues on them and burn them down, or Fear one while you kill another. Eat, drink or bandage between pulls. Rogues and Assassins sit in stealth, so keep your back to cleared ground and send the Voidwalker onto whatever opens on you.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=62.0, y=37.3},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={2781}, names={"WANTED: Caliph Scorpidsting"}, text="Caliph Scorpidsting (46) stands in the middle of the southern camp and walks around with two guards. Leave him for the end of the camp, when you have a level more on you. Rest to full, put a Soulstone on yourself and have a Healthstone ready. Pull the group from as far away as you can and back off so the three string out; Voidwalker on the first guard, Fear the second, kill the guards first, then the Caliph. Howl of Terror is your escape if all three reach you. If he is too much alone, wait for other players or come back for him after the pirates.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=61.8, y=38.2},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={8366}, names={"Southsea Shakedown"}, text="Security Chief Bilgewhizzle at Steamwheedle Port, the goblin harbour on the coast north-east of the camps", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=67.1, y=23.9},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={8365}, names={"Pirate Hats Ahoy!"}, text="Haughty Modiste, in the north of the port", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=66.6, y=22.3},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={3520}, names={"Screecher Spirits"}, text="Yeh'kinya, the troll next to her. Keep it: the screechers are in Feralas, next segment.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=67.0, y=22.4},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={8366,8365,2875}, names={"Southsea Shakedown","Pirate Hats Ahoy!","WANTED: Andre Firebeard"}, text="Lost Rigger Cove, the walled pirate town down the coast south of the port. Kill 10 each of Southsea Pirates, Freebooters, Dock Workers and Swashbucklers (all 44-45); Andre Firebeard (45) stands by the fire near the docks (73.4, 47.1). The 20 Pirate Hats drop from any of them, but not often, so you stay well past the 40 kills: good, every kill here shortens the grind at the end. Pull from the gap in the wall, never more than two: the Voidwalker holds one, and you Fear the other only while you stand outside the wall, never inside the town. Let your DoTs finish runners, or Shadow Bolt them. If three come, Howl of Terror and back out through the gap. Dock Workers are on the piers, Swashbucklers on the ships.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=73.5, y=46.5, path={{65.0,22.9},{65.0,39.7},{69.8,47.2}}},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2876}, names={"Ship Schedules"}, text="Only if you find a Ship Schedule at the cove (a rare find from the pirates and their footlockers): right-click it to start Ship Schedules. No schedule: press Skip here and on its hand-in.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=73.5, y=46.5},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={8366}, names={"Southsea Shakedown"}, text="Security Chief Bilgewhizzle at Steamwheedle Port", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=67.1, y=23.9, path={{69.8,47.2},{65.0,39.7},{64.6,26.8}}},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={2875}, names={"WANTED: Andre Firebeard"}, text="Security Chief Bilgewhizzle", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=67.1, y=23.9},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={2876}, names={"Ship Schedules"}, text="Security Chief Bilgewhizzle (only if you had the Ship Schedule)", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=67.1, y=23.9},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={8365}, names={"Pirate Hats Ahoy!"}, text="Haughty Modiste", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=66.6, y=22.3},
  {t="H", seg=17, arg="Gadgetzan", text="Use your hearthstone"},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={1691}, names={"More Wastewander Justice"}, text="Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.5},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={2781}, names={"WANTED: Caliph Scorpidsting"}, text="Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.5},
  {t="L", seg=17, lvl=42, text="The grind of this segment: half a level or more by the estimate, less for every extra pirate you killed for hats. Best spots: the southern Wastewander camp (41-45, fast respawn, close to Gadgetzan) or back at Lost Rigger Cove if the hats kept you there anyway. Stay until 42 or close to it: the Mirage Raceway hand-ins that follow add about a tenth of a level, and Feralas, next, wants 42. Sell and repair in Gadgetzan before you leave.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=62.0, y=37.3},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={1137}, names={"News for Fizzle"}, text="Ride north out of Tanaris to the Mirage Raceway. Fizzle Brassbolts, on the gnome side.", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.1, y=77.1},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={1112}, names={"Parts for Kravel"}, text="Kravel Koalbeard", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=77.8, y=77.3},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={1114}, names={"Delivery to the Gnomes"}, text="Kravel Koalbeard", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=77.8, y=77.3},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={1114}, names={"Delivery to the Gnomes"}, text="Fizzle Brassbolts. Do not take Kravel's next one, The Rumormonger: it goes to Booty Bay.", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.1, y=77.1},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2770}, names={"Gahz'rilla"}, text="Wizzle Brassbolts at the Mirage Raceway. Gahz'rilla is summoned with the Mallet of Zul'Farrak, which takes its own trip to the Hinterlands; skip this one if your group does not have the mallet.", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.1, y=77.1, dg=10},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={1190}, names={"Keeping Pace"}, text="Pozzik, on the goblin side of the track", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=80.2, y=75.9},
  {t="N", seg=17, arg="Ask Zamek for his diversion", text="Zamek stands on the goblin side. Tell him to start: while his explosion draws Rizzle away, run straight over to the gnome side.", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=79.8, y=77.0},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={1190}, names={"Keeping Pace"}, text="Rizzle's Unguarded Plans, on the gnome side: click them while Rizzle is away", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=77.2, y=77.4},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={1194}, names={"Rizzle's Schematics"}, text="Rizzle's Unguarded Plans", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=77.2, y=77.4},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={1194}, names={"Rizzle's Schematics"}, text="Pozzik", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=80.2, y=75.9},
  {t="N", seg=17, arg="Next: ride west through Thousand Needles to Feralas", text="You keep 82 (Noxious Lair, Tanaris), 3520 (screechers, Feralas), 209 and 669 (Booty Bay), 212 (Stormwind). Your hearthstone stays in Gadgetzan."},
  {t="N", seg=18, arg="Ride west from the Mirage Raceway, up out of the Shimmering Flats and along the floor of Thousand Needles to Thalanaar", text="Stay on the canyon floor: Freewind Post on the mesa above is a Horde town. The road leaves the canyon at its west end; Thalanaar is the small night elf camp right at the Feralas border.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=89.5, y=45.9},
  {t="F", seg=18, arg="Thalanaar", text="Thyssiana, the hippogryph master", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=89.5, y=45.9},
  {t="N", seg=18, arg="Ride west on the Feralas road to the Moonweavers' hill", text="About 5 minutes on your Felsteed. The road passes just south of Camp Mojache, a Horde town: stay on the road and keep riding. Kindal and Jer'kai Moonweaver stand on a hill at the south-west edge of the Grimtotem compound.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=65.9, y=45.6, path={{89.7,38.5},{84.1,36.7},{82.1,36.7},{80.9,38.5},{79.1,37.0},{72.8,37.3}}},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={2969}, names={"Freedom for All Creatures"}, text="Kindal Moonweaver. First kill the Grimtotems that stand near the sprite darter pen, then take the quest: it has a 6-minute timer and starts as soon as you accept.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=65.9, y=45.6},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={2969}, names={"Freedom for All Creatures"}, text="Kindal walks with you into the camp. Open the pen with the Bamboo Cage Key, then kill the Grimtotems that rush in: at least 6 sprite darters and Kindal must live. Send the Voidwalker onto the attackers and keep them off the darters; you cannot heal them. Do not Fear here: a feared Grimtotem runs through the darters. Kill the Grimtotem healers first: a warlock has no interrupt, so put Curse of Tongues on them and burn them down. If it fails, take the quest again; if it keeps failing, skip it and Doling Justice.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=67.9, y=43.5},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={2969}, names={"Freedom for All Creatures"}, text="Kindal Moonweaver, back on the hill", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=65.9, y=45.6},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={2970}, names={"Doling Justice"}, text="Jer'kai Moonweaver, next to her", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=66.0, y=45.6},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={2970}, names={"Doling Justice"}, text="The Grimtotem compound below the hill: 12 Grimtotem Naturalists, 10 Raiders and 6 Shamans (41-44; the Shamans heal). Pull from the edge of the camp, one at a time: Voidwalker first, then Corruption, Curse of Agony and Immolate. Kill the healers first, with Curse of Tongues on them instead of Curse of Agony; Fear a second mob only at the outer edge. Eat, drink or bandage between pulls.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=67.3, y=46.7},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={2970}, names={"Doling Justice"}, text="Jer'kai Moonweaver. He offers a second Doling Justice that goes to Darnassus: leave it.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=66.0, y=45.6},
  {t="N", seg=18, arg="Ride west along the road to the dock on the Forgotten Coast and take the boat to Feathermoon Stronghold", text="The road ends at the coast; the dock is where the gnome Zorbin Fandazzle stands. The boat crosses to Sardor Isle in about a minute.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=44.8, y=43.4},
  {t="F", seg=18, arg="Feathermoon Stronghold", text="Fyldren Moonfeather", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=30.2, y=43.3},
  {t="S", seg=18, arg="Feathermoon Stronghold", text="Innkeeper Shyria (31.0, 43.5)"},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={2866}, names={"The Ruins of Solarsal"}, text="Shandris Feathermoon, in the main building", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=30.3, y=46.2},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={4124}, names={"The Missing Courier"}, text="Latronicus Moonspear, next to her", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=30.4, y=46.2},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={2982}, names={"The High Wilderness"}, text="Angelas Moonbreeze", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=31.8, y=45.6},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={4124}, names={"The Missing Courier"}, text="Ginro Hearthkindle", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=31.9, y=45.1},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={4125}, names={"The Missing Courier"}, text="Ginro Hearthkindle", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=31.9, y=45.1},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={2821}, names={"The Mark of Quality"}, text="Pratt McGrubben, near the hippogryph master", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=30.6, y=42.7},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={2866}, names={"The Ruins of Solarsal"}, text="Ride south-west on the isle to the Ruins of Solarsal and click the Solarsal Gazebo (26.3, 52.3). Hatecrest naga (41-43) stand around it.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=26.3, y=52.3, path={{25.6,46.3}}},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={2867}, names={"Return to Feathermoon Stronghold"}, text="From the gazebo", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=26.3, y=52.3},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={2867}, names={"Return to Feathermoon Stronghold"}, text="Back in the stronghold: Shandris Feathermoon", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=30.3, y=46.2},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={3130}, names={"Against the Hatecrest"}, text="Shandris Feathermoon", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=30.3, y=46.2},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={3130}, names={"Against the Hatecrest"}, text="Latronicus Moonspear", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=30.4, y=46.2},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={2869}, names={"Against the Hatecrest"}, text="Latronicus Moonspear", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=30.4, y=46.2},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={2869}, names={"Against the Hatecrest"}, text="Back at the Ruins of Solarsal: Hatecrest Warriors, Screamers, Sirens and Wave Riders drop the 10 scales. Screamers and Sirens are casters: put Curse of Tongues on them and kill them first, or Fear one while you kill the other.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=28.5, y=53.8},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={2869}, names={"Against the Hatecrest"}, text="Latronicus Moonspear", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=30.4, y=46.2},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={2870}, names={"Against Lord Shalzaru"}, text="Latronicus Moonspear. Lord Shalzaru is level 47: you kill him after the level 44 grind, on your next visit.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=30.4, y=46.2},
  {t="N", seg=18, arg="Take the boat back to the mainland dock", text="Keep any OOX-22/FE Distress Beacon that drops from here on: almost every Feralas mob can drop it (about 1 in 100), and you use it on the east loop.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=44.8, y=43.4},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={4125}, names={"The Missing Courier"}, text="Ride south along the Forgotten Coast to the Wrecked Row Boat on the beach.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=45.4, y=65.0},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={4127}, names={"Boat Wreckage"}, text="From the boat", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=45.4, y=65.0},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={2821}, names={"The Mark of Quality"}, text="Ride east into Feral Scar Vale. Feral Scar Yetis, Enraged and Hulking Feral Scars (43-46) drop the 10 Thick Yeti Hides.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=53.5, y=57.5},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={3520}, names={"Screecher Spirits"}, text="Screecher Spirits: Rogue Vale Screechers (44-46) roam north and west of the vale (48-61, 47-59), Vale Screechers (41-43) the slopes east of it (57-60, 55-62). Kill one, use Yeh'kinya's Bramble on the corpse, then click the spirit that appears. You need three.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=55.0, y=52.0},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={2982}, names={"The High Wilderness"}, text="Ride south-east to the Ruins of Isildien. Gordunni Brutes stand at the north edge (60, 55), Gordunni Shamans and Warlocks deeper in (59-61, 64-68): 8 of each. Kill casters first (Curse of Tongues on them: you have no interrupt) and pull them out of sight of the next group; if a second ogre joins, Fear it and back off onto cleared ground.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=60.0, y=64.0, path={{55.4,60.6},{58.6,64.8}}},
  {t="L", seg=18, lvl=44, text="The big grind of the route starts here. Stay on the Gordunni ogres of the Ruins of Isildien (42-46) and the Feral Scar yetis in the vale just west (43-46) until level 44. Everything left in Feralas is level 44-50: Lord Shalzaru, the Zukk'ash hive, the Rage Scar yetis, the coast giants. Drain Soul now and then: keep 3-5 Soul Shards. Keep looting: the robot beacon drops here too.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=60.0, y=62.0},
  {t="H", seg=18, arg="Feathermoon Stronghold", text="Use your hearthstone: you last used it in Gadgetzan, long ago. If it is not ready, ride west to the dock on the Forgotten Coast (44.8, 43.4) and take the boat."},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={4127}, names={"Boat Wreckage"}, text="Ginro Hearthkindle", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=31.9, y=45.1},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={4129}, names={"The Knife Revealed"}, text="Ginro Hearthkindle", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=31.9, y=45.1},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={4129}, names={"The Knife Revealed"}, text="Quintis Jonespyre, in the next building (32.4, 43.8)", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=32.4, y=43.8},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={4130}, names={"Psychometric Reading"}, text="Quintis Jonespyre", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=32.4, y=43.8},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={4130}, names={"Psychometric Reading"}, text="Ginro Hearthkindle", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=31.9, y=45.1},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={4131}, names={"The Woodpaw Gnolls"}, text="Ginro Hearthkindle", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=31.9, y=45.1},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={2821}, names={"The Mark of Quality"}, text="Pratt McGrubben", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=30.6, y=42.7},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={7733}, names={"Improved Quality"}, text="Pratt McGrubben", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=30.6, y=42.7},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={2982}, names={"The High Wilderness"}, text="Angelas Moonbreeze", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=31.8, y=45.6},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={2870}, names={"Against Lord Shalzaru"}, text="Swim south from Sardor Isle to the Isle of Dread. Lord Shalzaru (47) is in the naga cave on its shore; Hatecrest Serpent Guards, Sorceresses and Myrmidons (43-45) stand on the way in. Clear to him, rest to full, put a Soulstone on yourself and fight him alone: Voidwalker on him, Curse of Tongues to slow his casts, Health Funnel when the Voidwalker drops low, Healthstone for yourself. Stay on the shore: in Classic the high ground of this isle belongs to elite chimaeroks.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=28.5, y=70.5},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={2870}, names={"Against Lord Shalzaru"}, text="Back in the stronghold: Latronicus Moonspear", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=30.4, y=46.2},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={2871}, names={"Delivering the Relic"}, text="Latronicus Moonspear", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=30.4, y=46.2},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={2871}, names={"Delivering the Relic"}, text="Vestia Moonspear (30.1, 45.1)", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=30.1, y=45.1},
  {t="N", seg=18, arg="Take the boat to the mainland and ride east along the road to the Woodpaw Hills", text="A long ride: follow the road east past the Twin Colossals turn-off, then leave it south-east before Camp Mojache (Horde).", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=73.3, y=56.3},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={4131}, names={"The Woodpaw Gnolls"}, text="Large Leather Backpacks in the big Woodpaw gnoll camp (73.3, 56.3). Woodpaw Mystics, Reavers and Alphas (42-44) guard it.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=73.3, y=56.3},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={4135}, names={"The Writhing Deep"}, text="From the backpacks. You also get an Undelivered Parcel.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=73.3, y=56.3},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={4281}, names={"Thalanaar Delivery"}, text="Right-click the Undelivered Parcel in your bags to start Thalanaar Delivery. You hand it in when you leave Feralas.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=73.3, y=56.3},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={4135}, names={"The Writhing Deep"}, text="Ride south into the Writhing Deep, the silithid hive. The Zukk'ash Pod hangs at the bottom of the hive (72.1, 63.7). Zukk'ash bugs are 44-46: kill your way down, do not run past them.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=72.1, y=63.7},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={4265}, names={"Freed from the Hive"}, text="From the pod: Raschal is freed. You report it to Ginro later.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=72.1, y=63.7},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={7733}, names={"Improved Quality"}, text="Ride back north-west to the road, west along it, then north to Rage Scar Hold. Rage Scar Yetis, Ferocious and Elder Rage Scars (46-49) drop the 10 hides. Pull one at a time, at full health: the Voidwalker holds it, Health Funnel keeps the Voidwalker up, Drain Life keeps you up. Eat or bandage between pulls.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=53.4, y=31.7},
  {t="L", seg=18, lvl=45, text="Second half of the grind: stay on the Rage Scar yetis until level 45. They are 2-4 levels above you and pay well; if they hurt too much, ride back to the Gordunni ogres at the Ruins of Isildien (60, 62) instead. Zorbin's and Rockbiter's quests need level 44-45.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=53.4, y=31.7},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={2766}, names={"Find OOX-22/FE!"}, text="Ride south to Feral Scar Vale. Right-click the OOX-22/FE Distress Beacon: the robot is in a small cave at the edge of the vale. No beacon yet? Kill the yetis and screechers around the cave until one drops; if you give up, skip these four robot steps (the Booty Bay hand-ins for it in segment 20 then drop out too).", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=53.4, y=55.7, path={{51.8,31.6},{49.6,37.0},{49.6,43.3},{53.0,48.7},{53.0,53.1},{53.8,54.3},{53.0,56.1}}, cave=true},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={2766}, names={"Find OOX-22/FE!"}, text="Homing Robot OOX-22/FE", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=53.4, y=55.7},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={2767}, names={"Rescue OOX-22/FE!"}, text="Homing Robot OOX-22/FE", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=53.4, y=55.7},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={2767}, names={"Rescue OOX-22/FE!"}, text="Escort the robot west to the dock on the Forgotten Coast. Stay off your Felsteed. Ambushers jump it on the way: send the Voidwalker onto them so they leave the robot alone, and kill them fast. You hand it in at Booty Bay in segment 20.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=45.0, y=43.5, path={{54.0,54.3},{53.0,52.8},{53.0,48.7},{49.2,41.5},{46.8,41.5}}},
  {t="N", seg=18, arg="Take the boat to Feathermoon Stronghold", text="You are at the dock already.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=44.8, y=43.4},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={4265}, names={"Freed from the Hive"}, text="Ginro Hearthkindle", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=31.9, y=45.1},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={4266}, names={"A Hero's Welcome"}, text="Ginro Hearthkindle", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=31.9, y=45.1},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={4266}, names={"A Hero's Welcome"}, text="Shandris Feathermoon. She offers Rise of the Silithid (to Darnassus): leave it.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=30.3, y=46.2},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={7733}, names={"Improved Quality"}, text="Pratt McGrubben", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=30.6, y=42.7},
  {t="N", seg=18, arg="Lord Shalzaru still alive? Kill him now and hand in to Latronicus and Vestia Moonspear", text="Only if you skipped him earlier."},
  {t="N", seg=18, arg="Take the boat back to the mainland dock", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=44.8, y=43.4},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={7003,7721}, names={"Zapped Giants","Fuel for the Zapping"}, text="Zorbin Fandazzle at the dock", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=44.8, y=43.4},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={2844}, names={"The Giant Guardian"}, text="Ride north along the coast to Rockbiter, the friendly giant at the foot of the Twin Colossals (42.4, 22.0). On the way, zap any giant you pass with Zorbin's Ultra-Shrinker and kill the small version: Land Walkers and Cliff Giants walk around Rockbiter's camp.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=42.4, y=22.0},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={2844}, names={"The Giant Guardian"}, text="Shay Leafrunner, further north at the edge of the Northspring harpy nests (38.2, 10.3)", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=38.2, y=10.3},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={2845}, names={"Wandering Shay"}, text="Shay Leafrunner. 15-minute timer.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=38.2, y=10.3},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={2845}, names={"Wandering Shay"}, text="Take Shay's Bell from the chest next to her, then walk back south to Rockbiter. She wanders off every minute or so: ring the bell and she runs back. Stay off your Felsteed and kill anything that comes near her (Voidwalker on it first); the Northspring harpies (48-50) are close at the start.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=42.4, y=22.0},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={2845}, names={"Wandering Shay"}, text="Rockbiter", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=42.4, y=22.0},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={7003,7721}, names={"Zapped Giants","Fuel for the Zapping"}, text="Back down the coast, south of the dock. Sea Elementals and Sea Sprays (47-49) drop the 10 cores; if two come at once, Banish one and kill the other. For the 15 residues, zap Shore, Wave and Deep Striders with the Ultra-Shrinker, then kill the small zapped giant. The giants are elite: never fight one that is not zapped.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=43.5, y=49.0, path={{46.0,36.7},{46.0,48.4}}},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={7003,7721}, names={"Zapped Giants","Fuel for the Zapping"}, text="Zorbin Fandazzle. Skip his repeat versions.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=44.8, y=43.4},
  {t="N", seg=18, arg="Take the boat to Feathermoon Stronghold (or use your hearthstone)", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=30.2, y=43.3},
  {t="FLY", seg=18, arg="Thalanaar", text="Fyldren Moonfeather"},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={4281}, names={"Thalanaar Delivery"}, text="Falfindel Waywarder (89.6, 46.6)", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=89.6, y=46.6},
  {t="FLY", seg=18, arg="Gadgetzan", text="Thyssiana"},
  {t="S", seg=18, arg="Gadgetzan", text="Innkeeper Fizzgrimble. Your hearthstone stays here into the next segment."},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={5863}, names={"The Dunemaul Compound"}, text="Andi Lynn", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.8, y=27.4},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={2605}, names={"The Thirsty Goblin"}, text="Marin Noggenfogger", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.8, y=28.7},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={3362}, names={"Thistleshrub Valley"}, text="Tran'rek", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.6, y=26.8},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={82}, names={"Noxious Lair Investigation"}, text="Ride west to the Noxious Lair. Centipaar bugs (47-50) drop the 5 insect parts; Workers, Tunnelers and Sandreavers drop them most often. Fight at the mouth of the hive, one at a time. They poison, and a warlock cannot cure it: bandage, Drain Life and eat.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=33.5, y=44.5, path={{51.6,24.7},{49.6,24.7},{45.6,27.1},{44.0,29.5},{44.0,35.2},{36.8,48.1},{35.2,47.8}}},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={82}, names={"Noxious Lair Investigation"}, text="Back in Gadgetzan: Alchemist Pestlezugg", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.9, y=27.0, path={{35.2,47.8},{36.8,48.1},{44.0,36.1},{44.0,29.5},{45.6,27.1},{48.2,25.9}}},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={10}, names={"The Scrimshank Redemption"}, text="Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.2, y=27.5},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={3161}, names={"Gahz'ridian"}, text="Ride south out of Gadgetzan to Marvon Rivetseeker, alone at a small camp in the desert (52.7, 45.9)", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.7, y=45.9},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={3161}, names={"Gahz'ridian"}, text="Ride south-west to the Eastmoon Ruins. Keep the Gahz'ridian Detector running: it shows the buried ornaments on your minimap. You need 30; the Southmoon Ruins (40, 73) hold more. Dunemaul ogres camp in both ruins.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=47.5, y=65.0},
  {t="L", seg=18, lvl=46, text="The Dunemaul Compound, just north-west. Thistleshrub Valley and the two escorts after it are level 48-50, so kill Dunemaul Brutes and Enforcers (46-48) here until level 46; they count for The Dunemaul Compound. The ogres stand in twos and threes: pull the ones at the edge, kill Ogre Mages and Warlocks first (Curse of Tongues on them, or Fear one while you kill the other; Howl of Terror if three reach you), and eat, drink or bandage between pulls.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=40.7, y=58.0},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={5863}, names={"The Dunemaul Compound"}, text="Finish the 10 Dunemaul Brutes and 10 Enforcers, then kill Gor'marok the Ravager (49) in the compound. Clear the ogres around him first and fight him on his own, at full health, with a Soulstone on yourself and the Voidwalker on him.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=41.5, y=57.8},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={2605,3362}, names={"The Thirsty Goblin","Thistleshrub Valley"}, text="Thistleshrub Valley, the cactus garden south-west of the compound. Thistleshrub Dew Collectors drop the gland (about 1 in 10); 8 Gnarled Thistleshrubs and 8 Rootshapers (48-50) are the kill targets. Pull them one at a time.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=29.3, y=65.5, path={{41.4,60.3},{34.0,69.6},{32.0,69.3}}},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={1560}, names={"Tooga's Quest"}, text="Tooga the turtle sits at the south end of the valley (31.8, 74.1). Accept it only when the rest of the valley is done: 30-minute timer.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=31.8, y=74.1},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={3161}, names={"Gahz'ridian"}, text="Lead Tooga north-east across the desert. Marvon Rivetseeker (52.7, 45.9) is right on your line to Torta: hand in Gahz'ridian as you pass. Tooga follows you: stay off your Felsteed, keep him close and send the Voidwalker onto anything that attacks him.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.7, y=45.9, path={{38.0,65.7},{39.8,65.7},{40.8,67.2},{48.8,67.8},{49.2,63.0},{52.2,59.4},{51.6,53.4},{52.8,51.6}}},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={1560}, names={"Tooga's Quest"}, text="Go on north-east to Torta, on the beach just south of Steamwheedle Port. No detours and no extra pulls.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=66.6, y=25.7},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={1560}, names={"Tooga's Quest"}, text="Torta", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=66.6, y=25.7},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={3520}, names={"Screecher Spirits"}, text="Yeh'kinya in Steamwheedle Port, just north of Torta. Skip his next quest, The Prophecy of Mosh'aru: it needs Zul'Farrak.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=67.0, y=22.4},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={10}, names={"The Scrimshank Redemption"}, text="Ride south along the coast to the Gaping Chasm. Scrimshank's Surveying Gear lies deep inside the silithid hive. Hazzali bugs are 47-50: clear your way in, one or two at a time, and keep your back to cleared tunnel so more bugs can only come from the front.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=56.0, y=71.2, path={{65.0,22.9},{64.6,31.0},{59.6,37.9},{58.4,41.5},{57.2,41.5},{54.8,45.4},{54.8,51.6},{57.8,58.2},{57.4,69.6}}},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={351}, names={"Find OOX-17/TN!"}, text="Right-click the OOX-17/TN Distress Beacon if one has dropped (any Tanaris mob, about 1 in 100): the robot sits just north-east of the Gaping Chasm. No beacon? Skip these four robot steps; Oglethorpe's hand-in for it in Booty Bay (segment 20) then drops out too.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=60.2, y=64.7},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={351}, names={"Find OOX-17/TN!"}, text="Homing Robot OOX-17/TN", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=60.2, y=64.7},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={648}, names={"Rescue OOX-17/TN!"}, text="Homing Robot OOX-17/TN", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=60.2, y=64.7},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={648}, names={"Rescue OOX-17/TN!"}, text="Escort the robot north to Steamwheedle Port. Stay off your Felsteed; when ambushers jump it, send the Voidwalker onto them so they leave the robot alone. You hand it in at Booty Bay in segment 20.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=67.0, y=23.0, path={{60.0,59.4},{54.8,51.6},{54.8,45.4},{57.2,41.5},{58.4,41.5},{59.6,37.9},{64.6,31.0},{64.6,26.8}}},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={3527}, names={"The Prophecy of Mosh'aru"}, text="Yeh'kinya in Steamwheedle Port, after Screecher Spirits. The two tablets drop from Theka the Martyr and Hydromancer Velratha.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=67.0, y=22.4, dg=10},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={10}, names={"The Scrimshank Redemption"}, text="Back in Gadgetzan (ride west along the road): Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.2, y=27.5},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={110}, names={"Insect Part Analysis"}, text="Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.2, y=27.5},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={110}, names={"Insect Part Analysis"}, text="Alchemist Pestlezugg", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.9, y=27.0},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={113}, names={"Insect Part Analysis"}, text="Alchemist Pestlezugg", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.9, y=27.0},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={113}, names={"Insect Part Analysis"}, text="Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser. He offers Rise of the Silithid (to Darnassus): leave it.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.2, y=27.5},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={5863}, names={"The Dunemaul Compound"}, text="Andi Lynn", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.8, y=27.4},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={3362}, names={"Thistleshrub Valley"}, text="Tran'rek", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.6, y=26.8},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={2605}, names={"The Thirsty Goblin"}, text="Marin Noggenfogger", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.8, y=28.7},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={2606}, names={"In Good Taste"}, text="Marin Noggenfogger", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.8, y=28.7},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={3042}, names={"Troll Temper"}, text="Trenton Lighthammer in Gadgetzan. 20 Vials of Troll Temper from the trolls inside.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.4, y=28.8, dg=10},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={2768}, names={"Divino-matic Rod"}, text="Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle in Gadgetzan. The rod drops from Sergeant Bly after the stairs fight.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.5, dg=10},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={2606}, names={"In Good Taste"}, text="Sprinkle, a few steps away. Leave her next quest: its herb grows in the Hinterlands.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.1, y=26.9},
  {t="N", seg=18, arg="Optional dungeon: Zul'Farrak, levels 44-54", text="The entrance is in the north-west corner of Tanaris, a short ride from Gadgetzan. Thadius Grimshade at Nethergarde Keep also has Nekrum's Medallion for it, after a feather from the gryphon master at Aerie Peak. Quests you picked up for it: Gahz'rilla, The Prophecy of Mosh'aru, Troll Temper, Divino-matic Rod. Not on your path, only if you want the detour: Tiara of the Deep (Dustwallow Marsh 46, 57). The route does not come back to these hand-ins, go when it suits you: The Prophecy of Mosh'aru (Tanaris); Gahz'rilla (Thousand Needles).", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=38.7, y=20.1, dg=10, run=true},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={2865}, names={"Scarab Shells"}, zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.6, y=26.8, dg=10},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={3042}, names={"Troll Temper"}, zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.4, y=28.8, dg=10},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={2768}, names={"Divino-matic Rod"}, zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.5, dg=10},
  {t="FLY", seg=18, arg="Theramore", text="Bera Stonehammer, the Gadgetzan gryphon master (51.0, 29.3)"},
  {t="N", seg=18, arg="Take the boat from the Theramore dock to Menethil Harbor", text="Your hearthstone stays set to Gadgetzan. Keep these for later: 648 and 2767 (robots), 209 and 669 (all Booty Bay, segment 20) and 212 (Stormwind, next segment)."},
  {t="FLY", seg=19, arg="Ironforge", text="You arrive at Menethil Harbor by boat. Shellei Brondir, the gryphon master (Wetlands 9.5, 59.7)."},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=19, text="Briarthorn, the warlock trainer in the Forlorn Cavern, in the north of the city: learn everything he offers from level 42 to 46 (the route made no training stop in Kalimdor). Death Coil (42) is new: an instant that sends the enemy running for a moment and heals you, your second escape beside Howl of Terror. The demon trainer beside him sells the new pet spell books.", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=50.4, y=5.7},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={1360}, names={"Reclaimed Treasures"}, text="Krom Stoutarm in the Hall of Explorers. His chest is in the North Common Hall, before the dungeon portal.", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=74.2, y=9.4, dg=9},
  {t="N", seg=19, arg="Optional dungeon: Uldaman, levels 41-51", text="The main entrance is the dig site in the north of the Badlands; a back entrance is further east (Badlands 65.2, 43.5). Before the portal, Hammertoe Grez continues A Sign of Hope into Amulet of Secrets, and Prospector Ironband's Agmond's Fate (Loch Modan) wants urns from the dig. Inside: the three lost dwarves, the Shattered Necklace chain (Talvash del Kissel in Ironforge) and, after the last boss, The Platinum Discs for High Explorer Magellas in Ironforge. Quests you picked up for it: Reclaimed Treasures, Uldaman Reagent Run, Power Stones, Solution to Doom. Needs an earlier quest chain this route does not do: A Sign of Hope. The route does not come back to these hand-ins, go when it suits you: Power Stones (Badlands); Solution to Doom (Badlands); Uldaman Reagent Run (Loch Modan).", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=44.6, y=12.1, dg=9, run=true},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={1360}, names={"Reclaimed Treasures"}, zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=74.2, y=9.4, dg=9},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={2279}, names={"The Platinum Discs"}, text="The Platinum Discs: High Explorer Magellas in the Hall of Explorers.", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=62.3, y=24.1, dg=9},
  {t="N", seg=19, arg="Buy 15 Silk Cloth and one Mithril Casing at the Ironforge auction house", text="The silk is for Caught! in the Searing Gorge (it is not a drop there). The Mithril Casing is an engineering part you need in Un'Goro Crater in segment 21; an engineer can also make it. If there is none, try again on your next two stops here."},
  {t="FLY", seg=19, arg="Southshore", text="Gryth Thurden, the Ironforge gryphon master"},
  {t="N", seg=19, arg="Ride north-east from Southshore past Durnholde Keep and up the mountain path into the Hinterlands, to Aerie Peak", text="The path starts in the hills north-east of Durnholde and comes out at the west end of the Hinterlands, right below Aerie Peak.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=11.1, y=46.2},
  {t="F", seg=19, arg="Aerie Peak", text="Guthrum Thunderfist", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=11.1, y=46.2},
  {t="S", seg=19, arg="Aerie Peak", text="Innkeeper Thulfram (14.2, 41.6). The hearthstone stays here for the rest of this segment."},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={2880,2877}, names={"Troll Necklace Bounty","Skulk Rock Clean-up"}, text="Fraggar Thundermantle", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=14.8, y=44.6},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={2988}, names={"Witherbark Cages"}, text="Gryphon Master Talonaxe, at the gryphon roost (9.8, 44.5)", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=9.8, y=44.5},
  {t="N", seg=19, arg="Keep any OOX-09/HL Distress Beacon that drops in the Hinterlands", text="Trolls, oozes and most beasts can drop it (about 1 in 100). It starts the third robot escort, later in this loop."},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={2988}, names={"Witherbark Cages"}, text="Ride south-east to the two Witherbark villages. The first and second cage stand in Zun'watha (23.3, 58.8), the third in Hiri'watha (32.0, 57.3): click each. Witherbark trolls (40-43) drop Troll Tribal Necklaces: kill what stands in your way and loot.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=23.2, y=58.8, path={{9.7,49.0},{10.9,52.2},{17.7,54.6},{21.7,52.8},{23.7,55.2}}},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={2988}, names={"Witherbark Cages"}, text="Back at Aerie Peak: Gryphon Master Talonaxe", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=9.8, y=44.5, path={{23.7,55.2},{21.7,52.8},{17.7,54.6},{10.9,52.2},{9.7,49.0}}},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={2989}, names={"The Altar of Zul"}, text="Gryphon Master Talonaxe", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=9.8, y=44.5},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={2989}, names={"The Altar of Zul"}, text="Ride east along the road, then south to the Altar of Zul. Climb the stairs to the top: the quest ticks when you reach it. Vilebranch trolls (45-47) stand around the foot; two level 50 Keepers stand on top. Pull them down one at a time, or run up, take the credit and run back down. Stay out of Jintha'Alor, the terraced city further east: it is elite.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=49.0, y=68.7, path={{9.7,49.0},{11.3,52.5},{17.7,54.6},{21.7,52.8},{24.9,57.0},{24.9,58.8},{26.8,62.1},{41.6,63.3},{44.0,67.5}}},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={2880}, names={"Troll Necklace Bounty"}, text="Finish the 5 Troll Tribal Necklaces on the Vilebranch Scalpers, Soothsayers and Axe Throwers around the altar. Kill the Soothsayers first: they heal and a warlock has no interrupt, so put Curse of Tongues on them and burn them down, or Fear one when no other troll is near.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=47.0, y=66.0},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={2877}, names={"Skulk Rock Clean-up"}, text="Ride north to Skulk Rock. 10 Green Sludges (46-47) lie around the rock and along the stream west of it, 10 Jade Oozes (47-48) in and around the cave. They are slow: let the Voidwalker hold one and step back when you need to bandage or Drain Life.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=53.2, y=43.9},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={485}, names={"Find OOX-09/HL!"}, text="Right-click the OOX-09/HL Distress Beacon if one has dropped: the robot stands at the head of the river just north-west of Skulk Rock. No beacon? Kill oozes a while longer; if you give up, skip these four robot steps (An OOX of Your Own in segment 20 then drops out too).", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=49.4, y=37.7},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={485}, names={"Find OOX-09/HL!"}, text="Homing Robot OOX-09/HL", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=49.4, y=37.7},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={836}, names={"Rescue OOX-09/HL!"}, text="Homing Robot OOX-09/HL", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=49.4, y=37.7},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={836}, names={"Rescue OOX-09/HL!"}, text="Escort the robot east across the zone to the shore below the Overlook Cliffs. A long walk: stay off your Felsteed; when ambushers jump it, send the Voidwalker onto them so they leave the robot alone. You hand it in at Booty Bay in segment 20.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=79.0, y=61.0, path={{50.2,36.4},{51.4,41.5},{52.8,41.5},{59.8,49.6},{67.2,47.8},{69.4,51.0},{75.7,51.0},{79.1,55.8}}},
  {t="H", seg=19, arg="Aerie Peak", text="Use your hearthstone."},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={2989}, names={"The Altar of Zul"}, text="Gryphon Master Talonaxe", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=9.8, y=44.5},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={2990}, names={"Thadius Grimshade"}, text="Gryphon Master Talonaxe. The feather goes to Nethergarde Keep, at the end of this segment.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=9.8, y=44.5},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={2880,2877}, names={"Troll Necklace Bounty","Skulk Rock Clean-up"}, text="Fraggar Thundermantle", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=14.8, y=44.6},
  {t="FLY", seg=19, arg="Ironforge", text="Guthrum Thunderfist. In Ironforge, buy the 15 Silk Cloth now if you had none before."},
  {t="FLY", seg=19, arg="Thelsamar", text="Gryth Thurden"},
  {t="N", seg=19, arg="Ride south through Loch Modan into the Badlands, west across the Badlands, and out of its west end into the Searing Gorge", text="Stay away from Kargath, the Horde outpost in the north-west Badlands. The pass at the west end climbs into the south-east corner of the Searing Gorge; the Wooden Outhouse stands a short ride north-west of it, at the Grimesilt Dig Site.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=65.6, y=62.2},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={4449}, names={"Caught!"}, text="The Wooden Outhouse (65.6, 62.2): someone is locked inside", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=65.6, y=62.2},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={4449}, names={"Caught!"}, text="Kill 8 Dark Iron Geologists (43-44) at the dig site right next to the outhouse. The 15 Silk Cloth come from your bags.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=63.3, y=60.5},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={4449}, names={"Caught!"}, text="The Wooden Outhouse", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=65.6, y=62.2},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={4450}, names={"Ledger from Tanaris"}, text="The Wooden Outhouse", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=65.6, y=62.2},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={4450}, obj={1}, names={"Ledger from Tanaris"}, text="Take the Goodsteel Ledger that is pushed out under the outhouse door.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=65.5, y=62.2},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={4450}, obj={2}, names={"Ledger from Tanaris"}, text="20 Solid Crystal Leg Shafts: Glassweb Spiders (43-45) on the ridge north of the outhouse (66-69, 45-53) and in the gullies south-west of it (60-64, 68-71). Most kills drop one. The other two items on the ledger come later: Jarquia in the Swamp of Sorrows (this segment) and a crate in Dustwallow Marsh (segment 21).", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=66.5, y=50.0},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={3367}, names={"Suntara Stones"}, text="Dorius Stonetender lies wounded at the dig site (63.9, 61.0)", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=63.9, y=61.0},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={3367}, names={"Suntara Stones"}, text="Walk with Dorius: he heads north along the east ridge. Dark Iron dwarves ambush him near the end: send the Voidwalker onto the attackers and kill them one by one; you cannot heal him. When he falls, a Singed Letter stays behind (74.4, 19.3): click it.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=74.4, y=19.3},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={3368}, names={"Suntara Stones"}, text="From the Singed Letter. It goes to Ironforge.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=74.4, y=19.3},
  {t="N", seg=19, arg="Ride west along the north ridge to Thorium Point", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=37.9, y=30.9},
  {t="F", seg=19, arg="Thorium Point", text="Lanie Reed", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=37.9, y=30.9},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={7728,7729}, names={"STOLEN: Smithing Tuyere and Lookout's Spyglass","JOB OPPORTUNITY: Culling the Competition"}, text="The Wanted/Missing/Lost & Found board (37.6, 26.5)", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=37.6, y=26.5},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={7723,7724,7727}, names={"Curse These Fat Fingers","Fiery Menace!","Incendosaurs? Whateverosaur is More Like It"}, text="Hansel Heavyhands", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=38.6, y=27.8},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={7722}, names={"What the Flux?"}, text="Master Smith Burninate", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=38.8, y=28.5},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={3377}, names={"Prayer to Elune"}, text="Zamael Lunthistle, in a cage west of Thorium Point (29.6, 26.3). Listen to his tale.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=29.6, y=26.3},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={3377}, names={"Prayer to Elune"}, text="Zamael Lunthistle. His next quest goes to Darnassus: leave it.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=29.6, y=26.3},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={3441}, names={"Divine Retribution"}, text="Kalaran Windblade, south of Thorium Point at the edge of the Cauldron (39.1, 39.0). Listen to his story.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=39.1, y=39.0},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={3441}, names={"Divine Retribution"}, text="Kalaran Windblade", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=39.1, y=39.0},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={3442}, names={"The Flawless Flame"}, text="Kalaran Windblade", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=39.1, y=39.0},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={7723,3442}, names={"Curse These Fat Fingers","The Flawless Flame"}, text="Circle the outside of the Cauldron. 20 Heavy War Golems (47-49) walk around its rim and drop Golem Oil; Magma Elementals (46-48, south-east of the Cauldron) and Inferno Elementals (47-49, south-west) drop the Hearts of Flame. You need 4 oil and 4 hearts. Fire does nothing to the fire elementals: leave Immolate off them and use Corruption, Curse of Agony and Shadow Bolt. If a second elemental joins, Banish it until the first is dead.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=40.8, y=49.2},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={7724}, names={"Fiery Menace!"}, text="20 Greater Lava Spiders (47-49) on the plateaus and lava pools in the south-west of the gorge.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=27.0, y=60.0},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={3442}, names={"The Flawless Flame"}, text="Kalaran Windblade", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=39.1, y=39.0},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={3443}, names={"Forging the Shaft"}, text="Kalaran Windblade", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=39.1, y=39.0},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={7729,3443}, names={"JOB OPPORTUNITY: Culling the Competition","Forging the Shaft"}, text="Go down into the Cauldron. 15 Dark Iron Taskmasters and 15 Dark Iron Slavers (45-48) stand over the slaves on the ramps and in the Slag Pit; they and the other Dark Iron dwarves drop the 8 Thorium Plated Daggers. Voidwalker first and pull to the edge; do not Fear on the ramps, a feared dwarf comes back with the next group. If a Grimesilt Outhouse Key drops, keep it.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=42.6, y=40.0},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={7728}, names={"STOLEN: Smithing Tuyere and Lookout's Spyglass"}, text="The Smithing Tuyere drops from Dark Iron Steamsmiths (38-43, 48-52), the Lookout's Spyglass from Dark Iron Lookouts on the south side of the Cauldron (42, 58): about 1 in 10 each.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=41.0, y=54.0},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={7727}, names={"Incendosaurs? Whateverosaur is More Like It"}, text="20 Incendosaurs (47-49) in the lava pools inside the Slag Pit, the mine whose entrances are in the Cauldron walls. They breathe fire: fight one at a time, at full health.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=48.4, y=28.0},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={7722}, names={"What the Flux?"}, text="The Secret Plans: Fiery Flux lie deep in the Slag Pit, beside Overseer Maltorius (level 50 elite). Clear the dwarves around him first. If he is too strong for you, pull him away from the plans, run (Death Coil or Howl of Terror buys the first seconds), and loot them when he resets; or skip this quest.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=40.5, y=35.7},
  {t="N", seg=19, arg="Look for Chambermaid Pillaclencher in the Slag Pit: she drops Chambermaid Pillaclencher's Pillow", text="Right-click the pillow to start Look at the Size of It!. The data has no position for her: if you do not find her, skip the two pillow steps below."},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={4451}, names={"The Key to Freedom"}, text="Only if a Grimesilt Outhouse Key dropped (about 3 in 100 from the Cauldron dwarves): right-click it to start The Key to Freedom, then ride back east to the Wooden Outhouse. No key? Skip this step and the next.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=65.6, y=62.2},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={4451}, names={"The Key to Freedom"}, text="The Wooden Outhouse", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=65.6, y=62.2},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={3443}, names={"Forging the Shaft"}, text="Kalaran Windblade. His next quest, The Flame's Casing, is elite: leave it.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=39.1, y=39.0},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={7728,7729}, names={"STOLEN: Smithing Tuyere and Lookout's Spyglass","JOB OPPORTUNITY: Culling the Competition"}, text="Back at Thorium Point: Taskmaster Scrange", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=39.0, y=27.5},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={7723,7724,7727}, names={"Curse These Fat Fingers","Fiery Menace!","Incendosaurs? Whateverosaur is More Like It"}, text="Hansel Heavyhands", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=38.6, y=27.8},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={7722}, names={"What the Flux?"}, text="Master Smith Burninate", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=38.8, y=28.5},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={7704}, names={"Look at the Size of It!"}, text="Right-click Chambermaid Pillaclencher's Pillow, if you found it.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=38.4, y=27.7},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={7704}, names={"Look at the Size of It!"}, text="Evonice Sootsmoker", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=38.4, y=27.7},
  {t="L", seg=19, lvl=47, text="Short of 47? Kill Heavy War Golems and elementals around the Cauldron rim, just south of Thorium Point, until level 47. The Blasted Lands animals later in this segment are level 45-52.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=38.0, y=44.0},
  {t="FLY", seg=19, arg="Ironforge", text="Lanie Reed"},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={3368}, names={"Suntara Stones"}, text="Curator Thorius in the Hall of Explorers (71.5, 15.7). Leave his next quest, Dwarven Justice.", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=71.5, y=15.7},
  {t="N", seg=19, arg="Still no Mithril Casing? Check the auction house once more", text="Then take the Deeprun Tram from Tinker Town to Stormwind."},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={212}, names={"A Meal Served Cold"}, text="Angus Stern in the Blue Recluse, Mage Quarter (51.8, 93.6). This quest has a 30-minute timer and you took it in segment 15: if it shows as failed in your log, it cannot be handed in. Abandon it and skip this step.", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=51.8, y=93.6},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={1477}, names={"Vital Supplies"}, text="High Sorcerer Andromath, at the top of the mage tower (48.7, 87.6)", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=48.7, y=87.6},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={1363}, names={"Mazen's Behest"}, text="Mazen Mac'Nadir, in the Mage Quarter (51.8, 74.2)", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=51.8, y=74.2},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={1363}, names={"Mazen's Behest"}, text="Acolyte Dellis, next to him", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=51.4, y=73.8},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={1364}, names={"Mazen's Behest"}, text="Acolyte Dellis", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=51.4, y=73.8},
  {t="FLY", seg=19, arg="Darkshire", text="Dungar Longdrink, the Stormwind gryphon master (71.0, 72.5)"},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={1477}, names={"Vital Supplies"}, text="Watchmaster Sorigal (75.8, 46.2)", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=75.8, y=46.2},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={1395}, names={"Supplies for Nethergarde"}, text="Watchmaster Sorigal. The crate goes to Nethergarde Keep.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=75.8, y=46.2},
  {t="N", seg=19, arg="Ride east out of Darkshire, through Deadwind Pass, into the Swamp of Sorrows", text="Stay on the road through Deadwind Pass. Watcher Biggs stands by the road just inside the swamp.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=26.7, y=59.8},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={1398}, names={"Driftwood"}, text="Watcher Biggs", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=26.7, y=59.8},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={1364}, names={"Mazen's Behest"}, text="Khadgar's Essays drop from the swamp plants: Swampwalkers (north-west of Biggs, 28, 37) and Tangled Horrors (all over the middle and east of the swamp). About 1 in 20, and they are grey to you, so kill every one you pass on the way east. Keep north of the road around Stonard (45, 55): it is a Horde town with level 56 guards.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=58.4, y=47.1},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={1398}, names={"Driftwood"}, text="8 Sundried Driftwood: pieces of wood lying on the beach of Misty Reed Strand, the east coast.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=89.4, y=53.0},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={4450}, obj={4}, names={"Ledger from Tanaris"}, text="Jarquia (46), a named murloc off the same beach (94.8, 52.0), drops Goodsteel's Balanced Flameberge for the ledger.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=94.8, y=52.0},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={1398}, names={"Driftwood"}, text="Ride back west to Watcher Biggs. Still no essays? Kill Tangled Horrors on the way; if they have not dropped by the time you reach him, abandon Mazen's Behest.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=26.7, y=59.8},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={1425}, names={"Deliver the Shipment"}, text="Watcher Biggs", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=26.7, y=59.8},
  {t="N", seg=19, arg="Ride south from Watcher Biggs into the Blasted Lands and on to Nethergarde Keep", text="The keep is on the hill in the north-east, just past the zone border.", zone="Blasted Lands", map=1419, x=65.5, y=24.3},
  {t="F", seg=19, arg="Nethergarde Keep", text="Alexandra Constantine", zone="Blasted Lands", map=1419, x=65.5, y=24.3},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={1395,1425}, names={"Supplies for Nethergarde","Deliver the Shipment"}, text="Quartermaster Lungertz (66.5, 21.4)", zone="Blasted Lands", map=1419, x=66.5, y=21.4},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={1364}, names={"Mazen's Behest"}, text="Watcher Mahar Ba, in the mage tower (67.7, 19.2)", zone="Blasted Lands", map=1419, x=67.7, y=19.2},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={2990}, names={"Thadius Grimshade"}, text="Thadius Grimshade, in the same tower (66.9, 19.5). He offers Nekrum's Medallion, which needs Zul'Farrak: leave it.", zone="Blasted Lands", map=1419, x=66.9, y=19.5},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={2581,2583,2585}, names={"Snickerfang Jowls","A Boar's Vitality","The Decisive Striker"}, text="Ride west along the north edge of the Blasted Lands to the two blood elves on the hill (50.6, 14.3): Bloodmage Drazial", zone="Blasted Lands", map=1419, x=50.5, y=14.2},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={2601,2603}, names={"The Basilisk's Bite","Vulture's Vigor"}, text="Bloodmage Lynnore, next to him", zone="Blasted Lands", map=1419, x=50.6, y=14.3},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={2581,2583,2585,2601,2603}, names={"Snickerfang Jowls","A Boar's Vitality","The Decisive Striker","The Basilisk's Bite","Vulture's Vigor"}, text="Farm all five together. You need 5 Snickerfang Jowls, 6 Blasted Boar Lungs, 6 Scorpok Pincers, 11 Basilisk Brains and 14 Vulture Gizzards in all. The lowest sources: Starving Snickerfangs (45-46) and Scorpok Stingers (50-51) just south of the bloodmages (44-57, 14-30); Ashmane Boars (48-49), Redstone Basilisks (46-48) and Black Slayers (46-48) south-west of Nethergarde (55-63, 26-37). Drop rates are 30-40 in 100, so this takes a while: treat it as your grind. Scorpoks poison, and a warlock cannot cure it: bandage, Drain Life and eat. If you run out of patience, hand in what is complete and abandon the rest.", zone="Blasted Lands", map=1419, x=55.0, y=28.0},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={2581,2583,2585}, names={"Snickerfang Jowls","A Boar's Vitality","The Decisive Striker"}, text="Bloodmage Drazial", zone="Blasted Lands", map=1419, x=50.5, y=14.2},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={2601,2603}, names={"The Basilisk's Bite","Vulture's Vigor"}, text="Bloodmage Lynnore", zone="Blasted Lands", map=1419, x=50.6, y=14.3},
  {t="N", seg=19, arg="Ride back east to Nethergarde Keep", text="The next segment (20) starts with the flight to Booty Bay. Your hearthstone is still set to Aerie Peak. Keep these for Booty Bay: 209, 669, 648, 836, 2767; and 4450 for Gadgetzan.", zone="Blasted Lands", map=1419, x=65.5, y=24.3},
  {t="N", seg=19, arg="Optional dungeon: Sunken Temple, levels 50-60", text="The temple is in the lake in the middle of the Swamp of Sorrows: swim down through the sunken doorway and follow the halls to the portal. Brohann Caskbelly in Stormwind gives Into The Temple of Atal'Hakkar (10 Atal'ai Tablets), after Rhapsody's Tale from the Hinterlands. Not on your path, only if you want the detour: Jammal'an the Prophet (The Hinterlands 34, 75). Needs an earlier quest chain this route does not do: The God Hakkar.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=69.9, y=53.5, dg=12, run=true},
  {t="FLY", seg=20, arg="Booty Bay", text="Alexandra Constantine, the Nethergarde Keep gryphon master. The flight goes by Darkshire."},
  {t="S", seg=20, arg="Booty Bay", text="Innkeeper Skindle (27.0, 77.3)"},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={2767,648,836}, names={"Rescue OOX-22/FE!","Rescue OOX-17/TN!","Rescue OOX-09/HL!"}, text="Oglethorpe Obnoticus, the gnome engineer (28.4, 76.3). Hand in each robot you rescued.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.4, y=76.3},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3721}, names={"An OOX of Your Own"}, text="Oglethorpe Obnoticus offers An OOX of Your Own only if you rescued all three robots. Missed one? Skip this step and the next.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.4, y=76.3},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3721}, names={"An OOX of Your Own"}, text="Oglethorpe Obnoticus", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.4, y=76.3},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={669}, names={"Sunken Treasure"}, text="Fleet Master Seahorn (27.2, 77.0). Leave the second Sunken Treasure.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.2, y=77.0},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={604}, names={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers"}, text="Fleet Master Seahorn", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.2, y=77.0},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={609}, names={"Voodoo Dues"}, text="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley (27.8, 77.1)", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.8, y=77.1},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={621}, names={"Zanzil's Secret"}, text="Crank Fizzlebub, next to the innkeeper (27.1, 77.2)", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.1, y=77.2},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={617}, names={"Akiris by the Bundle"}, text="Privateer Bloads (26.8, 76.4)", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.8, y=76.4},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={587}, names={"Up to Snuff"}, text="Deeg (26.9, 77.3)", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.9, y=77.3},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={576}, names={"Keep An Eye Out"}, text="Dizzy One-Eye (28.6, 75.9)", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.6, y=75.9},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={348}, names={"Stranglethorn Fever"}, text="Fin Fizracket, lying sick (27.6, 76.7)", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.6, y=76.7},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={617}, names={"Akiris by the Bundle"}, text="Leave Booty Bay through the tunnel and ride north-west to the coast. Naga Explorers (43-44) on the beach and in the shallows (24-28, 59-65) drop the 10 Bundles of Akiris Reed, about 1 in 3.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.2, y=62.0},
  {t="N", seg=20, arg="Get a Gorilla Fang from the Elder Mistvale Gorillas", text="Mistvale Valley, just east of the naga beach. Elder Mistvale Gorillas (40-41) and Silverback Patriarchs (42-43) drop it. You need one for the witch doctor.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.9, y=64.6},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={348}, names={"Stranglethorn Fever"}, text="Witch Doctor Unbagwa stands in a small cave at the north end of the valley (35.3, 60.4). Give him the Gorilla Fang: he summons three gorillas, one after another. The last, Mokk the Savage (44), drops the Heart of Mokk. Rest to full, make a Healthstone and heal the Voidwalker up before you talk to him: the three come without a break. Send the Voidwalker onto each gorilla, then Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate and Drain Life; between two gorillas use Health Funnel on the Voidwalker and Life Tap only if your health allows it.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.3, y=60.4},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={609}, obj={3}, names={"Voodoo Dues"}, text="Ride east to the Ruins of Aboraz. Chucky \"Ten Thumbs\" (43-44) stands in the ruins and drops Chucky's Huge Ring.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=40.0, y=58.2},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={621}, names={"Zanzil's Secret"}, text="Zanzil's Zombies, Hunters, Witch Doctors and Naga (43-44) in and around the Ruins of Aboraz drop the 12 Zanzil's Mixture, about 1 in 3. They stand close together: send the Voidwalker onto one from as far away as you can and fight where it comes to you. Kill the Witch Doctors first with Curse of Tongues on them (a warlock has no interrupt). Do not Fear in the ruins: a feared mob brings the rest. If too many come, Howl of Terror and run.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=38.2, y=56.0},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={609}, obj={1}, names={"Voodoo Dues"}, text="Ride north-west to the Ruins of Jubuwal. Maury \"Club Foot\" Wilkins drops Maury's Clubbed Foot.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.3, y=51.3},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={609}, obj={2}, names={"Voodoo Dues"}, text="Jon-Jon the Crow stands next to him and drops Jon-Jon's Golden Spyglass. Fight the two one at a time: Voidwalker on the one you pulled, DoTs, Drain Life. If both come, the Voidwalker holds one and you Fear the other once the zombies near them are dead. The zombies around them also drop mixture.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=34.9, y=51.8},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={209}, names={"Skullsplitter Tusks"}, text="Ride north-east to the Skullsplitter troll ruins east of the road (42-48, 33-44). Every Skullsplitter troll drops tusks, about 1 in 5: you need 18. They are level 39-44 and pay little experience now: if you would rather not ride there, abandon Skullsplitter Tusks and skip its hand-in.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=45.6, y=40.0},
  {t="H", seg=20, arg="Booty Bay", text="Use your Hearthstone: it saves the long ride back south."},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={209}, names={"Skullsplitter Tusks"}, text="Kebok (27.0, 77.1)", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.0, y=77.1},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={617}, names={"Akiris by the Bundle"}, text="Privateer Bloads. Leave the second Akiris by the Bundle.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.8, y=76.4},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={609}, names={"Voodoo Dues"}, text="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley. His next quest, Cracking Maury's Foot, is elite: leave it.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.8, y=77.1},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={621}, names={"Zanzil's Secret"}, text="Crank Fizzlebub", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.1, y=77.2},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={348}, names={"Stranglethorn Fever"}, text="Fin Fizracket", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.6, y=76.7},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={604}, names={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers"}, text="The Bloodsail camp on the Wild Shore, the beach south of Booty Bay. Kill 10 Bloodsail Swashbucklers (41-43); the Bloodsail Charts and the Bloodsail Orders are papers lying in the camp (27.2, 82.7 and 27.7, 83.1). Every pirate can drop Snuff for Deeg and Dizzy's Eye: loot them all. Kill the Bloodsail Warlocks first: Curse of Tongues on them, Voidwalker on the pirate beside them. Fear a second pirate only at the edge of the camp, never towards the tents.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.3, y=82.8},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={604}, names={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers"}, text="Back in Booty Bay: Fleet Master Seahorn", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.2, y=77.0},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={608}, names={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers"}, text="Fleet Master Seahorn", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.2, y=77.0},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={594}, names={"Message in a Bottle"}, text="Leave through the tunnel and go down to the beach east of Booty Bay. Open a Half-Buried Bottle on the sand (they lie all along this coast) and right-click the Carefully Folded Note inside.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.8, y=78.7},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={594}, names={"Message in a Bottle"}, text="Swim south-east to Jaguero Isle: Princess Poobah (38.5, 80.6). Skymane Gorillas (50) roam the isle and King Mukla (51 elite) is at its south end: go straight to her. Her next quest is elite: leave it.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=38.5, y=80.6},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={608}, names={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers"}, text="Swim west to the three Bloodsail ships anchored off the Wild Shore. Captain Stillwater (45-46) is on the eastern ship (32.9, 88.2), Captain Keelhaul (46-47) on the western one (29.3, 88.3), Fleet Master Firallon (48) on the southern one (30.6, 90.6). In Classic each captain stands in his ship's cabin with one or two guards: clear the deck first, pull the guards out one at a time with the Voidwalker and start every captain at full health and mana, with a Healthstone in the bag and your Soulstone on yourself. Voidwalker on the captain, then Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate and Drain Life; Health Funnel keeps the Voidwalker up. If a guard comes too, Fear him (the deck is clear by then) or kill him first while the Voidwalker holds the captain. If it goes badly: Death Coil or Howl of Terror, then jump off the ship and eat or bandage.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=30.9, y=89.0},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={587,576}, names={"Up to Snuff","Keep An Eye Out"}, text="The ship crews drop the rest of the 15 Snuff and Dizzy's Eye.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=30.9, y=89.0},
  {t="L", seg=20, lvl=50, text="The second big grind of the route. Stay on the three ships (Bloodsail Sea Dogs, Elder Magi and deckhands, 43-48; they respawn fast) until level 50. Voidwalker first, DoT two or three pirates at once and Drain Life the one on you; Curse of Tongues on the Elder Magi; Drain Soul a last hit now and then so you always carry 3-5 Soul Shards. For a change of scene: Zanzil's undead at the Ruins of Aboraz (38, 56). Mobs here are turning green, so it is slow: you can also stop early and finish this level on the Dunemaul ogres in Tanaris (46-48) or in Un'Goro Crater at the start of the next segment, where Bungle in the Jungle needs level 50.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=30.9, y=89.0},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={608}, names={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers"}, text="Back in Booty Bay: Fleet Master Seahorn", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.2, y=77.0},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={587}, names={"Up to Snuff"}, text="Deeg", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.9, y=77.3},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={576}, names={"Keep An Eye Out"}, text="Dizzy One-Eye", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.6, y=75.9},
  {t="N", seg=20, arg="No Mithril Casing yet? Look for one before you sail", text="You need it for A-Me 01 in Un'Goro Crater. Booty Bay and Gadgetzan had auction houses in Classic; an engineer can make one."},
  {t="N", seg=20, arg="Take the boat from the Booty Bay dock to Ratchet", text="Your hearthstone stays set to Booty Bay until Gadgetzan. Keep 4450 Ledger from Tanaris."},
  {t="FLY", seg=21, arg="Theramore", text="You arrive at Ratchet by boat. Bragok, the Ratchet flight master (The Barrens 63.1, 37.2). This detour is for the last item on Goodsteel's ledger."},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4450}, obj={3}, names={"Ledger from Tanaris"}, text="Ride west out of Theramore into the marsh to the Damaged Crate (54.1, 55.9) and take the Overdue Package from it. Then ride back to Theramore.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=54.1, y=55.9},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={2846}, names={"Tiara of the Deep"}, zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=46.1, y=57.1, dg=10},
  {t="FLY", seg=21, arg="Gadgetzan", text="Baldruc, the Theramore gryphon master (67.5, 51.3)"},
  {t="S", seg=21, arg="Gadgetzan", text="Innkeeper Fizzgrimble"},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4450}, names={"Ledger from Tanaris"}, text="Krinkle Goodsteel, the blacksmith (51.5, 28.8). He wants the ledger, 20 Solid Crystal Leg Shafts, the Overdue Package and Goodsteel's Balanced Flameberge. Missing one? Abandon the quest and skip this step.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.5, y=28.8},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4496}, names={"Bungle in the Jungle"}, text="Alchemist Pestlezugg. Needs level 50: if you left Stranglethorn at 49, take it on your next Gadgetzan stop instead (it is handed in there in segment 22 anyway).", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.9, y=27.0},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4504}, names={"Super Sticky"}, text="Tran'rek", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.6, y=26.8},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Optional dungeon: Maraudon, levels 46-55", text="Maraudon is in the west of Desolace; fly to Nijel's Point and ride south-west. Inside the outer caves, before the portals, Cavindra gives Legends of Maraudon. Quests you picked up for it: Shadowshard Fragments. Not on your path, only if you want the detour: Vyletongue Corruption (Desolace 68, 9); Corruption of Earth and Seed (Desolace 64, 11); Twisted Evils (Desolace 62, 40); The Pariah's Instructions (Desolace 50, 87). The route does not come back to these hand-ins, go when it suits you: Shadowshard Fragments (Dustwallow Marsh).", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=29.1, y=62.5, dg=11, run=true},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Optional dungeon: Alcaz Prison, levels 48-53", text="New Forever dungeon, not checked in game yet. It is on Alcaz Island, off the north-east coast of Dustwallow Marsh, a short swim from Theramore. Its Alliance quests include The Secret Prison and Somber News (Sully McCleary, Dustwallow Marsh) and The Dragon's Journal (Archmage Lan'dalock in Dalaran, Alterac Mountains 15.3, 73.8); the other givers are not published yet. Ask around Theramore and take what is offered: the addon logs it so these steps can be filled in.", dg=16, run=true},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Ride south-west across Tanaris and down the ramp into Un'Goro Crater", text="In Classic the ramp is in the west wall of Tanaris, past Thistleshrub Valley; it comes out in the south-east of the crater. Torwa Pathfinder, a tauren, stands at the bottom. Devilsaurs (54-56 elite) walk the whole crater: look around before every pull and keep well away from them.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4290,4289}, names={"The Fare of Lar'korwi","The Apes of Un'Goro"}, text="Torwa Pathfinder", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={3844}, names={"It's a Secret to Everybody"}, text="A Wrecked Raft at the edge of the pond west of Torwa (63.0, 68.6)", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=63.0, y=68.6, path={{71.4,69.3},{69.2,69.3},{65.4,65.7},{63.6,65.7}}},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={3844}, names={"It's a Secret to Everybody"}, text="A Small Pack, in the water of the same pond (63.1, 69.1)", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=63.1, y=69.1},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={3845}, names={"It's a Secret to Everybody"}, text="From the pack", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=63.1, y=69.1},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4290}, names={"The Fare of Lar'korwi"}, text="Ride north along the east wall to the Fresh Threshadon Carcass and take a piece. Ravasaur Hunters and Venomhide Ravasaurs (49-51) hunt around it. Send the Voidwalker first so it takes the bites. The Venomhides poison you and a warlock cannot cure it: Drain Life during the fight, bandage and eat after it.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=68.7, y=56.7},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4290}, names={"The Fare of Lar'korwi"}, text="Back to Torwa Pathfinder", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4291}, names={"The Scent of Lar'korwi"}, text="Torwa Pathfinder", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4291}, names={"The Scent of Lar'korwi"}, text="West of Torwa, among the Ravasaurs (48-50), lie nests of ravasaur eggs. Walk up to a nest: a Lar'korwi Mate (49-50) attacks: put the Voidwalker on her, then Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate. Two mates, two Ravasaur Pheromone Glands. The data has no nest positions: look for the egg piles between Torwa and the raft pond.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=63.1, y=72.4},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4291}, names={"The Scent of Lar'korwi"}, text="Torwa Pathfinder", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4292}, names={"The Bait for Lar'korwi"}, text="Torwa Pathfinder. Lar'korwi is level 56: you summon him on your last round, after the grind.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Ride north along the east wall of the crater to Marshal's Refuge", text="The camp lies at the very north end of the crater. Loot everything on the way: any crater mob can drop A Mangled Journal (it starts a quest for Williden Marshal), and Power Crystals (red, blue, yellow, green) grow on the ground all over the crater. Pick up every crystal you pass: you will need 7 of each.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=45.2, y=5.8, path={{72.8,65.7},{76.9,59.4},{76.9,51.3},{75.5,49.3},{74.8,43.9},{67.8,33.4},{66.0,33.1},{61.4,28.0},{59.6,28.0},{54.2,21.7},{51.0,21.7},{46.2,16.0},{45.2,14.5}}},
  {t="F", seg=21, arg="Marshal's Refuge", text="Gryfe", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=45.2, y=5.8},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={3845}, names={"It's a Secret to Everybody"}, text="Linken (44.7, 8.1)", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=44.7, y=8.1},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={3908}, names={"It's a Secret to Everybody"}, text="Linken. The sword goes to Donova Snowden in Winterspring (segment 23).", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=44.7, y=8.1},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={3881}, names={"Expedition Salvation"}, text="Williden Marshal", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=44.0, y=7.1},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={3883}, names={"Alien Ecology"}, text="Hol'anyee Marshal", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.9, y=7.2},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={3882}, names={"Roll the Bones"}, text="Spark Nilminer", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.5, y=7.4},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4492}, names={"Lost!"}, text="Spraggle Frock", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.6, y=8.5},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4501}, names={"Beware of Pterrordax"}, text="The Beware of Pterrordax poster next to him (43.5, 8.4)", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.5, y=8.4},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4141}, names={"Muigin and Larion"}, text="Muigin (42.9, 9.6)", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=42.9, y=9.6},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4503}, names={"Shizzle's Flyer"}, text="Shizzle (44.2, 11.6)", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=44.2, y=11.6},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4284}, names={"Crystals of Power"}, text="J.D. Collie, at the north end of the camp (41.9, 2.7)", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=41.9, y=2.7},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4243}, names={"Chasing A-Me 01"}, text="Karna Remtravel, at the south edge of the camp (46.4, 13.4)", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=46.4, y=13.4},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4504}, names={"Super Sticky"}, text="The Lakkari Tar Pits, south-east of the Refuge. Tar Beasts and Tar Creepers (50-52) in the eastern pits drop the 12 Super Sticky Tar, about 1 in 3. The Tar Lurkers and Tar Lords (52-54) in the western pits drop it too, but leave them for later.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=56.0, y=29.5},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4243}, names={"Chasing A-Me 01"}, text="Ride north-east to Fungal Rock, the gorilla cave in the north-east corner. A-Me 01, a broken robot ape, stands inside (67.7, 16.8). Un'Goro Gorillas, Stompers and Thunderers (50-53) fill the cave: send the Voidwalker onto one at a time and let it come to you. Do not Fear inside the cave: a feared gorilla brings more.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=67.7, y=16.8},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4244}, names={"Chasing A-Me 01"}, text="A-Me 01", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=67.7, y=16.8},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4244}, names={"Chasing A-Me 01"}, text="A-Me 01: hand over the Mithril Casing. No casing? Skip this step and the escort; you can still do the pelts.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=67.7, y=16.8},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4289}, names={"The Apes of Un'Goro"}, text="2 pelts each from Un'Goro Gorillas, Stompers and Thunderers, in and around the cave. Do this before the escort so the way out is clear. U'cha (55), the named ape deeper in (68.1, 12.6), is for later.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=66.1, y=16.1},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4245}, names={"Chasing A-Me 01"}, text="A-Me 01", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=67.7, y=16.8},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4245}, names={"Chasing A-Me 01"}, text="Escort A-Me 01 out of the cave and west to Karna Remtravel. Stay on foot and close to her; gorillas attack on the way out. You cannot heal her: send the Voidwalker onto every attacker at once, DoT it and use Drain Life. If two come, the Voidwalker takes one and you kill the other on yourself with DoTs and Drain Life.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=46.4, y=13.4, path={{67.4,22.3},{54.6,22.3},{51.4,21.7}}},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4245}, names={"Chasing A-Me 01"}, text="Karna Remtravel", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=46.4, y=13.4},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4141}, names={"Muigin and Larion"}, text="Ride down the east side. Bloodpetal Lashers and Threshers (48-50) here drop the 15 Bloodpetals, about 4 in 5.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=68.0, y=35.0},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={3881}, obj={1}, names={"Expedition Salvation"}, text="The Crate of Foodstuffs stands in the wrecked camp among the bloodpetals (68.5, 36.5).", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=68.5, y=36.5},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4289}, names={"The Apes of Un'Goro"}, text="Ride on south to Torwa Pathfinder", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4301}, names={"The Mighty U'cha"}, text="Torwa Pathfinder. U'cha is level 55: last round.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4496}, names={"Bungle in the Jungle"}, text="Ride west along the south wall to the Slithering Scar, the silithid hive. Gorishi Wasps, Workers and Reavers (51-53) drop the Gorishi Scent Gland (about 1 in 12) and more than half of them drop Un'Goro Soil; the soil also comes from the dirt piles on the ground all over the crater. You need 1 gland and 5 soil.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=48.5, y=81.0},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={3883}, names={"Alien Ecology"}, text="Go down into the hive to a hatchery chamber, where larval sacs hang from the ceiling (48.7, 85.3), and use the Unused Scraping Vial there. Clear as you go and do not run past bugs: more join in the tunnels, so fight with your back to the cleared way and rest to full between pulls. Voidwalker first on every pull, never Fear down here, and keep a Healthstone; if a pull goes wrong, Howl of Terror and run back the way you came.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=48.7, y=85.3},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={3881}, obj={2}, names={"Expedition Salvation"}, text="Ride north-west to the second wrecked camp and take the Research Equipment (38.5, 66.1).", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=38.5, y=66.1},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={3882}, names={"Roll the Bones"}, text="8 Dinosaur Bones: bone piles on the ground in the south-west corner (around 33, 73). Stegodons and Diemetradons drop them too, but the Stegodons are 52-55: pick up the piles instead.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=33.3, y=73.2},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4284}, names={"Crystals of Power"}, text="Ride north-east to Fire Plume Ridge, the volcano in the middle. Power Crystals grow in clusters all around its foot (45-60, 37-58): circle it until you have 7 red, 7 blue, 7 yellow and 7 green.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=53.0, y=48.0, path={{42.8,73.2},{51.2,61.2},{54.8,59.1},{57.6,54.9},{57.6,50.4},{56.6,49.0}}},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4503}, names={"Shizzle's Flyer"}, text="Around the south foot of the ridge: Diemetradons (51-52) drop the 8 Webbed Diemetradon Scales and Pterrordax (50-52) the 8 Webbed Pterrordax Scales, about 1 in 5 each. Every Pterrordax also counts for the poster (10 needed). This is slow: it is a good part of your grind towards 52. A Pterrordax flies off at low health: keep Corruption and Curse of Agony on it so they finish it while it flees, or Drain Life it down.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=52.2, y=59.7},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Ride north to Marshal's Refuge", text="About 3 minutes on your mount, up the middle of the crater past the tar pits.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=45.2, y=5.8, path={{52.2,60.9},{53.2,60.9},{57.8,54.6},{57.8,50.4},{59.0,47.5},{57.8,44.2},{55.2,42.4},{55.2,37.0},{44.4,20.8},{44.0,16.3},{45.2,14.5}}},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={3881}, names={"Expedition Salvation"}, text="Williden Marshal", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=44.0, y=7.1},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={3884}, names={"Williden's Journal"}, text="If A Mangled Journal has dropped, right-click it now. No journal? Skip this step and the next.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=44.0, y=7.1},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={3884}, names={"Williden's Journal"}, text="Williden Marshal", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.9, y=7.1},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={3883}, names={"Alien Ecology"}, text="Hol'anyee Marshal", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.9, y=7.2},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={3882}, names={"Roll the Bones"}, text="Spark Nilminer", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.5, y=7.4},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4141}, names={"Muigin and Larion"}, text="Muigin. Leave his next quest: it sends you to Feralas.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=42.9, y=9.6},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4503}, names={"Shizzle's Flyer"}, text="Shizzle", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=44.2, y=11.6},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4284}, names={"Crystals of Power"}, text="J.D. Collie", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=41.9, y=2.7},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4285,4287,4288}, names={"The Northern Pylon","The Eastern Pylon","The Western Pylon"}, text="J.D. Collie", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=41.9, y=2.7},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4285}, names={"The Northern Pylon"}, text="The Northern Crystal Pylon, east of the Refuge (56.5, 12.5). Walk up to it and click it.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=56.5, y=12.5, path={{48.0,1.3},{52.2,1.9},{52.6,6.4}}},
  {t="L", seg=21, lvl=52, text="Short of 52? Stay on the gorillas in and around Fungal Rock (50-53) until level 52 (Voidwalker first, DoTs, Drain Life; Drain Soul a last hit now and then to keep 3-5 Soul Shards); the Tar Lurkers and Tar Lords of the western tar pits (52-54) on the way here also pay well. The targets that follow are level 55-56.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=66.1, y=16.1},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4301}, names={"The Mighty U'cha"}, text="U'cha (55), deep in Fungal Rock. Clear the gorillas near him first and start at full health and mana, with a Healthstone and your Soulstone on yourself. He hits hard: send the Voidwalker, give it a few seconds, then Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate and Drain Life, with Health Funnel on the Voidwalker when it drops low. If he turns on you: Death Coil, then Fear him (the room is clear) and bandage or drink a potion. If he is too strong, abandon The Mighty U'cha.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=68.1, y=12.6},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4287}, names={"The Eastern Pylon"}, text="Ride south along the east wall to the Eastern Crystal Pylon (77.2, 50.0). Click it.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=77.2, y=50.0},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4292}, names={"The Bait for Lar'korwi"}, text="Lar'korwi (56). Torwa describes the spot as a small trail into the mountains north of his camp, strewn with huge bones; in Classic that is the ledge right by the Eastern Pylon. Use Torwa's Pouch there: place the meat, then rub the mixture on it. Start at full health and mana, with a Healthstone and your Soulstone on yourself, and send the Voidwalker the moment he appears. Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate, then Drain Life; Health Funnel keeps the Voidwalker alive. If the Voidwalker is about to die, use its Sacrifice for the shield, then Death Coil, Fear him and drink a potion early. If he is too strong, abandon the quest.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=77.2, y=50.0},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4301}, names={"The Mighty U'cha"}, text="Ride south to Torwa Pathfinder", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4292}, names={"The Bait for Lar'korwi"}, text="Torwa Pathfinder", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4288}, names={"The Western Pylon"}, text="Ride west along the south wall, then up the west side to the Western Crystal Pylon (23.9, 59.2). Click it.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=23.9, y=59.2},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={974}, names={"Finding the Source"}, text="Krakle, the goblin at the hot springs north-east of the pylon (30.9, 50.4). Needs level 51.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=30.9, y=50.4},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4501}, names={"Beware of Pterrordax"}, text="15 Frenzied Pterrordax (51-54) fly around the hot springs and the west side of the crater. Finish the 10 Pterrordax south of Fire Plume Ridge (52, 61) if you still need them.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=31.6, y=48.6},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={974}, names={"Finding the Source"}, text="Ride east up onto Fire Plume Ridge. Right-click Krakle's Thermometer at each hot spot until one reads as the hottest; the data lists spots at 49.7, 45.6 / 54.0, 47.6 / 53.9, 55.2 / 48.1, 53.3 / 45.5, 48.5. Fire elementals guard the ridge: Immolate does nothing to them, so use Corruption, Curse of Agony, Shadow Bolt and Drain Life. Banish a second elemental and kill it when the first is dead.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=49.7, y=45.6},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={974}, names={"Finding the Source"}, text="Back down west to Krakle", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=30.9, y=50.4},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={980}, names={"The New Springs"}, text="Krakle. It goes to Donova Snowden in Winterspring (segment 23).", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=30.9, y=50.4},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4492}, names={"Lost!"}, text="Ride back up Fire Plume Ridge to Ringo (51.9, 49.8)", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=51.9, y=49.8},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4491}, names={"A Little Help From My Friends"}, text="Ringo. 25-minute timer.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=51.9, y=49.8},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4491}, names={"A Little Help From My Friends"}, text="Lead Ringo north to Marshal's Refuge. When he faints, use Spraggle's Canteen on him and he gets up again. Stay on foot beside him, keep clear of the tar pits, and send the Voidwalker onto whatever comes near.", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.6, y=8.5},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4491}, names={"A Little Help From My Friends"}, text="Spraggle Frock", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.6, y=8.5},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4501}, names={"Beware of Pterrordax"}, text="Spraggle Frock", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.6, y=8.5},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4285,4287,4288}, names={"The Northern Pylon","The Eastern Pylon","The Western Pylon"}, text="J.D. Collie", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=41.9, y=2.7},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4321}, names={"Making Sense of It"}, text="J.D. Collie", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=41.9, y=2.7},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4321}, names={"Making Sense of It"}, text="J.D. Collie, a moment later", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=41.9, y=2.7},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="You are done in the crater", text="The next segment starts here with the flight to Gadgetzan (Gryfe, 45.2, 5.8). Keep 4496 and 4504 for Gadgetzan, 3908 and 980 for Winterspring."},
  {t="FLY", seg=22, arg="Gadgetzan", text="You start at Marshal's Refuge at level 52, hearthstone set to Gadgetzan. Gryfe is the gryphon master", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=45.2, y=5.8},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={4496}, names={"Bungle in the Jungle"}, text="Alchemist Pestlezugg, Gadgetzan", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.9, y=27.0},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={4504}, names={"Super Sticky"}, text="Tran'rek, a few steps away", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.6, y=26.8},
  {t="FLY", seg=22, arg="Astranaar", text="Bera Stonehammer, the Gadgetzan gryphon master. A long flight north", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.0, y=29.3},
  {t="S", seg=22, arg="Astranaar", text="Innkeeper Kimlya, in the inn. You hearth back here from the far end of Azshara", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=37.0, y=49.2},
  {t="G", seg=22, text="Ride east along the main road through Ashenvale to its end and on into Azshara. Past Raynewood the road runs by Splintertree Post and the Warsong camps (Horde): stay on the road and keep moving. Talrendis Point is on the right just after the border", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=11.9, y=77.6},
  {t="F", seg=22, arg="Talrendis Point", text="Jarrodenus, the hippogryph master", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=11.9, y=77.6},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={5535,5536}, names={"Spiritual Unrest","A Land Filled with Hatred"}, text="Loh'atu, a few steps from the hippogryph master", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=11.4, y=78.2},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={5535}, names={"Spiritual Unrest"}, text="Shadowsong Shrine, the ruins north-east of Loh'atu: Highborne Apparitions and Lichlings. They are level 45-47 and easy; the Lichlings cast frost bolts that slow you, so put Curse of Tongues on them and kill them first while the Voidwalker holds the Apparition", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=16.3, y=70.0},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={5536}, names={"A Land Filled with Hatred"}, text="The Haldarr satyr camp, further north-east: 6 Satyrs, 2 Tricksters and 2 Felsworn. The Felsworn are casters: a warlock has no interrupt, so put Curse of Tongues on them and kill them first, Voidwalker on the satyr beside them", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=20.1, y=61.8},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={5535,5536}, names={"Spiritual Unrest","A Land Filled with Hatred"}, text="Back to Loh'atu, Talrendis Point", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=11.4, y=78.2},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={3601}, names={"Kim'jael Indeed!"}, text="Kim'jael, far to the north-east: follow the road north and then east across Azshara, past the Ruins of Eldarath, and up the hill north of the ruins. A long ride", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=53.5, y=21.8, path={{14.7,80.1},{30.4,79.8},{34.4,81.3},{39.4,73.8},{42.6,73.2},{46.6,66.6},{46.4,62.1},{44.8,59.1},{44.2,50.7},{43.2,49.3},{43.2,46.9},{45.6,42.1},{45.0,35.8},{48.0,31.6},{48.2,28.0}}},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={3601}, names={"Kim'jael Indeed!"}, text="The Thalassian Base Camp, on the bluff south-east of Kim'jael. Open the Kim'jael's Equipment crates on the ground until you have the compass, scope, stuffed chicken and wizzlegoober; each crate holds one random part, so it takes a few. The Blood Elf Surveyors and Reclaimers (51-53) cast: send the Voidwalker onto one at a time and put Curse of Tongues on it before your DoTs. If a second one comes, Fear it only when no other blood elves stand near", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=58.0, y=29.1},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={3601}, names={"Kim'jael Indeed!"}, text="Kim'jael", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=53.5, y=21.8},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={5534}, names={"Kim'jael's \"Missing\" Equipment"}, text="Kim'jael", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=53.5, y=21.8},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={5534}, names={"Kim'jael's \"Missing\" Equipment"}, text="Ride back south to the Ruins of Eldarath and kill Spitelash Sirens and Myrmidons on the east side, near the shore, until one drops Some Rune (about 1 in 12). They stand in pairs: send the Voidwalker onto the Myrmidon, put Curse of Tongues and all your DoTs on the Siren and kill her first (she casts), then Drain Life the Myrmidon. Fight at full health and rest between pairs", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=45.5, y=52.0},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={5534}, names={"Kim'jael's \"Missing\" Equipment"}, text="Ride back north to Kim'jael", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=53.5, y=21.8},
  {t="H", seg=22, arg="Astranaar", text="Use your Hearthstone. It saves the whole ride back across Azshara"},
  {t="G", seg=22, text="Ride east out of Astranaar on the main road, take the fork north after Raynewood Retreat and follow that road up into Felwood. The Emerald Sanctuary is the first camp past the border", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=50.9, y=85.0},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={8460}, names={"Timbermaw Ally"}, text="Grazle, the furbolg beside the road just south of the Emerald Sanctuary", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=50.9, y=85.0},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={4101}, names={"Cleansing Felwood"}, text="Arathandris Silversky, east of the road a little south of the camp. Her Warpwood elementals are in the far north: you do them later", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=54.1, y=86.8},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={5155}, names={"Forces of Jaedenar"}, text="Greta Mosshoof, Emerald Sanctuary", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.2, y=82.1},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={4421}, names={"The Corruption of the Jadefire"}, text="Eridan Bluewind, Emerald Sanctuary", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.4, y=81.5},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={8460}, names={"Timbermaw Ally"}, text="Deadwood Village, west of the road just south of the camp: 6 Warriors, 6 Pathfinders and 6 Gardeners. Only a few Pathfinders stand here, so kill them first when you see one. Every kill also raises Timbermaw reputation, which you need for the tunnel at the end of the segment", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=48.1, y=90.9},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={8460}, names={"Timbermaw Ally"}, text="Grazle", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=50.9, y=85.0},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={8462}, names={"Speak to Nafien"}, text="Grazle. Nafien waits at the north end of Felwood", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=50.9, y=85.0},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={4421}, obj={1}, names={"The Corruption of the Jadefire"}, text="Jadefire Glen, west of the Sanctuary: kill the 11 Jadefire Felsworn here. They cast: Voidwalker first, Curse of Tongues on each, then Corruption, Immolate and Drain Life", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=41.3, y=85.3},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={4421}, names={"The Corruption of the Jadefire"}, text="Ride north to the Ruins of Constellas, west of the road: 9 Jadefire Shadowstalkers and 9 Rogues. Both stealth, so expect to be jumped: stay near full health, keep the Voidwalker at your side so it can pull a satyr off you, carry a Healthstone and do not sit down to eat inside the ruins. Xavathras (54) stands at the west end of the ruins (32.2, 67.1): clear the satyrs next to him first, then Voidwalker, DoTs and Drain Life", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=36.0, y=67.3},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={5155}, names={"Forces of Jaedenar"}, text="Jaedenar, just north of the ruins: 4 Hounds, 4 Guardians, 6 Adepts and 6 Cultists on the path up to the cave. Stay outside Shadow Hold for now. Kill the Adepts and Cultists first, with Curse of Tongues on them. The Hounds are demons: Banish one that comes as a second enemy. Do not Fear on the path: a feared mob runs into the next group", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=37.3, y=60.8, path={{39.5,59.9}}, cave=true},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={4421}, names={"The Corruption of the Jadefire"}, text="Ride back south to Eridan Bluewind, Emerald Sanctuary", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.4, y=81.5},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={4906}, names={"Further Corruption"}, text="Eridan Bluewind. The second satyr camp is in the far north", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.4, y=81.5},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={5155}, names={"Forces of Jaedenar"}, text="Greta Mosshoof", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.2, y=82.1},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={5157}, names={"Collection of the Corrupt Water"}, text="Greta gives you an Empty Canteen", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.2, y=82.1},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={5157}, names={"Collection of the Corrupt Water"}, text="The corrupted moon well in the middle of Jaedenar. Clear the cultists around it (Voidwalker first, Curse of Tongues on the casters) and use the canteen at the well", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=35.2, y=59.8},
  {t="N", seg=22, arg="Go into Shadow Hold, the cave at the top of Jaedenar, and kill Jaedenar Darkweavers, Warlocks and Enforcers until one drops a Blood Red Key", text="A rare drop (about 1 in 30), so this is also part of the grind this segment needs. Stay in the first rooms and the first spiral down. Kill the Darkweavers and Warlocks first, with Curse of Tongues on them, while the Voidwalker holds the Enforcer; Banish a demon pet that comes with them. Pull one group at a time and never Fear in the cave; if a third mob joins, Howl of Terror and back out towards the entrance. Drain Soul some of the kills so your Soul Shards stay at 3-5. No key after 40 kills or so? Skip the next seven steps", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=37.5, y=54.0},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={5202}, names={"A Strange Red Key"}, text="Right-click the Blood Red Key", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=37.5, y=54.0},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={5202}, names={"A Strange Red Key"}, text="Captured Arko'narin, in a cage on the first level down inside Shadow Hold", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=36.2, y=55.5},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={5203}, names={"Rescue From Jaedenar"}, text="Captured Arko'narin. Get to full health before you accept: she starts walking at once", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=36.2, y=55.5},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={5203}, names={"Rescue From Jaedenar"}, text="Escort her to her equipment and then out of Shadow Hold. Demons attack her on the way; she fights well once she has her gear. You cannot heal her: until then send the Voidwalker onto every attacker, Banish a second demon and DoT the first", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=36.2, y=55.5},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={5157}, names={"Collection of the Corrupt Water"}, text="Ride back south to Greta Mosshoof, Emerald Sanctuary. Skip her follow-up: it goes to the Barrens", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.2, y=82.1},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={5203}, names={"Rescue From Jaedenar"}, text="Jessir Moonbow, Emerald Sanctuary", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.3, y=82.0},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={5204}, names={"Retribution of the Light"}, text="Jessir Moonbow", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.3, y=82.0},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={5204}, names={"Retribution of the Light"}, text="Back into Shadow Hold, deeper this time: kill the succubus Rakaiah (56). Clear the mobs near her first and start at full health and mana, with a Healthstone and your Soulstone on yourself. Send the Voidwalker, put Curse of Tongues on her, then Corruption, Immolate and Drain Life; Death Coil if she turns on you. If the way down turns out too crowded for you, abandon this quest and skip the next two steps", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=38.3, y=50.5},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={5204}, names={"Retribution of the Light"}, text="The Remains of Trey Lightforge, next to where Rakaiah stood", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=38.5, y=50.4},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={5385}, names={"The Remains of Trey Lightforge"}, text="The Remains of Trey Lightforge", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=38.5, y=50.4},
  {t="G", seg=22, text="Leave Jaedenar and ride north on the main road past Bloodvenom Falls. Next comes Shatter Scar Vale, the crater field north-east of here (around 40-46, 37-44): its infernals are elite in Classic, so follow the road around it instead of cutting across", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=42.0, y=47.0},
  {t="N", seg=22, arg="Warlock, level 50: Impsy and Niby the Almighty stand just north of here", text="Their level 50 warlock quests are optional and not routed: they send you to other zones and to a dungeon. Take them only if you want to do them on your own later", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=41.4, y=44.9},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={4906}, names={"Further Corruption"}, text="Jadefire Run, west of the road in the north: 8 Hellcallers, 8 Betrayers and 8 Tricksters. Loot every satyr: you also need 5 Jadefire Felbind in a moment. Xavaric (55) stands at the back of the camp (39.1, 22.4). Kill the Hellcallers first: they are the casters, so Curse of Tongues on them and the Voidwalker on the satyr beside them. For Xavaric: clear around him, then Voidwalker, DoTs, Drain Life", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=41.8, y=18.6},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={939}, names={"Flute of Xavaric"}, text="Xavaric drops the Flute of Xavaric: right-click it. Stay until you have 5 Jadefire Felbind from the satyrs here (about 1 in 4 drops one)", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=39.1, y=22.4},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={4101}, names={"Cleansing Felwood"}, text="Irontree Cavern, across the road to the north-east: Warpwood Moss Flayers and Shredders drop the 15 Blood Amber, nearly every kill. They are elementals: when two come, Banish one and kill the other. Dessecus, a rare elemental, can be up at the south-east end (around 58, 22): leave him unless you feel strong", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=56.8, y=18.9, path={{42.2,22.0},{44.2,24.7},{48.8,20.5},{51.4,20.8},{55.4,24.1},{56.8,22.0},{56.5,16.5}}, cave=true},
  {t="F", seg=22, arg="Talonbranch Glade", text="Mishellena, the hippogryph master, just east of Irontree Cavern. You will not need it today, but it links Felwood for later", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=62.5, y=24.2, path={{61.8,18.4},{63.4,20.8}}},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={5385}, names={"The Remains of Trey Lightforge"}, text="Ride all the way back south to Jessir Moonbow, Emerald Sanctuary (go around Shatter Scar Vale again)", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.3, y=82.0},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={4906}, names={"Further Corruption"}, text="Eridan Bluewind", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.4, y=81.5},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={939}, names={"Flute of Xavaric"}, text="Eridan Bluewind. Do not take Felbound Ancients: it sends you to Darnassus", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.3, y=81.5},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={4101}, names={"Cleansing Felwood"}, text="Arathandris Silversky, south of the camp. Skip her salve quests", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=54.1, y=86.8},
  {t="L", seg=22, lvl=53, text="Ivy Leafrunner's quest needs level 53 and you should be a few kills short at most. Already 53? Skip this. Otherwise kill Deadwood furbolgs in the village next to Grazle until you are (Timbermaw reputation as well)", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=48.1, y=90.9},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={5249}, names={"To Winterspring!"}, text="Ivy Leafrunner, Emerald Sanctuary. Wynd Nightchaser is in Winterspring (next segment)", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.0, y=81.6},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={8462}, names={"Speak to Nafien"}, text="Ride north the whole length of Felwood to Nafien, the furbolg outside Timbermaw Hold at the end of the road", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=64.8, y=8.1, path={{55.6,81.6},{55.6,70.5},{65.4,55.8},{66.6,41.5},{71.2,33.1},{71.2,4.9},{69.2,1.9},{64.8,2.5},{63.4,4.6},{63.4,7.3}}},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={8461}, names={"Deadwood of the North"}, text="Nafien", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=64.8, y=8.1},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={8461}, names={"Deadwood of the North"}, text="Felpaw Village, just west of Nafien: 6 Den Watchers, 6 Avengers and 6 Shamans. The last kind heals: kill those first. A warlock cannot interrupt the heal: Curse of Tongues makes it slow, and all your DoTs plus Shadow Bolt outdo it. If two furbolgs come at once, the Voidwalker holds one and you Fear the other only if it will run out of the village, not into it", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=62.1, y=8.9},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={8461}, names={"Deadwood of the North"}, text="Nafien", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=64.8, y=8.1},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={8465}, names={"Speak to Salfa"}, text="Nafien. Salfa stands at the Winterspring end of the tunnel", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=64.8, y=8.1, path={{65.6,7.3}}, cave=true},
  {t="L", seg=22, lvl=54, text="Quest XP runs short here. Grind Felpaw Village to 54: every kill adds Timbermaw reputation as well. Send the Voidwalker onto one furbolg at a time from the edge of the village, put Curse of Tongues on the healers, Drain Life instead of eating where you can, Drain Soul a last hit now and then to keep 3-5 Soul Shards, and Life Tap, eat, drink or bandage between pulls. Tired of furbolgs? The Irontree Stompers and Toxic Horrors in Irontree Woods to the south-west (around 50, 24) are the same level", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=62.1, y=8.9},
  {t="N", seg=22, arg="Open the Reputation tab and check Timbermaw Hold before you go in", text="It must be Unfriendly or better, or the furbolgs inside attack you. Still Hostile? Kill more Deadwood furbolgs until it changes. Got Deadwood Headdress Feathers? Nafien takes them 5 at a time for reputation"},
  {t="N", seg=22, arg="Segment done. Next segment walks through Timbermaw Hold into Winterspring", text="Keep The New Springs (980), It's a Secret to Everybody (3908), To Winterspring! (5249) and Speak to Salfa (8465) in the log. Your hearthstone is set to Astranaar. Never attack the Timbermaw furbolgs inside the tunnel", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=64.8, y=8.1},
  {t="G", seg=23, text="You start at Nafien at level 54, hearthstone set to Astranaar. Walk through Timbermaw Hold and keep right for the Winterspring exit. Never attack the Timbermaw furbolgs inside", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=27.7, y=34.5},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={8465}, names={"Speak to Salfa"}, text="Salfa, at the tunnel exit", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=27.7, y=34.5},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={8464}, names={"Winterfall Activity"}, text="Salfa. Den Watchers live in the camps right here; Shamans and Ursa only in Winterfall Village, far to the east", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=27.7, y=34.5},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={3908}, names={"It's a Secret to Everybody"}, text="Donova Snowden, beside the hot springs a short ride south-east. She offers The Videre Elixir next: skip it, it is a Feralas trip", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={980}, names={"The New Springs"}, text="Donova Snowden", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={4842}, names={"Strange Sources"}, text="Donova Snowden. The spot is in the far south of Winterspring: you go there from Everlook", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="N", seg=23, arg="Kill Winterfall furbolgs in the camp just south-east of Salfa until one drops an Empty Firewater Flask", text="The camp spreads over 30-34, 35-37: Pathfinders (53-54), Totemics (54-55) and three Den Watchers (55-56, they count for Salfa). About 1 kill in 10 drops the flask. A Totemic sets down totems: have the Voidwalker hold the furbolg and shoot the totems down with your wand first. Pull one at a time from the edge of the camp: Voidwalker in, then Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate and Drain Life. Do not Fear inside the camp, a feared furbolg brings friends. Drain Soul the last hit now and then to keep 3-5 Soul Shards; eat, drink or bandage between pulls. Salfa buys Winterfall Spirit Beads 5 at a time: loot everything", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.5, y=36.3},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={5083}, names={"Winterfall Firewater"}, text="Right-click the Empty Firewater Flask. No flask after 30 kills or so? Go on to the grind step below and take it when it drops; without it, skip Donova's chain", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.5, y=36.3},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={5083}, names={"Winterfall Firewater"}, text="Donova Snowden", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={5084}, names={"Falling to Corruption"}, text="Donova Snowden", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="N", seg=23, arg="Go back through Timbermaw Hold to the Felwood side", text="Short trip number one. Carrying 5 Winterfall Spirit Beads? Hand them to Salfa as you pass"},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={5084}, names={"Falling to Corruption"}, text="The Deadwood Cauldron in the middle of Felpaw Village, just west of Nafien. Clear the furbolgs around it first: Voidwalker on one, Fear on a second", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=60.2, y=5.8},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={5085}, names={"Mystery Goo"}, text="The Deadwood Cauldron", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=60.2, y=5.8},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={5085}, names={"Mystery Goo"}, text="Back through the tunnel to Donova Snowden", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={5086}, names={"Toxic Horrors"}, text="Donova Snowden", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="N", seg=23, arg="Go back through Timbermaw Hold once more", text="Short trip number two"},
  {t="C", seg=23, q={5086}, names={"Toxic Horrors"}, text="Irontree Woods, down the road south-west of Felpaw Village: Toxic Horrors (53-54) drop the 3 droplets, nearly every kill. They are elementals: when two come, Banish one and kill the other. They poison and a warlock cannot cure it: Drain Life, bandage and eat", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=49.7, y=25.0},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={5086}, names={"Toxic Horrors"}, text="Back through the tunnel to Donova Snowden", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={5087}, names={"Winterfall Runners"}, text="Donova Snowden. The runners are level 57 and come three at a time: grind first", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="L", seg=23, lvl=55, text="Quest XP is thin in Winterspring. Grind the two Winterfall camps in the west to 55: the big one south-east of Salfa (30-34, 35-37) and the one east of Donova (39-42, 42-45). Every kill adds Timbermaw reputation, and the Den Watchers count for Salfa (three in the first camp, one in the second). Pull singles from the edge with the Voidwalker, keep Corruption and Curse of Agony on the target and Drain Life when you are hurt; Life Tap, then eat or bandage, between pulls", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.5, y=36.3},
  {t="C", seg=23, q={5087}, names={"Winterfall Runners"}, text="Three Winterfall Runners (57) come out of the Timbermaw tunnel beside Salfa and walk east along the road toward Winterfall Village. Wait at the exit, or ride the road east until you meet them. They come as a group of three: put a Soulstone on yourself, hold a Healthstone and start at full health and mana. Send the Voidwalker at the first, Fear the second (the road is empty, nothing for it to bring back), then put Corruption and Curse of Agony on all three and kill them one by one; keep the Voidwalker alive with Health Funnel. When two are on you: Howl of Terror, Fear one again, Death Coil if you are low. Loot the Winterfall Crate. Going badly? Sacrifice the Voidwalker for its shield, run back toward Salfa and try again", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=27.9, y=34.5},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={5087}, names={"Winterfall Runners"}, text="Donova Snowden. Skip High Chief Winterfall: he is elite", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={5249}, names={"To Winterspring!"}, text="Ride east along the road to Starfall Village, the night elf lodge on the hill north of Lake Kel'Theril. Wynd Nightchaser is inside", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=52.0, y=30.4},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={5244}, names={"The Ruins of Kel'Theril"}, text="Wynd Nightchaser", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=52.0, y=30.4},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={5244}, names={"The Ruins of Kel'Theril"}, text="Jaron Stoneshaper, the dwarf standing next to her", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=52.1, y=30.4},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={5245}, names={"Troubled Spirits of Kel'Theril"}, text="Jaron gives you his pick. The fragments are in the lake south of here; you collect them after Everlook", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=52.1, y=30.4},
  {t="G", seg=23, text="Ride on east to Everlook", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=61.0, y=38.0},
  {t="F", seg=23, arg="Everlook", text="Maethrya, the hippogryph master outside the north gate", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=62.3, y=36.6},
  {t="S", seg=23, arg="Everlook", text="Innkeeper Vizzie, at the inn. Your hearthstone now brings you back here", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=61.4, y=38.8},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={6603}, names={"Trouble in Winterspring!"}, text="Meggi Peppinrocker, near the west gate. It goes to Donova on your way back west", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=60.7, y=38.2},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={3783}, names={"Are We There, Yeti?"}, text="Umi Rumplesnicker", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=60.9, y=37.6},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={6604}, names={"Enraged Wildkin"}, text="Harlo Wigglesworth, next to the inn", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=61.1, y=38.4},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={6028,6030}, names={"The Everlook Report","Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff"}, text="Gregor Greystone, in the inn. Both are deliveries to the Plaguelands, at the very end of the route: keep them", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=61.3, y=39.0},
  {t="C", seg=23, q={3783}, names={"Are We There, Yeti?"}, text="Ice Thistle Yetis (55-56) on the hills south-east of Everlook drop the 10 Thick Yeti Furs", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=67.4, y=42.3},
  {t="C", seg=23, q={8464}, names={"Winterfall Activity"}, text="Winterfall Village, just east of Everlook: 8 Shamans and 8 Ursa, and whatever Den Watchers Salfa still needs. Only six Shamans live here, so wait for a respawn. The Shamans heal and a warlock has no interrupt: put Curse of Tongues on a Shaman and kill it first; Death Coil stops a heal that is about to land. The Ursa (57-58) hit hardest: let the Voidwalker take them, one at a time, at full health, with Health Funnel when it drops low. Do not Fear inside the village. High Chief Winterfall in the cave at the back (69.6, 38.3) is elite: stay out of it", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=67.1, y=36.8, path={{68.2,41.3}}, cave=true},
  {t="L", seg=23, lvl=56, text="Stay in Winterfall Village and grind to 56 before the higher yetis and the owlbeasts. Pull at the edge of the camp, one at a time, Voidwalker first. A pair at the edge: Fear the second one away from the camp; a pair in the middle: back off. Life Tap, eat and bandage between pulls. The yetis next door are an easier alternative", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=67.1, y=36.8},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={3783}, names={"Are We There, Yeti?"}, text="Umi Rumplesnicker, Everlook", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=60.9, y=37.6},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={977}, names={"Are We There, Yeti?"}, text="Umi Rumplesnicker", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=60.9, y=37.6},
  {t="C", seg=23, q={977}, names={"Are We There, Yeti?"}, text="Ice Thistle Matriarchs and Patriarchs (56-58) higher up in the Ice Thistle Hills drop the 2 Pristine Yeti Horns. Pull them one at a time with the Voidwalker; Fear a second yeti (the hills are open, but keep it away from other yetis)", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=69.2, y=40.8},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={977}, names={"Are We There, Yeti?"}, text="Umi Rumplesnicker. Do not take her third quest: the mechanical yeti has to visit Gadgetzan and Un'Goro and come back here, and you leave Winterspring for good today", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=60.9, y=37.6},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={6604}, names={"Enraged Wildkin"}, text="Ride west to Jaron Stoneshaper, Starfall Village", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=52.1, y=30.4},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={4861}, names={"Enraged Wildkin"}, text="Jaron Stoneshaper", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=52.1, y=30.4},
  {t="C", seg=23, q={5245}, names={"Troubled Spirits of Kel'Theril"}, text="Lake Kel'Theril, south of Starfall. Four Highborne Relic Fragments stick out of the ice (50.9, 41.7; 52.4, 41.5; 53.3, 43.4; 55.1, 43.0): use Jaron's Pick next to each one, then loot it. The Anguished and Suffering Highborne (54-55) around them are ghosts with a mana burn: put Curse of Tongues on them to slow it and kill them fast; Life Tap gives the mana back. Fear a second one. Keep the four fragments for the Plaguelands", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=53.0, y=42.4},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={4861}, names={"Enraged Wildkin"}, text="Ride south along the road, past the Mazthoril cave (stay on the road), to Jaron's wrecked camp at the edge of Owl Wing Thicket: the Damaged Crate", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=59.0, y=59.8},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={4863}, names={"Enraged Wildkin"}, text="The Damaged Crate", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=59.0, y=59.8},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={4863}, names={"Enraged Wildkin"}, text="Jaron's Wagon, a little further east", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=61.4, y=60.7},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={4864}, names={"Enraged Wildkin"}, text="Jaron's Wagon", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=61.4, y=60.7},
  {t="C", seg=23, q={4864}, names={"Enraged Wildkin"}, text="Pick up Jaron's Supplies from the snow beside the wagon, then kill Crazed, Moontouched and Berserk Owlbeasts (56-59) around the camp and in Owl Wing Thicket just east until one drops the Blue-feathered Amulet. They hit hard and enrage: the Voidwalker tanks, one at a time; Fear a second one and keep Health Funnel on the Voidwalker. Drain Life or use your Healthstone early", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=64.8, y=60.8},
  {t="C", seg=23, q={4842}, names={"Strange Sources"}, text="Ride to the far south until the sky turns dark at the mouth of Darkwhisper Gorge. The way runs through Frostwhisper Gorge (around 58-66, 65-73), whose Frostmaul Giants and Preservers are elite, level 59-60: stay mounted, keep to the middle and do not stop (if a giant knocks you off your mount, use Death Coil or Howl of Terror and run on). Reaching the mouth of Darkwhisper Gorge is enough; the demons further in are elite too", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=59.8, y=74.3},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={4864}, names={"Enraged Wildkin"}, text="Ride back north, through Frostwhisper Gorge the same way, to Jaron Stoneshaper at Starfall Village", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=52.1, y=30.4, path={{57.8,68.4},{60.6,63.6},{60.6,57.3},{57.8,53.1},{57.8,44.8},{56.8,39.4},{54.2,38.5},{52.6,36.1}}},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={6603}, names={"Trouble in Winterspring!"}, text="Ride west along the road to Donova Snowden at the hot springs", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2, path={{52.0,32.2},{48.8,32.2},{46.0,38.2},{30.8,40.9},{30.4,43.9}}},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={5082}, names={"Threat of the Winterfall"}, text="Donova Snowden", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={4842}, names={"Strange Sources"}, text="Donova Snowden", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="C", seg=23, q={5082}, names={"Threat of the Winterfall"}, text="The two western Winterfall camps again: 8 Pathfinders, 8 Totemics and 8 Den Watchers. Only four Den Watchers live in the west (three in the camp south-east of Salfa at 30.5, 36.3, one in the camp east of Donova at 41.6, 42.6): kill them, do the Pathfinders and Totemics, and they are back for the second round. Same method as before: Voidwalker first, DoTs, wand the totems, no Fear inside a camp", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.8, y=36.5},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={5082}, names={"Threat of the Winterfall"}, text="Donova Snowden", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={8464}, names={"Winterfall Activity"}, text="Salfa, at the tunnel exit. Hand him any Winterfall Spirit Beads too, 5 at a time", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=27.7, y=34.5},
  {t="H", seg=23, arg="Everlook", text="Use your Hearthstone"},
  {t="N", seg=23, arg="Segment done. Next segment flies south from Everlook", text="Keep Troubled Spirits of Kel'Theril (5245, with the four relic fragments), The Everlook Report (6028) and Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff (6030) in the log: all three are for the Plaguelands. Sell and repair here; your hearthstone is set to Everlook"},
  {t="FLY", seg=24, arg="Marshal's Refuge", text="You start in Everlook at level 56, hearthstone set to Everlook. Maethrya, outside the north gate. A very long flight: stay on until it lands in Un'Goro Crater", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=62.3, y=36.6},
  {t="N", seg=24, arg="Optional dungeon: Blackmaw Hold, levels 55-60", text="New Forever dungeon, not checked in game yet. It is a furbolg city behind the big gate in Azshara. Quests named for it: The Twin Bears (Lorekeeper Nok), Get to the Roots of It (Mathrengyl Bearwalker in Darnassus), Claws That Rend, Tusks that Gore (Ogtinc in Azshara) and Blackmaw Pouches (Ekkal at the Ruins of Eldarath in Azshara); positions are not published yet. Take what is offered: the addon logs it so these steps can be filled in.", dg=17, run=true},
  {t="N", seg=24, arg="Ride to the north-west corner of Un'Goro Crater and take the ridge path west into Silithus", text="It comes out at Valor's Rest, the graveyard in the north-east of Silithus"},
  {t="G", seg=24, text="Follow the road south-west from Valor's Rest to Cenarion Hold. Stay on the road: Hive'Ashi, north of it as you get close to the Hold, is all elite", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=50.6, y=34.5},
  {t="F", seg=24, arg="Cenarion Hold", text="Cloud Skydancer, the hippogryph master on the north side of the Hold", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=50.6, y=34.5},
  {t="S", seg=24, arg="Cenarion Hold", text="Calandrath, the innkeeper. From now on your hearthstone brings you back here", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.9, y=39.2},
  {t="A", seg=24, q={8280}, names={"Securing the Supply Lines"}, text="Windcaller Proudhorn", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.1, y=38.3},
  {t="A", seg=24, q={8277}, names={"Deadly Desert Venom"}, text="Beetix Ficklespragg", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.6, y=38.6},
  {t="A", seg=24, q={8284}, names={"The Twilight Mystery"}, text="Geologist Larksbane", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=49.7, y=37.5},
  {t="C", seg=24, q={8277,8280}, names={"Deadly Desert Venom","Securing the Supply Lines"}, text="East and north-east of the Hold: Stonelash Scorpids (stingers), Sand Skitterers (fangs) and 15 Dredge Strikers share the open sand, all level 54-56. Stay east of Hive'Ashi, the big hive north-west of the Hold: its silithids are elite. Send the Voidwalker first, then Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate and your wand; Fear a second one, the sand is open. The scorpids poison and a warlock cannot cure it: Drain Life, bandage and eat", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=61.0, y=28.0},
  {t="C", seg=24, q={8284}, names={"The Twilight Mystery"}, text="Ride back past the Hold, go round the south and west sides of Hive'Ashi and north to the abandoned Twilight camp in the north-west: 8 Twilight Tablet Fragments lie on the ground among the air elementals. Banish works on every one of them: when two come, Banish one and let the Voidwalker hold the other. The Windreaver, a level 60 elite elemental, patrols the east and south sides of the camp (he starts around 28.7, 26.9): spot him and let him pass, and skip the lone fragment at the south end. If he does come for you, Banish him and ride away", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=23.2, y=13.0, path={{62.0,17.2},{58.6,16.0},{56.8,13.3},{49.6,15.4},{45.4,20.5},{42.4,17.2},{35.4,16.6},{33.4,15.1},{26.2,15.1}}},
  {t="T", seg=24, q={8280}, names={"Securing the Supply Lines"}, text="Windcaller Proudhorn, Cenarion Hold", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.1, y=38.3, path={{25.8,14.8},{35.6,15.1},{36.8,16.9},{42.4,17.2},{45.6,20.8},{47.0,31.9}}},
  {t="A", seg=24, q={8281}, names={"Stepping Up Security"}, text="Windcaller Proudhorn", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.1, y=38.3},
  {t="T", seg=24, q={8284}, names={"The Twilight Mystery"}, text="Geologist Larksbane", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=49.7, y=37.5},
  {t="A", seg=24, q={8285}, names={"The Deserter"}, text="Geologist Larksbane", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=49.7, y=37.5},
  {t="T", seg=24, q={8277}, names={"Deadly Desert Venom"}, text="Beetix Ficklespragg", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.6, y=38.6},
  {t="A", seg=24, q={8278}, names={"Noggle's Last Hope"}, text="Beetix Ficklespragg", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.6, y=38.6},
  {t="L", seg=24, lvl=57, text="The rest of Silithus is level 57-60, and Bor's quest needs 57. Grind the sand east and north-east of the Hold to 57: Dredge Strikers, Stonelash Scorpids and Sand Skitterers (54-56) die fast. Dredge Crushers (57-58) south of the Hold are slower but count for Proudhorn's new quest (20). One at a time: Voidwalker in, Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate, then wand or Drain Life. Fear a second one. Drain Soul the last hit when you are short of Soul Shards (keep 3-5), Life Tap after each kill, and eat or bandage between pulls", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=61.0, y=28.0},
  {t="A", seg=24, q={8318}, names={"Secret Communication"}, text="Bor Wildmane, Cenarion Hold. From now on keep every Encrypted Twilight Text: you need 20 in all, 10 for Bor and 10 for Hermit Ortell", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=48.6, y=37.8},
  {t="T", seg=24, q={8285}, names={"The Deserter"}, text="Hermit Ortell, in his hut in the far south-east. Ride east first and then south, so the elite silithids on the sand south-east of the Hold stay on your right. Kill the Stonelash Pincers and Dredge Crushers you pass: Beetix wants 3 Pincer stingers and Proudhorn 20 Crushers", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=67.2, y=69.8},
  {t="A", seg=24, q={8279}, names={"The Twilight Lexicon"}, text="Hermit Ortell", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=67.2, y=69.8},
  {t="C", seg=24, q={8278}, obj={2}, names={"Noggle's Last Hope"}, text="Leave the hut to the north-west: Hive'Regal starts just south-west of it. Finish the 3 Stonelash Pincer Stingers on the sand here, and keep killing every Dredge Crusher you meet", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=60.0, y=62.0},
  {t="C", seg=24, q={8278,8278}, obj={1,3}, names={"Noggle's Last Hope","Noggle's Last Hope"}, text="Ride west along the north edge of Hive'Regal, then south-west into the foothills below Hive'Zora: Stonelash Flayers (stingers) and Rock Stalkers (fangs), 57-59", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=38.0, y=78.0},
  {t="C", seg=24, q={8279}, obj={2}, names={"The Twilight Lexicon"}, text="Keep west along the foothills to Twilight Keeper Exeter's camp in the far south-west. He is level 60 and not elite, but the camp is full of 57-60 cultists: put a Soulstone on yourself and hold a Healthstone first. Pull them out one or two at a time from as far away as you can, Voidwalker on the first. A warlock has no interrupt: put Curse of Tongues on the casters (Geolords and Stonecallers) and kill them first. Fear a second cultist only when you have pulled the fight well clear of the camp, or it comes back with more. Back out of the camp if more come (Howl of Terror or Death Coil, then run), and kill Exeter last at full health and mana, with the Voidwalker on him and Health Funnel when it drops low. Every cultist can drop Encrypted Twilight Texts. Too many deaths? Abandon The Twilight Lexicon and skip the Keeper steps and Ortell's follow-ups", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=16.1, y=86.4},
  {t="G", seg=24, text="Ride back east along the foothills, then north between Hive'Zora and the Hold. Dredge Crushers and Stonelash Pincers roam this strip", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=42.0, y=55.0},
  {t="C", seg=24, q={8279}, obj={1}, names={"The Twilight Lexicon"}, text="Twilight Keeper Mayna's camp, north of Hive'Zora. Same method: Soulstone, Voidwalker first, Curse of Tongues on the casters, Keeper last. An elite Twilight Prophet can walk the west side of the zone: let him pass", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=26.4, y=36.6},
  {t="C", seg=24, q={8279,8281}, obj={3,0}, names={"The Twilight Lexicon","Stepping Up Security"}, text="Twilight Keeper Havunth at the Twilight Post, just south-west of the Hold. Same method again. Finish the 20 Dredge Crushers on the sand around both camps", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=40.9, y=42.2},
  {t="C", seg=24, q={8318}, names={"Secret Communication"}, text="Stay at the Twilight Post until you hold 20 Encrypted Twilight Texts: Twilight Avengers, Geolords and Stonecallers, pulled out to the edge one at a time. The quest shows 10 of 10 long before that; count the stack in your bags", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=39.6, y=44.0},
  {t="T", seg=24, q={8278}, names={"Noggle's Last Hope"}, text="Beetix Ficklespragg, Cenarion Hold", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.6, y=38.6},
  {t="T", seg=24, q={8281}, names={"Stepping Up Security"}, text="Windcaller Proudhorn", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.1, y=38.3},
  {t="T", seg=24, q={8318}, names={"Secret Communication"}, text="Bor Wildmane takes 10 of the texts. Keep the other 10 for Ortell", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=48.6, y=37.8},
  {t="A", seg=24, q={8282}, names={"Noggle's Lost Satchel"}, text="Noggle Ficklespragg, lying next to Beetix", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.6, y=38.5},
  {t="C", seg=24, q={8282}, names={"Noggle's Lost Satchel"}, text="Ride south, passing the elite silithids below the Hold on their west side, and keep west of Hive'Regal until you reach the mountains at the south edge. Noggle's Satchel lies on the ground among the Stonelash Flayers. Deathclasp, a level 59 elite scorpid, rests a few steps south-east of it (45.1, 92.3): come in from the north-west, grab the satchel and leave. If she comes for you, Fear or Death Coil her, leave the Voidwalker behind and run north; do not fight her", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=44.6, y=91.4, path={{51.6,42.7},{56.0,48.4},{56.0,57.6},{57.2,60.0},{57.2,61.5},{54.4,64.5},{54.0,69.9},{54.0,76.8},{55.8,89.4},{53.0,91.8},{50.8,96.3},{45.0,94.8}}},
  {t="T", seg=24, q={8279}, names={"The Twilight Lexicon"}, text="Hermit Ortell. Ride back north the same way, then east, keeping north of Hive'Regal", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=67.2, y=69.8, path={{44.6,94.2},{46.8,95.7},{55.4,99.0},{60.0,97.5},{61.8,94.2},{61.8,80.1},{64.8,75.9},{64.6,70.5}}},
  {t="A", seg=24, q={8323}, names={"True Believers"}, text="Hermit Ortell", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=67.2, y=69.8},
  {t="T", seg=24, q={8323}, names={"True Believers"}, text="Give him the 10 Encrypted Twilight Texts", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=67.2, y=69.8},
  {t="A", seg=24, q={8287}, names={"A Terrible Purpose"}, text="Hermit Ortell", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=67.2, y=69.8},
  {t="T", seg=24, q={8282}, names={"Noggle's Lost Satchel"}, text="Noggle Ficklespragg, Cenarion Hold", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.6, y=38.5},
  {t="T", seg=24, q={8287}, names={"A Terrible Purpose"}, text="Commander Mar'alith, on the north side of the Hold. Skip his follow-ups: they are elite", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=49.2, y=34.2},
  {t="FLY", seg=24, arg="Theramore", text="Cloud Skydancer. A long flight by way of Gadgetzan; if it stops there, take the next one on to Theramore Isle", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=50.6, y=34.5},
  {t="N", seg=24, arg="Take the boat from Theramore to Menethil Harbor", text="The dock is at the east end of Theramore. Keep Troubled Spirits of Kel'Theril (5245), The Everlook Report (6028) and Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff (6030) in the log. Your hearthstone is set to Cenarion Hold: do not use it from here on"},
  {t="FLY", seg=25, arg="Ironforge", text="You arrive on the boat from Theramore at level 57, hearthstone still set to Cenarion Hold (do not use it). Shellei Brondir is the Menethil gryphon master", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=9.5, y=59.7},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=25, text="Briarthorn, the warlock trainer in the Forlorn Cavern in the north of the city: learn everything he offers up to level 56 (the route made no training stop in Kalimdor). The demon trainer beside him sells the new ranks of the Voidwalker's spell books. Stock up on Soul Shards on the first Plaguelands kills if you are short", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=50.4, y=5.7},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5090}, names={"A Call to Arms: The Plaguelands!"}, text="Courier Hammerfall walks a circuit through Ironforge and has no fixed spot: ride the outer ring until you meet him. You need this one: Commander Ashlam Valorfist's quests at Chillwind Camp only open after it", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=60.1, y=34.2},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={3702}, names={"The Smoldering Ruins of Thaurissan"}, text="Royal Historian Archesonus, in the throne room wing (38.4, 55.3)", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=38.4, y=55.3},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={3702}, names={"The Smoldering Ruins of Thaurissan"}, text="Listen to her story to the end", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=38.4, y=55.3},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={3701}, names={"The Smoldering Ruins of Thaurissan"}, text="Royal Historian Archesonus. The ruins are in the Burning Steppes, the last stop of the route", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=38.4, y=55.3},
  {t="FLY", seg=25, arg="Southshore", text="Gryth Thurden, the Ironforge gryphon master", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=55.5, y=47.7},
  {t="G", seg=25, text="Ride north out of Southshore into the Alterac Mountains and follow the road up the east side of the zone to the Western Plaguelands border. Chillwind Camp is right behind it. Crushridge ogres and Syndicate sit beside the road: keep riding", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=42.9, y=85.1},
  {t="F", seg=25, arg="Chillwind Camp", text="Bibilfaz Featherwhistle, the gryphon master", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=42.9, y=85.1},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5090}, names={"A Call to Arms: The Plaguelands!"}, text="Commander Ashlam Valorfist", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=42.7, y=84.0},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5092}, names={"Clear the Way"}, text="Commander Ashlam Valorfist", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=42.7, y=84.0},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={6028}, names={"The Everlook Report"}, text="Argent Officer Pureheart", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=43.0, y=83.5},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5903}, names={"A Plague Upon Thee"}, text="Nathaniel Dumah. The termite mounds are in the Eastern Plaguelands: keep the jar until you get there", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=43.4, y=84.8},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={5092}, names={"Clear the Way"}, text="Sorrow Hill, the graveyard east of the camp: 10 Skeletal Flayers and 10 Slavering Ghouls (50-52). Easy at your level: Voidwalker in, Corruption and Curse of Agony on two at once, Fear a third (Fear works on undead)", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=50.8, y=79.4},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5142}, names={"Little Pamela"}, text="Marlene Redpath, the ghost in the house at Sorrow Hill. Pamela is in the Eastern Plaguelands", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=49.2, y=78.6},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5092}, names={"Clear the Way"}, text="Commander Ashlam Valorfist, Chillwind Camp", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=42.7, y=84.0},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5097,5215}, names={"All Along the Watchtowers","The Scourge Cauldrons"}, text="Commander Ashlam Valorfist. He gives you a Beacon Torch", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=42.7, y=84.0},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5215}, names={"The Scourge Cauldrons"}, text="High Priestess MacDonnell, next to him", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=43.0, y=84.5},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5216}, names={"Target: Felstone Field"}, text="High Priestess MacDonnell. Keep the empty bottle", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=43.0, y=84.5},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={4971}, names={"A Matter of Time"}, text="Chromie, in the ruined inn at the north-west corner of Andorhal. Andorhal has elites: Araj the Summoner (61) in the middle of town (45.3, 69.2) and Skeletal Warlords (56-57) on the streets. Look down each street before you ride in and stay away from the centre", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=39.5, y=66.8},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={5097}, names={"All Along the Watchtowers"}, text="Mark the four towers: stand in each doorway and use the Beacon Torch. Tower Two (42.3, 66.2) and Tower Three (44.3, 63.2) are on the north side, Tower Four (46.6, 71.0) in the south-east, Tower One (40.0, 71.6) in the south-west. Pull the Skeletal Executioners and Acolytes at each door out to you one at a time, Voidwalker first; the Acolytes are casters and a warlock has no interrupt: put Curse of Tongues on them and kill them first. Do not Fear in the streets: a feared mob runs into the Skeletal Warlords", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=42.2, y=67.0},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={4971}, names={"A Matter of Time"}, text="Use the Temporal Displacer next to one of the silos on the east edge of town (45-50, 62-69) and kill the Temporal Parasites that appear. Repeat at other silos until you have 10", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=48.1, y=65.2},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={4971}, names={"A Matter of Time"}, text="Chromie", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=39.5, y=66.8},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={4972}, names={"Counting Out Time"}, text="Chromie", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=39.5, y=66.8},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={4972}, names={"Counting Out Time"}, text="Small Lockboxes lie in the rubble all over Andorhal; open them for the 5 watches. Start on the west side near Chromie (38-42, 66-72)", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=40.0, y=68.0},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={4972}, names={"Counting Out Time"}, text="Chromie. She offers the same quest again for 5 more watches (repeatable, very little XP): skip it", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=39.5, y=66.8},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={5216}, names={"Target: Felstone Field"}, text="Felstone Field, the farm north-west of Andorhal: kill Cauldron Lord Bilemaw (53) beside the cauldron for its key. Clear the undead around him one at a time first, Voidwalker on each", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=37.2, y=56.8},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5216}, names={"Target: Felstone Field"}, text="Use the key on the Scourge Cauldron", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=37.2, y=56.8},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5217}, names={"Return to Chillwind Camp"}, text="The Scourge Cauldron", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=37.2, y=56.8},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5021}, names={"Better Late Than Never"}, text="Janice Felstone's ghost, upstairs in the Felstone farmhouse", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=38.4, y=54.1},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5021}, names={"Better Late Than Never"}, text="Janice's Parcel, in the barn behind the house. Do not take the follow-up: it goes to Stormwind", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=38.7, y=55.2},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5217}, names={"Return to Chillwind Camp"}, text="High Priestess MacDonnell, Chillwind Camp", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=43.0, y=84.5, path={{39.2,61.8},{35.4,66.9},{34.8,75.9},{40.6,78.3},{41.0,81.3}}},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5219}, names={"Target: Dalson's Tears"}, text="High Priestess MacDonnell", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=43.0, y=84.5},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5097}, names={"All Along the Watchtowers"}, text="Commander Ashlam Valorfist", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=42.7, y=84.0},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={4984}, names={"The Wildlife Suffers Too"}, text="Mulgris Deepriver, the tauren at the Writhing Haunt, the farm north-east of Andorhal. Go around Andorhal on its east side. The cauldron here comes later", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=53.7, y=64.7},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={5219}, names={"Target: Dalson's Tears"}, text="Dalson's Tears, the next farm north-west: kill Cauldron Lord Malvinious (55) beside the cauldron", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=46.2, y=51.9},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5219}, names={"Target: Dalson's Tears"}, text="The Scourge Cauldron", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=46.2, y=51.9},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5220}, names={"Return to Chillwind Camp"}, text="The Scourge Cauldron", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=46.2, y=51.9},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5058}, names={"Mrs. Dalson's Diary"}, text="Mrs. Dalson's Diary, an open book in the farm buildings at Dalson's Tears (the arrow points at it)", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=47.8, y=50.7},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5058}, names={"Mrs. Dalson's Diary"}, text="Read it to the end", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=47.8, y=50.7},
  {t="N", seg=25, arg="Kill the Wandering Skeleton that walks around the Dalson farm and take the Dalson Outhouse Key", text="Not there? It respawns after a few minutes: do the wolves below first", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=47.7, y=49.9},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5059}, names={"Locked Away"}, text="The outhouse behind the farmhouse", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=48.1, y=49.6},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5059}, names={"Locked Away"}, text="Open it and Farmer Dalson (56) jumps out. Kill him for the cabinet key", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=48.1, y=49.6},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5060}, names={"Locked Away"}, text="The Locked Cabinet upstairs in the farmhouse", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=47.4, y=49.6},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5060}, names={"Locked Away"}, text="Open it", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=47.4, y=49.6},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={4984}, names={"The Wildlife Suffers Too"}, text="8 Diseased Wolves (53-54) in the fields around and north of Dalson's Tears", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=46.4, y=43.0},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={4984}, names={"The Wildlife Suffers Too"}, text="Mulgris Deepriver, the Writhing Haunt", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=53.7, y=64.7},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={4985}, names={"The Wildlife Suffers Too"}, text="Mulgris Deepriver. The grizzlies are further east", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=53.7, y=64.7},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5220}, names={"Return to Chillwind Camp"}, text="High Priestess MacDonnell, Chillwind Camp", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=43.0, y=84.5},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5222}, names={"Target: Writhing Haunt"}, text="High Priestess MacDonnell", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=43.0, y=84.5},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={5222}, names={"Target: Writhing Haunt"}, text="Back to the Writhing Haunt: kill Cauldron Lord Razarch (56) beside the cauldron", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=53.0, y=65.6},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5222}, names={"Target: Writhing Haunt"}, text="The Scourge Cauldron", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=53.0, y=65.6},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5223}, names={"Return to Chillwind Camp"}, text="The Scourge Cauldron", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=53.0, y=65.6},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5223}, names={"Return to Chillwind Camp"}, text="High Priestess MacDonnell, Chillwind Camp", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=43.0, y=84.5},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5225}, names={"Target: Gahrron's Withering"}, text="High Priestess MacDonnell. Sell and repair: you are away from the camp for a long time now", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=43.0, y=84.5},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={4985}, names={"The Wildlife Suffers Too"}, text="8 Diseased Grizzlies (55-56) in the fields on the way east, between Dalson's Tears and Gahrron's Withering", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=60.0, y=50.0},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={5225}, names={"Target: Gahrron's Withering"}, text="Gahrron's Withering, the easternmost farm: kill Cauldron Lord Soulwrath (58) beside the cauldron. Clear the ghosts around him first. He casts shadow bolts: put Curse of Tongues on him, let the Voidwalker hold him and keep Corruption, Curse of Agony and Immolate running; Drain Life when you are hurt. Fight him at full health and mana with a Healthstone in your bags", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=62.5, y=58.5},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5225}, names={"Target: Gahrron's Withering"}, text="The Scourge Cauldron", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=62.5, y=58.5},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5226}, names={"Return to Chillwind Point"}, text="The Scourge Cauldron. You hand it in when you come back from the Eastern Plaguelands", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=62.5, y=58.5},
  {t="G", seg=25, text="Ride east on the road and cross the bridge over the Thondroril River into the Eastern Plaguelands. Tirion Fordring's hut stands on the east bank, a little north of the road", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=5.2, y=35.6},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5542,5543,5544}, names={"Demon Dogs","Blood Tinged Skies","Carrion Grubbage"}, text="Tirion Fordring. Three kill quests for the whole zone: from here on kill every Plaguehound, Plaguebat and Carrion Grub you pass", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=5.2, y=35.6},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={5543}, names={"Blood Tinged Skies"}, text="Ride south along the river side: 30 Plaguebats (53-55) fly all over the south-west of the zone. Only the plain Plaguebats count here. The 20 Plaguehound Runts (53-54) run in the same fields, and every Carrion Grub can drop a Slab of Carrion Worm Meat (15)", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=14.3, y=64.1},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={6024}, names={"Hameya's Plea"}, text="A Torn Scroll on the ground beside the Undercroft crypt in the south. Infiltrator Hameya is in the far north-east; the crypt itself comes later", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=22.9, y=73.0},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5142}, names={"Little Pamela"}, text="Pamela Redpath, the ghost girl in the ruined house at Darrowshire, east of the Undercroft", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=31.1, y=78.0},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5149}, names={"Pamela's Doll"}, text="Pamela Redpath", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=31.1, y=78.0},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={5149}, names={"Pamela's Doll"}, text="The doll's head, left side and right side lie in the ruined houses of Darrowshire, just east of Pamela. Ghosts appear when you pick one up. Put the three parts together", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=33.4, y=78.6},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5149}, names={"Pamela's Doll"}, text="Pamela Redpath", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=31.1, y=78.0},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5241}, names={"Uncle Carlin"}, text="Pamela Redpath", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=31.2, y=78.0},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={5542}, obj={2}, names={"Demon Dogs"}, text="Ride north-east to the main road and follow it east: 5 Plaguehounds (55-56) roam the middle of the zone beside the road, with more Carrion Grubs", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=47.2, y=48.9},
  {t="F", seg=25, arg="Light's Hope Chapel", text="Keep east on the road to Light's Hope Chapel. Khaelyn Steelwing is the gryphon master", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=71.8, y=49.6},
  {t="S", seg=25, arg="Light's Hope Chapel", text="Jessica Chambers, the innkeeper. Your hearthstone now brings you back here", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=71.8, y=48.5},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5241}, names={"Uncle Carlin"}, text="Carlin Redpath", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=71.7, y=50.0},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5211}, names={"Defenders of Darrowshire"}, text="Carlin Redpath", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=71.7, y=50.0},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={6030}, names={"Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff"}, text="Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=71.6, y=50.1},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={6021}, names={"Zaeldarr the Outcast"}, text="Caretaker Alen, at the graves south-west of the chapel. Zaeldarr is in the Undercroft crypt", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=69.9, y=53.7},
  {t="N", seg=25, arg="Optional: Smokey LaRue's That's Asking A Lot (6026)", text="He wants 2 Thorium Bars, 1 Golden Rod, 8 Hi-Explosive Bombs and 8 Unstable Triggers: crafted goods. Only worth it if you can make or already own them. Skip his follow-up either way: it is elite"},
  {t="L", seg=25, lvl=58, text="The north of the zone is level 57-60. Not 58 yet? Grind the Noxious Plaguebats, Plaguehounds and Carrion Grubs along the road just west of Light's Hope first (the hounds and grubs count for Tirion). The bats silence: let the Voidwalker hold them, get your DoTs on before the silence lands and use your wand until it ends. Get to full health before you pull, and Life Tap, eat or bandage between pulls", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=58.0, y=51.0},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={5544}, names={"Carrion Grubbage"}, text="Ride north. Carrion Devourers (56-57) in the north-east finish the 15 Slabs of Carrion Worm Meat. Diseased Flayers (57-59) stand among them: each one releases a Darrowshire Spirit when it dies. Talk to the spirit to free it (15 for Carlin)", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=56.5, y=25.0},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={6024}, names={"Hameya's Plea"}, text="Infiltrator Hameya (60, not elite), a troll in the far north on the way to Zul'Mashar. Pull him alone with the Voidwalker and fight him at full health and mana, DoTs up and Health Funnel on the Voidwalker when it drops low; Fear a second troll if one comes, and Death Coil or Howl of Terror if you have to leave. Take his key", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=62.0, y=11.1},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={5542}, obj={3}, names={"Demon Dogs"}, text="Ride west across the north of the zone: 5 Frenzied Plaguehounds (57-58) roam here", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=43.9, y=28.9},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5245}, names={"Troubled Spirits of Kel'Theril"}, text="Aurora Skycaller, beside the Northpass Tower in the north. Do not take her follow-up: it sends you to Azshara", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=46.5, y=16.0},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={5903,5211}, names={"A Plague Upon Thee","Defenders of Darrowshire"}, text="Plaguewood, in the north-west: use the Empty Termite Jar on the Large Termite Mounds until you have 100 termites. The Cannibal Ghouls (54-55) all over Plaguewood release Darrowshire Spirits: free the rest of your 15 here. Ziggurat Protectors (58, elite) guard the ziggurats (about 19, 16; 23, 29; 25, 18; 28, 18): work the mounds on the west side (16-22, 19-27) and give them room. Never Fear a ghoul toward a ziggurat", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=19.0, y=23.0},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={6164}, names={"Augustus' Receipt Book"}, text="Augustus the Touched, in a cave at Terrordale, just west of the termite mounds", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=11.4, y=26.4},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={6164}, names={"Augustus' Receipt Book"}, text="Augustus' Receipt Book lies in the ruined inn at Terrordale, a short walk north-east of his cave, upstairs. Crypt Fiends and Crypt Walkers (53-56) live in and around it: pull them one at a time with the Voidwalker. The Fiends web you in place and poison: stand still and Drain Life, you cannot cure it", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=14.0, y=24.2},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={6164}, names={"Augustus' Receipt Book"}, text="Augustus the Touched", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=11.4, y=26.4},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={5542,5543,5544}, names={"Demon Dogs","Blood Tinged Skies","Carrion Grubbage"}, text="Ride south toward Tirion and finish whatever is left: Plaguehound Runts and Plaguebats in the fields south of his hut, Carrion Grubs everywhere", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=12.0, y=45.0},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5542,5543,5544}, names={"Demon Dogs","Blood Tinged Skies","Carrion Grubbage"}, text="Tirion Fordring", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=5.2, y=35.6},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5742}, names={"Redemption"}, text="Tirion Fordring", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=5.2, y=35.6},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5742}, names={"Redemption"}, text="Listen to Tirion", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=5.2, y=35.6},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5781}, names={"Of Forgotten Memories"}, text="Tirion Fordring", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=5.2, y=35.6},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={5781,6021}, names={"Of Forgotten Memories","Zaeldarr the Outcast"}, text="The Undercroft, in the far south. Kill Zaeldarr the Outcast (54-55) inside the crypt for his head. Then click the Loose Dirt Mound on the grave in front of the crypt (23.8, 74.5): Mercutio Filthgorger (57) arrives with Crypt Robbers. Before you click: Soulstone on yourself, Healthstone in your bags, full health and mana. Send the Voidwalker at Mercutio and kill him first for Taelan's Hammer; Fear one Robber, use Howl of Terror when several are on you, then kill the Robbers one by one. Sacrifice the Voidwalker for its shield if it goes wrong", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=23.5, y=74.0},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={6024}, names={"Hameya's Plea"}, text="Use Hameya's Key on the Mound of Dirt beside the wagon behind the crypt", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=23.6, y=73.8},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5781}, names={"Of Forgotten Memories"}, text="Ride back north-west to Tirion Fordring", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=5.2, y=35.6},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5845}, names={"Of Lost Honor"}, text="Tirion Fordring", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=5.2, y=35.6},
  {t="H", seg=25, arg="Light's Hope Chapel", text="Use your Hearthstone"},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={6021}, names={"Zaeldarr the Outcast"}, text="Caretaker Alen", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=69.9, y=53.7},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5211}, names={"Defenders of Darrowshire"}, text="Carlin Redpath. Skip his follow-up: it is elite", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=71.7, y=50.0},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={5845}, names={"Of Lost Honor"}, text="Ride north to Northdale: the Symbol of Lost Honor lies under the water of the pond in the hamlet. Scourge patrol the ruins: clear the bank first, Voidwalker on each. Cast Unending Breath before you dive", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=62.5, y=26.8},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5845}, names={"Of Lost Honor"}, text="Ride west across the zone to Tirion Fordring", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=5.2, y=35.6},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5846}, names={"Of Love and Family"}, text="Tirion Fordring", zone="Eastern Plaguelands", map=1423, x=5.2, y=35.6},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5846}, names={"Of Love and Family"}, text="Artist Renfray, a ghost on the island of Caer Darrow in the lake south of Tirion's hut: swim across. Scholomance is on the island too; do not go in. Do not take her follow-up: it is inside Stratholme", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=65.8, y=75.4},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={4985}, names={"The Wildlife Suffers Too"}, text="Mulgris Deepriver, the Writhing Haunt, on the way west. Skip Glyphed Oaken Branch: it goes to Darnassus", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=53.7, y=64.7},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5226}, names={"Return to Chillwind Point"}, text="High Priestess MacDonnell, Chillwind Camp", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=43.0, y=84.5},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5903}, names={"A Plague Upon Thee"}, text="Nathaniel Dumah", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=43.4, y=84.8},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={5904}, names={"A Plague Upon Thee"}, text="Nathaniel Dumah", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=43.4, y=84.8},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={6004}, names={"Unfinished Business"}, text="Kirsta Deepshadow: ride north past Dalson's Tears to her hiding spot just north-east of the Northridge Lumber Mill. On the way, note the Scarlet patrols around Dalson's Tears: Medics and Hunters", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=51.9, y=28.1, path={{41.0,81.3},{40.6,78.3},{34.8,75.9},{35.4,66.9},{38.4,62.4},{43.4,60.3},{43.2,53.1},{44.8,50.1},{47.0,36.7},{50.0,33.1},{50.4,29.8}}},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={6004}, names={"Unfinished Business"}, text="2 Scarlet Mages and 2 Knights (54-56) on the road south of Kirsta, 2 Medics and 2 Hunters (52-54) a little further south toward Dalson's Tears. A warlock has no interrupt: put Curse of Tongues on the Mages and on the Medics (healers), and kill the Medics first when they come in a group. Voidwalker on the Knight or Hunter, Fear the second enemy: the road is open, but keep it away from the next patrol", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=51.7, y=41.2},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={6004}, names={"Unfinished Business"}, text="Kirsta Deepshadow", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=51.9, y=28.1},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={6023}, names={"Unfinished Business"}, text="Kirsta Deepshadow", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=51.9, y=28.1},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={6023}, names={"Unfinished Business"}, text="Huntsman Radley (56) stands south-east of Kirsta at 57.8, 36.1; Cavalier Durgen (57) north-east of her at 55.2, 23.6, at the tower on the edge of Hearthglen. Do not go further into Hearthglen: it is elite. Pull each one away from his guards: Voidwalker on him, Fear a guard that comes along, DoTs and Drain Life", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=57.8, y=36.1},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={6023}, names={"Unfinished Business"}, text="Kirsta Deepshadow. Skip her follow-up: it is elite", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=51.9, y=28.1},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={5904}, names={"A Plague Upon Thee"}, text="The Northridge Lumber Mill, just south-west of Kirsta: set the barrel down in the middle of the mill", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=48.3, y=32.0},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={6389}, names={"A Plague Upon Thee"}, text="The Termite Barrel", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=48.3, y=32.0},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={6389}, names={"A Plague Upon Thee"}, text="Ride back south to Nathaniel Dumah, Chillwind Camp", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=43.4, y=84.8},
  {t="FLY", seg=25, arg="Ironforge", text="Bibilfaz Featherwhistle, Chillwind Camp", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=42.9, y=85.1},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=25, text="Briarthorn, the warlock trainer in the Forlorn Cavern in the north of the city: learn your level 58 spells, everything he offers", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=50.4, y=5.7},
  {t="FLY", seg=25, arg="Lakeshire", text="Gryth Thurden", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=55.5, y=47.7},
  {t="N", seg=25, arg="Optional dungeon: Shaper's Terrace, levels 58-60", text="New Forever dungeon, not checked in game yet. It is in the hills of Un'Goro Crater. Two Alliance quests are named for it (Panic at the Digsite, Mapping the Way Forward) but who gives them is not published yet: ask around Marshal's Refuge and take what is offered; the addon logs it so these steps can be filled in.", dg=18, run=true},
  {t="G", seg=25, text="Follow the road north out of Lakeshire and up the pass into the Burning Steppes. Morgan's Vigil, the Alliance camp, is to the right as you come out", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=84.3, y=68.3},
  {t="F", seg=25, arg="Morgan's Vigil", text="Borgus Stoutarm, the gryphon master", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=84.3, y=68.3},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={3823,4283}, names={"Extinguish the Firegut","FIFTY! YEP!"}, text="Oralius. Blackrock Medallions drop from every Blackrock orc and worg in the zone: keep them all", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=84.6, y=68.7},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={4262}, names={"Overmaster Pyron"}, text="Jalinda Sprig, a few steps away", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=85.4, y=70.1},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={3823}, names={"Extinguish the Firegut"}, text="Dreadmaul Rock, north of the camp: 15 Firegut Ogre Mages, 7 Ogres and 7 Brutes (50-53). The Mages are casters: put Curse of Tongues on them and kill them first, or Fear one while you kill another (the ogres stand well apart, but never Fear toward the dragonkin). Elite black dragonkin (Dragonspawn, Wyrmkin, 52-54) walk the ground east and north-east of the rock: stay on its west and south sides", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=79.8, y=44.1},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={3823}, names={"Extinguish the Firegut"}, text="Oralius, Morgan's Vigil", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=84.6, y=68.7},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={3824}, names={"Gor'tesh the Brute Lord"}, text="Oralius. Gor'tesh is far to the west; you get him with the orcs", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=84.6, y=68.7},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={4286}, names={"The Good Stuff"}, text="Oralius at Morgan's Vigil. 20 Dark Iron Fanny Packs from the dwarves inside. Needs level 50.", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=84.6, y=68.7, dg=13},
  {t="N", seg=25, arg="Optional dungeon: Blackrock Depths, levels 52-60", text="Blackrock Depths is inside Blackrock Mountain, between the Searing Gorge and the Burning Steppes: go in, take the chain down to the lowest ring and follow the tunnel to the portal. It is long; most groups do it in parts. Ragnar Thunderbrew in Kharanos also wants the Lost Thunderbrew Recipe (Hurley Blackbreath in the bar), after a pointer from Enohar Thunderbrew at Nethergarde Keep. Quests you picked up for it: The Good Stuff. Not on your path, only if you want the detour: Ribbly Screwspigot (Burning Steppes 66, 22); The Heart of the Mountain (Burning Steppes 65, 24); Incendius! (Burning Steppes 85, 70). Needs an earlier quest chain this route does not do: Marshal Windsor.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=34.8, y=85.3, dg=13, run=true},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={4286}, names={"The Good Stuff"}, zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=84.6, y=68.7, dg=13},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={4263}, names={"Incendius!"}, zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=85.4, y=70.1, dg=13},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={4296}, names={"Tablet of the Seven"}, text="Maxwort Uberglint, at Flame Crest, the goblin camp in the north. Ride north-west along the foot of Dreadmaul Rock; Flame Crest has only a Horde flight master", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=65.2, y=23.9},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={4123}, names={"The Heart of the Mountain"}, zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=65.2, y=23.9, dg=13},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={4136}, names={"Ribbly Screwspigot"}, zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=66.1, y=21.9, dg=13},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={4726}, names={"Broodling Essence"}, text="Tinkee Steamboil, beside him. She gives you the Draco-Incarcinatrix 900", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=65.2, y=24.0},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={4726}, names={"Broodling Essence"}, text="Scalding Broodlings (53-54) just south-west of Flame Crest: zap one with the Draco-Incarcinatrix, kill it and loot the essence it leaves on the ground. 8 in all. Stay west of about 80 and north of 55: elite dragonkin guard the other broodlings", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=59.3, y=31.7},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={3701}, names={"The Smoldering Ruins of Thaurissan"}, text="The Ruins of Thaurissan, south of Flame Crest: click the Thaurissan Relics lying among the ruins until the quest is complete (it counts 12 pieces of information). Thaurissan Spies stealth around them and jump you: keep the Voidwalker beside you to pull them off, keep your health up while you click and Drain Life them down", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=62.6, y=39.5},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={4296}, names={"Tablet of the Seven"}, text="The Tablet of the Seven, at the west end of the same ruins. Right-click it to copy it", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=54.1, y=40.8},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={4296}, names={"Tablet of the Seven"}, text="Maxwort Uberglint, Flame Crest", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=65.2, y=23.9},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={4726}, names={"Broodling Essence"}, text="Tinkee Steamboil. Do not take her letter: it goes to Winterspring", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=65.2, y=24.0},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={3824}, names={"Gor'tesh the Brute Lord"}, text="Ride south-west to the Blackrock orc camps in the middle of the zone. Gor'tesh (54) stands on the west side of them: take his head. Voidwalker on him, DoTs, and Fear whatever orc comes with him", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=39.3, y=55.3},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={4262}, names={"Overmaster Pyron"}, text="Overmaster Pyron, a level 52 elite fire elemental inside Blackrock Mountain, the volcano at the west end of the zone. Ride in through the Burning Steppes gate and go down to the Blackrock Quarry on the bottom level: he walks in front of the door to Blackrock Depths. Do not go through the door (that is the dungeon). Fire does nothing to him: no Immolate, use Corruption, Curse of Agony, Shadow Bolt and Drain Life. Put a Soulstone on yourself, start at full health and mana, send the Voidwalker first and keep it up with Health Funnel; Healthstone when you are low. He is an elemental: if it goes wrong, Banish him and walk away. Can't find or reach him? Abandon the quest"},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={4283}, names={"FIFTY! YEP!"}, text="Back out to the orc camps. 50 Blackrock Medallions: Blackrock Soldiers, Slayers, Sorcerers, Warlocks and Worgs (54-57) in the camps around here; about every second kill drops one. Kill the Sorcerers and Warlocks first, with Curse of Tongues on them (a warlock has no interrupt); Voidwalker on the melee orc. Step back out of the camp when a worg adds and Fear it only once you are clear of the tents", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=48.0, y=55.0},
  {t="L", seg=25, lvl=60, text="The last grind. Stay on the Blackrock orcs: singles at the edges of the camps, Voidwalker first, DoTs and Drain Life, Life Tap after each kill, and eat, drink or bandage between pulls. The hand-ins still open (Oralius three times, Jalinda, Archesonus in Ironforge) give about 26,800 XP, roughly an eighth of level 59: you can stop that far short of 60 and let them finish it", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=48.0, y=55.0},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={3824}, names={"Gor'tesh the Brute Lord"}, text="Ride back east to Oralius, Morgan's Vigil", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=84.6, y=68.7},
  {t="A", seg=25, q={3825}, names={"Ogre Head On A Stick = Party"}, text="Oralius", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=84.6, y=68.7},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={4283}, names={"FIFTY! YEP!"}, text="Oralius", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=84.6, y=68.7},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={4262}, names={"Overmaster Pyron"}, text="Jalinda Sprig. Skip her follow-up: it is in Blackrock Depths", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=85.4, y=70.1},
  {t="C", seg=25, q={3825}, names={"Ogre Head On A Stick = Party"}, text="Climb to the top of Dreadmaul Rock and plant Gor'tesh's head in the soft dirt mound", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=81.0, y=46.8},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={3825}, names={"Ogre Head On A Stick = Party"}, text="Oralius", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=84.6, y=68.7},
  {t="FLY", seg=25, arg="Ironforge", text="Borgus Stoutarm", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=84.3, y=68.3},
  {t="T", seg=25, q={3701}, names={"The Smoldering Ruins of Thaurissan"}, text="Royal Historian Archesonus", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=38.4, y=55.3},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=25, text="Briarthorn, the warlock trainer in the Forlorn Cavern in the north of the city: learn your level 60 spells, everything he offers. Route complete", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=50.4, y=5.7},
},
